{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/223770-homebrews-of-the-first-circle","id":223770,"title":"Homebrews of the First Circle?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-08-09T19:21:55-07:00","id":223770,"title":"Homebrews of the First Circle?","content":"Something I was curious about. I've been looking, but I'm having trouble finding any Homebrew First Circles. I found two(both in a blog named Octipodial Preservation), but that's pretty much it for anything with stats. So, does anyone know where I can find some? Those which were on the Lost Wiki would be prized, especially if they're of Yozi without any canonically(like Qaf, Hegra, Theion). Here is a collection of sone that were apparently on the wiki: <a href=\"http://forum.rpg.net/showthread.php?584857-EXALTED-Index-of-Fanmade-First-Circle-Demon\" target=\"_blank\">http://forum.rpg.net/showthread.php?...t-Circle-Demon</a>. Sorry for wasting your time!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-10T11:04:33-07:00","id":224305,"title":"","content":"I wrote up a number of First Circle species on the old forums, about half of which were statted (for 2E, obviously). I've linked to their Google Docs below. They're...adequate, hopefully.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/11wtWHtZx7pvMyBG_HfGkmfAfOO9Cb5JsyaT-Z-OHA7E/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Jaghanatha, the Crushing Chariots</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1TJv9XL5WMUFKFcYa5uv9fStDDMl9Nfs9pZYETDqf-l0/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Levivula, the Iridescent Rainclouds</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1gcqKS6lRe2esaZl6hKmbxFBzw-ksrcUU7Qq7X7Bobj0/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Sarsketch, the Blaze Malkins</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1rU--4nfWwFXybzv-C3RfxeCq4u6ly0Ooy7lqoadUob0/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Signifers, the Promise Snakes</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1jTUvU8_6XE8z-jbuYKFjjUUc9d_U0KgXyk7k972Zz1M/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Aruna, the Hounding Blades</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1mDX8nC2IY-dtSCGuUBU-l7osBEmCaZxx8MxgnQXJsII/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Chagurar, the Smoldering Giants</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1_h4VU8KYXbfB8r323DNiR8hFY1OVJ7lK2sNZ8H2uxbY/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Daramba, the Horned Trumpeteers</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1_QFNIhwPiUw15ghFEG48Z1WvcRt3HNCvIAx1OaxnefE/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Gnumgurgl, the White-Salve Gulperfish</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1u-_dIoFUM0nPkp9nA5jvQhFY8X2Qedu1_w5M57Uxr7Y/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Jabira, the Course Keepers</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1W_neyk7HtlKkUmrsJKC_954p-3NWbsaNQ1WNA1Rlqj4/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Vendaghan, the Cataclysm-Riders</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=238\" data-tempid=\"temp_238_1438728365271_197\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1821-golden-demon","name":"Golden Demon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1821_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"93"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-10T12:58:20-07:00","id":224387,"title":"","content":"Overall, i don't worry much about demon species as such because things like Neomah flesh-crafting and Anulehs-brewing opens the door for the existence of endless hordes of unique patchwork/hybrid demons spread all through the demon realm, some who might even have (some) sexual reproduction potential, depending on how much material from mortal things of Creation was blended or not in their making.<br /> <br /> There's much you can do with such &quot;amalgamated demons&quot; going from hardscrabble random masses of &quot;lowest of low&quot; rungs in demonic hierarchy to specialized &quot;built to p\u00e1rticular needs&quot; custom lovers, servants or pets, not to mention unique, unpredictable and distrusted one-of-a-kind citizens originated from peculiar mixes of demon, god, elemental, mortal, fae, exalt or even stranger things.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 01-21-2024, 08:41 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-10T14:13:26-07:00","id":224466,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Golden Demon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/223770-homebrews-of-the-first-circle?p=224305#post224305\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wrote up a number of First Circle species on the old forums, about half of which were statted (for 2E, obviously). I've linked to their Google Docs below. They're...adequate, hopefully.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://&amp;quot;&#91;url\" target=\"_blank\">https://docs.google.com/document/d/11wtWHtZx7pvMyBG_HfGkmfAfOO9Cb5JsyaT-Z-OHA7E/edit?usp=sharing&amp;quot;]Jaghanatha</a>, the Crushing Chariots[/URL]<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://&amp;quot;&#91;url\" target=\"_blank\">https://docs.google.com/document/d/1TJv9XL5WMUFKFcYa5uv9fStDDMl9Nfs9pZYETDqf-l0/edit?usp=sharing&amp;quot;]Levivula</a>, the Iridescent Rainclouds[/URL]<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://&amp;quot;&#91;url\" target=\"_blank\">https://docs.google.com/document/d/1gcqKS6lRe2esaZl6hKmbxFBzw-ksrcUU7Qq7X7Bobj0/edit?usp=sharing&amp;quot;]Sarsketch</a>, the Blaze Malkins[/URL]<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://&amp;quot;&#91;url\" target=\"_blank\">https://docs.google.com/document/d/1rU--4nfWwFXybzv-C3RfxeCq4u6ly0Ooy7lqoadUob0/edit?usp=sharing&amp;quot;]Signifers</a>, the Promise Snakes[/URL]<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://&amp;quot;&#91;url\" target=\"_blank\">https://docs.google.com/document/d/1jTUvU8_6XE8z-jbuYKFjjUUc9d_U0KgXyk7k972Zz1M/edit?usp=sharing&amp;quot;]Aruna</a>, the Hounding Blades[/URL]<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://&amp;quot;&#91;url\" target=\"_blank\">https://docs.google.com/document/d/1mDX8nC2IY-dtSCGuUBU-l7osBEmCaZxx8MxgnQXJsII/edit?usp=sharing&amp;quot;]Chagurar</a>, the Smoldering Giants[/URL]<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://&amp;quot;&#91;url\" target=\"_blank\">https://docs.google.com/document/d/1_h4VU8KYXbfB8r323DNiR8hFY1OVJ7lK2sNZ8H2uxbY/edit?usp=sharing&amp;quot;]Daramba</a>, the Horned Trumpeteers[/URL]<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://&amp;quot;&#91;url\" target=\"_blank\">https://docs.google.com/document/d/1_QFNIhwPiUw15ghFEG48Z1WvcRt3HNCvIAx1OaxnefE/edit?usp=sharing&amp;quot;]Gnumgurgl</a>, the White-Salve Gulperfish[/URL]<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://&amp;quot;&#91;url\" target=\"_blank\">https://docs.google.com/document/d/1u-_dIoFUM0nPkp9nA5jvQhFY8X2Qedu1_w5M57Uxr7Y/edit?usp=sharing&amp;quot;]Jabira</a>, the Course Keepers[/URL]<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://&amp;quot;&#91;url\" target=\"_blank\">https://docs.google.com/document/d/1W_neyk7HtlKkUmrsJKC_954p-3NWbsaNQ1WNA1Rlqj4/edit?usp=sharing&amp;quot;]Vendaghan</a>, the Cataclysm-Riders[/URL]</div> </div> </div> </div>These are all awesome! My favorites are the Jaghanatha and the Gnumgurgl. Though I'm curious, what Yozi do the Levivula and the Vendaghan belong to?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-10T14:31:22-07:00","id":224480,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ZealousChristian24</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/223770-homebrews-of-the-first-circle?p=224466#post224466\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> These are all awesome! My favorites are the Jaghanatha and the Gnumgurgl. Though I'm curious, what Yozi do the Levivula and the Vendaghan belong to?</div> </div> </div> </div>The levivula descend from Cytherea iirc (I didn't come up with them, I just statted them), and the vendaghan descend from Isidoros. Inunda, the Pillar of Cataclysm, progenitor of the vendaghan, was a homebrew Second Circle who iirc was the Wisdom Soul of Ferand, created by Robert Vance back before he was a freelancer. It was on the old forum so idk if the write-up is still around.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=238\" data-tempid=\"temp_238_1438728365271_197\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1821-golden-demon","name":"Golden Demon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1821_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"93"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-10T14:33:29-07:00","id":224484,"title":"","content":"Okay, thanks for responding. Both would make great familiars or EarthScorpion style Coaducators.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-10T18:03:35-07:00","id":224702,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"http://www.rpnation.com/threads/szmiya-the-sword-born-thralls-gargulee.52057/\" target=\"_blank\">Szmiya, the Sword-born Thralls</a>. For the curious, they are descended from Malfeas via Ligier.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1419-wardragon","name":"WarDragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1419_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1052"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-10T20:59:15-07:00","id":224809,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WarDragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/223770-homebrews-of-the-first-circle?p=224702#post224702\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"http://www.rpnation.com/threads/szmiya-the-sword-born-thralls-gargulee.52057/\" target=\"_blank\">Szmiya, the Sword-born Thralls</a>. For the curious, they are descended from Malfeas via Ligier.</div> </div> </div> </div>Cool! Though, I would've assumed they're descended from The Ebon Dragon 'cause they seem like the sort of thing he'd make for fun.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-11T08:19:10-07:00","id":225098,"title":"","content":"Eldagusto had a whole mess of homebrew demons at one point, I'm on my cell right now so I can't really hunt them down right now","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/359-dezeroth","name":"Dezeroth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar359_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"496"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-11T16:02:36-07:00","id":225368,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ZealousChristian24</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/223770-homebrews-of-the-first-circle?p=224809#post224809\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Cool! Though, I would've assumed they're descended from The Ebon Dragon 'cause they seem like the sort of thing he'd make for fun.</div> </div> </div> </div>If I remember right, their maker had a whole &quot;thing&quot; about slavery.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1419-wardragon","name":"WarDragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1419_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1052"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-22T20:23:49-08:00","id":1269962,"title":"","content":"Ah, fuck it. I can't find my own thread. Anyway, some stuff from Eldagusto.<br /> <b>Quiqui, the Mist Haired Singers.</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252525\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>Quiqui, the Mist Haired Singers.</b> <b>Demons of the First Circle, Orphans of the Neomah</b><br /> <br /> Rare is it that one of creations of the Neomah to thrive and breed true, and in the case of the Mist Haired Singers they can trace back the mythical spreading of their species to the century before the great contagion, though legend has it that the first of their kind was created long before that, perhaps during the final days of the Usurpation.<br /> <br /> <br /> In Creation the Mist Haired Singers take to standing upon cliff sides and spacious groves. They appear comely maidens wrapped in diaphanous mauve saris with translucent hair that unfolds into the very mist that surrounds them. They lack fingernails and their hands are warm and comforting to the touch. The mist that surrounds their faces would obscure their two columns of two almond eyes if not for the fact that their dark sockets glow red when their song is in the air. One pair of their arms tends to stay wrapped giving themselves or another a soft embrace, with their other pair gesticulating as they sing their lilting melody. The Mist Haired Singers have flesh that gleam with moonlight, pointed ears, and weigh as much as a bag of feathers. Those without awakened essence view the Mist Haired Singers as milky silhouettes that are barely in motion; however animals and those with essence can see them as they really are. Most are often shocked to discover images taken of the Mist Haired Singers, whether paintings modeled after one, or first age pictocaptures, will show their form in constant motion mouthing a silent song.<br /> <br /> <br /> Perhaps the key to their survival is tied to their origins, but such secrets are lost to the ages. It is said the first of their kind, only known as the Mist Haired Singer, eventually chose to Martyr herself by mastering sorcery and awaiting her starbound fate through the End of All Wisdom. The end of her life was never witnessed, however it has been recorded that she plumbed the depths of the Underworld for its secrets. She has learned secret melodies from her travels and passed them to her offspring when she finally discovered the secret to her replication. The Mist Haired Singer spent centuries pursuing the love her heart must have inherited from somewhere. When she cast aside here heart in learning Sorcery, or some whisper Necromancy, her cast aside heart shaped into the form of her five daughters. To her daughters she taught her secret songs. The Shade Danser Melody can awaken the turbulent Po in any corpse that died without knowing true love, or that had true love taken from it. The Lambent Mists Call can quell any storm and convert it to miles wide mists. Finally the Trembling Heart Serenade allows for the sacrifice of a Mist Haired Singer\u2019s Compassion dots to form offspring from them, and in so doing form a five dot intimacy towards each of her daughters in a different chosen subject. With this she ensured each of her daughters was the chosen consort of a different Citizen and spread her kin throughout the Demon City.<br /> <br /> <br /> Summoning:<br /> <br /> <br /> (Obscurity 3/5)<br /> <br /> Sorcerers often summon the Mist Haired Singers for a combination of their mysterious beauty, and pleasing emotion mastering voice. They normally find employ as professional courtesans both in Creation and Hell, and due to the nature of their birth many are valued concubines for royalty both mortal and Demonic. When a white haired maiden truly casts aside her love while singing a heart rending tune then mists will shroud her and a Mist Haired Singer will reveal herself in the moonlight drawn by her familiar pain.<br /> <br /> <br /> Motivation: To find true love. Intimacies: Love (Longing), other Mist Haired Singers (Sadness) (only for those who have never sung the Trembling Heart Serenade).<br /> <br /> <br /> To aid my children. Intimacies: Love (Disdain) (For those who sang the Trembling Heart Serenade), other Mist Haired Singers (Concern).<br /> <br /> Virtues:<br /> <br /> <br /> Compassion 5, Conviction 3 , Temperance 1 , Valor 2 (Before Trembling Heart Serenade)<br /> <br /> Compassion 1, Conviction 3 , Temperance 5 , Valor 2 (After Trembling Heart Serenade)<br /> <br /> Willpower 8<br /> <br /> Attributes: Strength 3, Dexterity 4 , Stamina 3 ; Charisma 5 , Manipulation 6 , Appearance 5 ; Perception 3, Intelligence 2, Wits 2<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Abilities:<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Martial Arts 1 (Embrace 2)<br /> <br /> Melee 1<br /> <br /> Archery<br /> <br /> Thrown 1<br /> <br /> War<br /> <br /> Integrity 3 (For Love 3)/(Against Love for the Heartless 3)<br /> <br /> Presence 4 (Sex Appeal 2)<br /> <br /> Performance 6 (Songs of Love 3) Resistance 2 Survival 1 (Weather 2, At Night 1)<br /> <br /> Medicine 1 (Heart Troubles 3) Investigation 1 (Longing 2, Love 1) Craft Water1 (Brewing 1), Air 1 (Invoking the Heart 2)<br /> <br /> Occult 3 (Secret Songs 2, Underworld 1)<br /> <br /> Lore 1 (Times of Glory 1, Lintha 1) Athletics 3 (Flexibility 3) Awareness 2 (Sight 2) Stealth 3 (Night 2, While Singing 1) Dodge 3 (While Singing 2) Larceny 2 (While Embracing 2, While Singing 1) Socialize 5 (Matters of the Heart 3) Ride 1 (At Night 1) Sail 2 (While Singing 2, Moonlight 1) Bureaucracy 1 (Contracts 2, Marriage 1) Linguistics 2+ (Native Old Realm, River Speak, High Realm, and maybe more)<br /> <br /> Backgrounds:<br /> <br /> <br /> Backing 2 (Most have a backing of at least two due to being born high prestige Courtesans or Concubines), Resources 4 (Most have a collection of gifts from paramours), Contacts 3 (Admirers, Other Quiqui, other Courtesans)<br /> <br /> <br /> Charms:<br /> <br /> <br /> 2nd Excellencies: Integrity, Presence, Performance, Socialize<br /> <br /> <br /> Essence Plethora x1<br /> <br /> <br /> Measure the Wind: to find greater patrons<br /> <br /> <br /> Materialize<br /> <br /> <br /> Benefaction: Targets receive a die bonus when working towards the Love or Admiration of the Mist Haired Singer.<br /> <br /> <br /> Eye of Inspiration: To lend the Performance and Presence excellency to those working for Love.<br /> <br /> <br /> Amethyst Awareness: Works as long as all 4 of their Eyes are open.<br /> <br /> <br /> Memory Mirror: While singing their tune crawls into the minds of its listeners.<br /> <br /> <br /> Sense Domain: They may sense love and Longing.<br /> <br /> <br /> Tracking: Instead of allowing themselves the use of this Charm they may allow anyone with an intimacy or motivation of love or admiration towards them to track them.<br /> <br /> <br /> Call: May call to the Lonely, or those attracted to them.<br /> <br /> <br /> Impromptu Messenger: Their song may be emitted through Mists and Moonlight, as well as through images of them.<br /> <br /> <br /> Worldly Illusions: Those listening to their melodies may meet with them in a field of Mists and Moonlight.<br /> <br /> <br /> Dreamscape: They may visit the Dreams of those who desire them.<br /> <br /> <br /> Weather Control: They may nullify any storm or winds and convert it to mists through their Lambent Mists Call.<br /> <br /> <br /> Mirror of Infinite Wardrobe: They may barrow the form of loved ones from a targets memory.<br /> <br /> <br /> Landscape Travel: They may travel upon mists and moonlight.<br /> <br /> <br /> Geas: May lay a Geas dealing with love, winning love, or marriage.<br /> <br /> <br /> Harrow the Mind: May cause targets to believe \u201cPursuing Love\u201d or \u201cAbandoning Love\u201d is the actions they must take.<br /> <br /> <br /> Mind Knife Sacrament: They have mastery over intimacies of Love and Desire.<br /> <br /> <br /> Stoke the Flame: Instills Desire<br /> <br /> <br /> Subtle Whisper: Through their Haunting Songs<br /> <br /> <br /> Landscape Hide: Within Mists and Moonlight<br /> <br /> <br /> Fruit of Living Essence: They may drain their Paramours with their Embrace.<br /> <br /> <br /> Spice of Custodial Delectation: When Singing.<br /> <br /> <br /> Wine of Infinite Heartbreak: Hearts are their bread and butter.<br /> <br /> <br /> Bane Weapon: Those who are Married.<br /> <br /> <br /> Words of Power: Her Songs of Power.<br /> <br /> Secret Songs:<br /> <br /> Shade Danser Melody: By Spending 1 Willpower and 10 Motes per Po their song is heard by any corpse that died before knowing true love, or that lost true love. After 10 minutes their hungry ghosts are summoned to protect the Mist Haired Singer or hunt and kill for her.<br /> <br /> Lambent Mists Call: Channels her Weather Control, Landscape Hide, and Landscape Travel. The mists they summon contain properties of the moon and so they reflect and refract light. Animas activated within may blind the Exalted imitating them if they fail a resistance + stamina roll with a difficulty of their own Essence level. If they fail they are completely blind within the Mists. The mists confer normal visibility penalties for mists, but the Mist Haired Singers may see easily through it.<br /> <br /> Trembling Hearts Serenade: If a Mist Haired Singer chooses to Sing this secret song then she lowers her Compassion to one condensing it in her heart which moves out of her body through her song and forms into five new Mist Haired Singers whom the mother may choose to tie an intimacy of love as a shaping effect to any 5 listeners tying them to one daughter each. This is a shaping effect on the targets mind and soul. Afterwards the Mother may always add her temperance to her MDV when being emotionally swayed.<br /> <br /> Essence: 4<br /> <br /> Soak 1L/6B Diaphanous Robes of Longing 0L/3B<br /> <br /> HEALTH: One -0, Six -1, Five -2, One -4, Incapacitated<br /> <br /> <br /> Mutations: Extra Limbs.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://web.archive.org/web/20160315091459/http://rathess.xi.co.nz:80/exalted/index.php/Characters:Quiqui_the_Mist_Haired_Singers\" target=\"_blank\">https://web.archive.org/web/20160315...Haired_Singers</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12952,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","user":"Accelerator","date":". 12-19-2018, 07:06 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-22T20:25:09-08:00","id":1269964,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sanctaphrax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/890286-homebrew-new-first-circle-demon#post890286\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Player needed a demon that could get the wounded and wyld-mutated back on their feet. So we came up with this.</div> </div> </div> </div></span></span></span><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sanctaphrax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/890286-homebrew-new-first-circle-demon#post890286\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Please excuse the odd font size. I copied this from another forum.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"><span style=\"color:#191919\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\"><b>VLIRVAKH</b></span></span></span></span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"><span style=\"color:#191919\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">A Vlirvakh looks like a giant glass spider with a fleshy human hand at the end of each leg. Their touch dissolves flesh and bone into threads, which they can weave like silk. Sorcerers call them up to alter the bodies of men and beasts, or to create clothes and other cloth goods.</span></span></span></span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"><span style=\"color:#191919\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Vlirvakh hate simplicity and dull patterns, so unless carefully micromanaged they will cover the bodies of those they are asked to modify and the goods they are asked to make with multicoloured fractals and strange structures of unclear purpose. They take pride in their intelligence and the complexity of their work, and expect to be treated respectfully even when bound.</span></span></span></span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"><span style=\"color:#191919\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Vlirvakh would be among the foremost mathematicians of the Demon City if they were capable of explaining themselves, but they are not. Their normal fondness for obscure words reaches an absurd extreme when they talk about mathematical topics, making their mathematical insights very difficult to follow.</span></span></span></span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"><span style=\"color:#191919\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Vlirvakh almost universally love Neomah, but this fondness is rarely reciprocated.</span></span></span></span></span></span><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"><span style=\"color:#191919\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\"><b>Common Intimacies:</b></span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Defining Principle: Simple things are boring and morally questionable.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Major Principle: I am intelligent and skilled and deserve to be respected for that.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Minor Tie: A particular Neomah (affection, lust or similar)</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Minor Tie: A particular piece of work (pride)</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"><b>Essence:</b> 2</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"><b>Willpower:</b> 5</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"><b>Motes:</b> 70</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"><b>Health Levels:</b> -0/-0/-0/-4/-4/-4/Incap</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"><b>Actions:</b> Senses 5, Resist poison/disease 6, Social influence 5, Knowledge 9, Read intentions 5, Weaving 12, Mathematics 12, Stealth 7</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"><b>Appearance:</b> 2 <b>Resolve:</b> 3 <b>Guile:</b> 3</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"><b>Join Battle:</b> 5</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"><b>Attack:</b> Bite 7 (11)</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"><b>Combat Movement:</b> 6</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"><b>Evasion/Parry:</b> 3/2</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"><b>Soak/Hardness:</b> 9/0</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"><b>Merits:</b></span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Master Weaver: A Vlirvakh is always treated as though it had access to tools of exceptional quality for weaving. It works four times as fast as a human.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Mathematical Mind: A Vlirvakh never forgets a number and may always act as though it had access to an abacus of exceptional quality in its mind. However, their explanations are generally incomprehensible; anyone tutored by a Vlirvakh in mathematics doubles their training times instead of reducing them, and following a Vlirvakh's explanation of the answer to a question generally requires an (Intelligence + Lore) roll against a difficulty 1 less than that of solving the problem yourself.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"><b>Charms:</b></span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Unraveling Touch (15m; Supplemental; Instant; Essence 2): This Charm supplements a decisive attack, doubling 9s on the damage roll and adding 1 to the wound penalty of anyone injured by it. Wounds inflicted with this Charm require a (Dexterity + Craft (Weaving)) roll against a difficulty of the resulting wound penalty or a (Dexterity + Medicine) roll against that difficulty plus one to re-knit the flesh before it can begin to heal. This Charm may also be used outside of combat, to justify weaving flesh that normally could not be woven.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Artisan of Meat (4m per dot granted, 1wp; Simple; Indefinite; Essence 2): The Vlirvakh spends a few hours modifying a body, and improves it in some way. The subject benefits from a physical Merit that could be created by adding woven structures to the body. A new hand or foot counts as a 2-dot Merit, a new limb counts as a 3-dot Merit. Taking a wound penalty or withdrawing the committed motes ends this Charm, and leaves a gruesome deformity in the form of a shattered structure of woven flesh behind. The Vlirvakh can fix such deformities, of course. </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#191919\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">If the Vlirvakh spends a month at work, they can make a granted Merit permanent. This inevitably involves trade-offs that leave the subject with the same amount of xp as before. Note that this Charm is not Stackable, so any given person may only benefit from one use of it at a time. Vlirvakh can incorporate foreign materials into the body to a limited extent, which may change the aesthetics but not the effects of their work.</span></span></span></span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"><span style=\"color:#191919\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Moment Of Calculation (10m; Reflexive; Instant; Essence 2): Once per turn, the Vlirvakh instantly performs mathematical work that would normally take it an hour to perform.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Hurry Home </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#191919\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">(10m, 1wp; Simple; Instant; Essence 1): The Vlirvakh teleports to its summoner at the beginning of its next turn.</span></span></span></span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"><span style=\"color:#191919\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Materialize (35m, 1wp; Simple; Instant; Essence 1): The Vlirvakh weaves itself out of thin glass strands.</span></span></span></span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"><span style=\"color:#191919\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Measure The Wind (5m, 1wp; Simple; Instant; Essence 1): The Vlirvakh gets the measure of anyone whose flesh it unravels.</span></span></span></span></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"><br /> <br /> So anyway, yes. i quote this from someone else. </span></span></span><br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/890286-homebrew-new-first-circle-demon\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/filedata/fetch?filedataid=1074\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/890286-homebrew-new-first-circle-demon\"> [Homebrew] New First Circle Demon - Onyx Path Forums </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/890286-homebrew-new-first-circle-demon\"> http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/890286-homebrew-new-first-circle-demon </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> Player needed a demon that could get the wounded and wyld-mutated back on their feet. So we came up with this. Please excuse the odd font size. I copied this from </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-22T20:26:18-08:00","id":1269965,"title":"","content":"More by Eldagusto<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://web.archive.org/web/20160314203456/http://rathess.xi.co.nz/exalted/index.php/Characters:Spindex_the_Mockeries\" target=\"_blank\">https://web.archive.org/web/20160314..._the_Mockeries</a><br /> <b>Spindex, the Mockeries.</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252525\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>Spindex, the Mockeries.</b></span></span></span><br /> <b>Demons of the First Circle, Progeny of the Infinitely Coiled</b> The Infinitely Coiled twists endlessly against the very oaths that bind the Yozis. There are no confirmations to which Yozis the Infinitely Coiled belongs, but many are the results of the plans to escape. The Spindex are progeny destined to die for freedom. In Malfeas they are naught but coiled bundles of potential. Awaiting destiny outside of the demon city they lay in their dream birth until a sorcerer summons one into Creation. They are summoned upon corpse of one of the dead and the Spindex has no Materialize charm, only a unique form of the Ride Charm were they perform the Ritual Weave the Goblin Chrysalis and over 8 hours out of the sickly green cocoon a Mockery takes its first breath.<br /> <br /> Mockeries will be reborn using the same abilities as the mortal corpse, but with only 15 points worth of the corpse\u2019s abilities. 16 points worth of Mutations maybe purchased, including negative mutations to gain additional points, 4 and three charms may be chosen from spirit excellencies, Ox-Bodies, Essence Plethoras, or Reserve of Wills. The Mockery may purchase new spirit charms as normal but must have a teacher. They also have a version of Endowment that allows them to raise abilities that they possess a 4 or more in (or any Language they know) over the course of a week as a training effect up to their rating. This may be spent on abilities, Specialties, and Thaumaturgy.<br /> <br /> Mockeries are effectively new Demons born from the union of a Spindex and a corpse; they are born from flesh and are naturally Material due to this. They inherit their parents summoning bindings. Sorcerers often summon a Mockery into being as teachers or advisers so they may take advantage of a slain enemy of great skill, or a fallen mentor who refused to release their greatest secrets. Mockeries have also been created as their name suggests desecrating a fallen foe, and having their likeness serve past death as a novel amusement. They make excellent doppelgangers to infiltrate everything from courts of rival kingdoms and even fixing weddings between two factions. What many do not realize however is that part of the nature of the Mockeries is the fact that they stay upon Creation after their bound service is up. This may be fixed with a simple banishing spell, or a swift swipe of the Goremaul, however. One of the leading causes of Mockeries rampant in Creation is simply Sorcerers bargaining with the Demon Prince the Infinitely Coiled, exchanging sorcerous training for the pledge to summon a variable amount of Mockeries into Creation. After all it is their nature to twist from their bounds.<br /> <br /> <b>Summoning</b>:<br /> (Obscurity 3/4)<br /> Spindex may twist their way into Creation when a skilled mortal, 5 or more in a skill, perishes with their last breath exhaling lament over their knowledge being lost to the world the Spindex taste these in their dreambirths and follow it into their dead lungs to have a Mockery born anew.<br /> Mockeries loose upon Creation may cough up a milky fishlike egg once every calibration. They will hide this and when they finally die or are banished to Malfeas the eggs will hatch and seek a corpse to perform the Rite of the Goblin Chrysalis upon.<br /> <b>Motivation</b>: To Birth Themselves into Being<br /> <b>Virtues</b>: Compassion 5, Conviction 5, Temperance 1, Valor 1<br /> <b>Attributes</b>: Strength 1, Dexterity 1, Stamina 1; Charisma 1, Manipulation 1, Appearance 1; Perception 1, Intelligence 1, Wits 1<br /> <b>Abilities</b>:<br /> <br /> Martial Arts<br /> Melee<br /> Archery<br /> Thrown<br /> War<br /> Integrity<br /> Presence<br /> Performance<br /> Resistance<br /> Survival 4 (Find Host + 3)<br /> Medicine<br /> Investigation<br /> Craft<br /> Occult 3 (Dreams 2<br /> Lore<br /> Athletics<br /> Awareness<br /> Stealth<br /> Dodge 5<br /> Larceny<br /> Socialize<br /> Ride<br /> Sail<br /> Bureaucracy<br /> Linguistics (Native Old Realm)<br /> <b>Backgrounds</b>: <b>Charms</b>:<br /> <br /> <br /> Ride A unique version that may only be used on human dead, and results in a new being that uses only the traits of the corpse.<br /> Track- Find Corpses<br /> <b>Essence</b>: 2<br /> <br /> <br /> NOTES:<br /> Spindex is often used to refer to the Dreamspirit that merges with a corpse, and the resulting being is referred to as a Mockery. However some have taken to referring to both using the title Mockery.<br /> <br /> Motivation: To Live A Life of Freedom. With intimacies of Fear towards Malfeas due to memories and instinct informing them to live in Hell will most assuredly result in their doom.<br /> Traits: Use the traits of the corpse but only retain 15 points worth of Abilities, and add 16 points worth of Mutations, and three charms from either Spirit Excellencies, Ox-Body, Essence Plethora, or Reserve of Will. Automatically learns the unique Endowment charm. Normal 0 false false false EN-US ZH-CN X-NONE Each Degree in Thaumaturgy kept counts as Three Skill points. Starting essence is 2<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-22T20:27:54-08:00","id":1269967,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://web.archive.org/web/20160315085956/http://rathess.xi.co.nz:80/exalted/index.php/Characters:Melicula_the_Horned_Greeters\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://web.archive.org/web/20160315085956im_/http:/rathess.xi.co.nz/exalted/resources/assets/poweredby_mediawiki_88x31.png\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://web.archive.org/web/20160315085956/http://rathess.xi.co.nz:80/exalted/index.php/Characters:Melicula_the_Horned_Greeters\" target=\"_blank\"> Characters:Melicula the Horned Greeters - exalted official wiki - mirror from archive.org </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://web.archive.org/web/20160315085956/http://rathess.xi.co.nz:80/exalted/index.php/Characters:Melicula_the_Horned_Greeters\" target=\"_blank\"> https://web.archive.org/web/20160315085956/http://rathess.xi.co.nz:80/exalted/index.php/Characters:Melicula_the_Horned_Greeters </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div> <br /> <b>Melicula, the Horned Greeters.</b><br /><br /> <span style=\"color:#252525\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Melicula, the Horned Greeters.</span></span></span><br /> <b>Demons of the First Circle, Progeny of the Weaver of Voices</b> Like her creator, the Green Sun, the Weaver of Voices indulges in the pursuits of vanity. The Horned Greeters are formed from the need to recognize Ligier\u2019s Glory coalescing into being from the avalanche of Berengiere\u2019s parted veil whenever Berengiere bares witness to Ligier in person, or when greeting the Green Sun after a long period of absence from seeing the skies of the Demon City. The Horned Greeters ply their trade across the many layers of the Demon City. As there is always a great demand for beautiful sycophants the Horned Greeters have spread far and wide across Hell for Millenia becoming a very common and popular species of demon.<br /> <br /> Melicula appear as lithe yet athletic nude females. They are hairless and have smooth skin in light tones varying from purples, greens, blues, and greys. Normally they sport two upturned horns upon their brows, though some may only sport one large horn and a rare few are hornless. Commonly they take to tattooing simple stripes and circles about their unadorned bodies. The simplicity of such ink provides all the modesty they desire. They take their names not just from the horns upon their head but also from the fact that each one carries a greeting horn of the same type that rises from their head only several sizes larger, which they instinctually are driven to play.<br /> <br /> Their duty is to deploy a sonorous greeting to the worthy and they are valued for this throughout the Demon City as not only does it ensure more sound to drive away the Silent Winds but it is deeply flattering to the glory hungry hordes. They are a natural race of groupies, and often they find employment as part of the retinue of the citizens of the Demon City. They are found in everywhere from the classiest brothels, to the grimiest allies of the Demon City. Sorcerers everywhere Summon them to caress their Egos, head their parades and triumphs, or simply as earnestly sycophantic toadies that are easy on the eyes.<br /> <br /> Their talents allows for impromptu poems from a thousand traditions both human and demon, upon the greatness of those they greet, all to be heard from their mouths and horns throughout the crowds of the Demon City. Even to the point of cutting through the skull-rattling cacophony that is commonplace even outside of celebrations and triumphs. Sorcerers often keep on in their retinue as their chosen confidants as they are naturals in winning over others with their earnest awe and devotion. The problem is they are perhaps too easy to win over and take to filling their role as a groupie extraordinaire as quickly as possible when not given an immediate task. They make excellent translators as each individual learns a large array of languages and poetry traditions. While Demons rarely care, many humans are put off by the hermaphroditic/androgynous nature of the Neomah, driving them to elegant and lovely arms of the Melicula whom are prized for their simplicity, sturdiness, and over all cheapness. They are well prepared for all but the harshest of abuses of the mortal world, as they cannot compare to what their masters amongst the Demon City can casually express. They enjoy gossiping amongst themselves and many thaumaturgists summon them for updates on Hell\u2019s rumor mill, or a night of celebration if they have something to brag about. Though one thing some forget is that they are apathetic at best towards the unimpressive, and when there are none around to brag about or greet they may show disdain and spite towards the weak, common, and inglorious. In the First Age many Exalted used the Horned Greeters to bolster the morale of their cults.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Summoning</b>:<br /> (Obscurity 1/1)<br /> When a hero has achieved a glorious triumph that has resulted in widespread change their return home may be greeted by over a hundred and one cheering maidens and a Horned Greeter may find herself amongst them, as her cheers cut through even the loudest mortals regards. When a Horned Greeter is driven to a state of hysteria by witnessing a truly magnificent spectacle they may unconsciously sunder one of their horns from their skulls and play a booming melody that causes the horn to grow till the point where a newborn Horned Greeter ripples into existence taking up their birth horn.<br /> <br /> <b>Motivation</b>:<br /> To Grandly Greet the Great. Many develop intimacies to powerful and or successful figures, and all are born with an intimacy of Awe towards Ligier. Conversely they have intimacies of Disdain for the unimpressive<br /> <b>Virtues</b>:<br /> Compassion 3, Conviction 2 , Temperance 1 , Valor 2 Willpower 5<br /> <b>Attributes</b>: Strength 2, Dexterity 4 , Stamina 4 ; Charisma 4 , Manipulation 2 , Appearance 4 ; Perception 3, Intelligence 2, Wits 2<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Abilities</b>:<br /> Martial Arts 1 (Horn 1)<br /> Melee 1 (Horn 1)<br /> Archery<br /> Thrown 1 (In Celebration 1)<br /> War 1 (Triumphs 2)<br /> Integrity 2 (In Awe 3)<br /> Presence 3 (Bragging 3)<br /> Performance 4 (Greeting 1, Horn 1, When Impressed 1) Resistance 2 (When Impressed 3) Survival 1 (Garlands 2)<br /> Medicine Investigation 1 (Reputations 3) Craft Wood 1 (Woodwinds 1, For the Great 1), Craft Water, Craft Air 1 (Tattoos 1, Scenes of Glory 2)<br /> Occult 1 (Triumphs of Hell 1)<br /> Lore 1 (Triumphs 3) Athletics 3 Awareness 2 Stealth 1 Dodge 2 Larceny Socialize 4 (Reputation 3) Ride 1 (Parades 2) Sail 1 Bureaucracy 1 (Celebrations 2) Linguistics 5+ (Native Old Realm, at least five other languages. Heroic Poetry 3 )<br /> <b>Backgrounds</b>:<br /> Backing 1, Contacts 3 (Horned Greeter\u2019s Gossip), Artifact Some have Demon Ink Tattoos in honor of meeting truly brag worthy individuals.<br /> <br /> <b>Charms</b>:<br /> 2<sup>nd</sup> Excellency: Presence, Socialize, Linguistics, Performance<br /> <br /> Measure the Wind: to measure ones greatness.<br /> <br /> Materialize<br /> <br /> Benefaction- When greeting a great one with their body in some way, be it a simple kiss, or a lengthy romp in the hay, they receive a one die presence bonus for the next scene.<br /> <br /> Eye of Inspiration- Presence may be boosted by the Melicula\u2019s excellency when the target brags about themselves.<br /> <br /> Touch of Divinity- a Horned Greeter\u2019s kiss may restore a Valor or Conviction channel.<br /> <br /> Sense Domain (Glory)- The Melicula may sense a being\u2019s glorious deeds and reputations so as to greet them properly.<br /> <br /> Call- Send messages of glory to all who are impressed or in awe.<br /> <br /> Impromptu Messenger- They may extend their horns clarion through all horns in the area.<br /> <br /> Spice of Custodial Delectation- They regain essence when praising and greeting.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Essence</b>: 2<br /> <br /> Soak 2L/4B<br /> HEALTH: One -0, Three -1, Three -2, One -4, Incapacitated<br /> <br /> Mutations: Most have the Horns mutation unless they have used their horns to spawn other Melicula, and some who have taken to wandering have developed exotic colorations, and bandy hooves.<br /> Notes: Illustrations of the Horned Greaters may be found on page 16 of Roll of Glorious Divininininty II, and page 22 of Compass of Celestial Directions Malfeas)<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-22T20:28:49-08:00","id":1269968,"title":"","content":"<b><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\">https://web.archive.org/web/20160314193252/http://rathess.xi.co.nz:80/exalted/index.php/Characters:Yisterza_the_Demon_Minters</span></b><br /><br /> <b>Yisterza, the Demon Minters.</b><br /><br /> <span style=\"color:#252525\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>Yisterza, the Demon Minters.</b> <b>Demons of the First Circle, Progeny of the Jeweled Auditor</b></span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252525\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">The Jeweled Auditor is found of two things that come from the humans of Creation, lovers and wine. Though some lovers he will not release for disappointing him, and he develops knots from the greed of unskilled lovers, and the left over tang of avarice on wine bottled by mortals with less passion for their wineries and greater lust for their profits. Sometimes these feels have caused precious stones to slough off of the Jeweled Auditors knots. When these stones strike the ground they crack releasing tiny insects that quickly swell as they devour the shards from their birth gems, and other precious resources and symbols of wealth. Soon they are full grown and the denizens of the Demon City know them as the Yisterza, the Demon Minters.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252525\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><br /> The Demon Minters are varied in shape, but can best be described as insects the height of tall men. Most have a set of six limbs, normally in the arrangement of two legs and four arms, but some end up having eight or even twelve limbs divided randomly between legs and arms. Their carapace takes the mixed features of different anthropoid life; one perhaps may have body features such as the head of a mantis with an abdomen appearing as a mix between a cockroach and a ladybug. The sheen of their hides matches those of the various forms of currency in Creation, including copper, silver, gold and even tin. Inside their mouths their mandibles appear as polished cowries, and their large eyes always appear as massive white jade discs with intricate patterns possessing pupils that match the holes found in yen. Spots and camouflage upon their shells blend with green patina, orange rust, and tarnished silver. When their wings deploy they appear as stain glass patterns of precious gems such as rubies, emeralds and diamonds, only thin as scripted bills and seemingly fragile as sugar. Those that dwell acclimated to Kimbery tend to take on the qualities of crustaceans such as possessing massive pinchers, eye stocks, and prawn tails. Minters are most often found wearing the loose billowy open backed robes of office with insignia and iconography depicting the empires that employ them. Their voice sounds like the jingling of spare change formed into words.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252525\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><br /> In most quarters that go beyond basic barter and trade legions of Demon Minters are employed to mint custom currency for their lords. Each Demon Minter has the ability to crystalize motes of essence into solid coins emblazoned with whatever markings their employer desire. Each Demon Minter also has an intuitive sense of weights and measures and can easily mint or forge even the most intricate of mortal currency. A Demon Minter wells up essence and circulates it through their large silk and ivory heart, and through their two smaller jade hearts until they pass them in solid coin form out of their mouths covered in threads of silk. The Yisterza live to count and distribute money in all forms. Each Demon Minter can no more pass up a bribe of honey then a mortal pass up a breath of air. And honey, even diluted with water, will have the same effect as strong alcohol imbibed by a human body. Though the Demon Minters find the barking of dogs hilarious, they detest the beasts as detestable distractions.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252525\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><br /> Though they may eat raw ore and uncut stones, these things will make a Demon Minter ill in the same manner that feeding uncooked meat to man will make him sickly. But anything made into currency instantly become edible and provide nourishment to a Demon Minter, and an interesting trick they can pull off is devouring currency and crapping out any form of selective change adding up to anything equal to or less than the value they devoured, up to an hour of devouring said money.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252525\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><br /> Not only are Yisterza found in groups Minting coins for their kingdoms, but they are also found traveling the edges of their masters\u2019 territories collecting taxes and tithes by crystallizing the very essence of their masters subjects. They vastly increase the efficiency of their masters ability to shepherd their kingdom\u2019s resources, as once they mint motes into coins these same motes may be re absorbed by burn, eating or breaking them in some way, which reverts them to air that may be collected by the first to respire them as they stick slow and heavy as clouds in the air. The process of condensing motes into tangible currency is unpleasant and trying so the Demon Minters prefer to use the motes from other Demons. This means Demons are brought to the Hive Banks of the Yisterza, or the Demon Minters take some Demon leg breakers and travel throughout their territory shaking peons down for their motes.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252525\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><br /> Alas the constant problem the Demon Minters face is that over all indifference the Demon City faces towards their currency initiative. Money is more a human conceit, and most 2nd Circle Demons do not bother with such scraps they can squeeze from their minions when they can just process precious chalcanth till their wicked hearts content. As for the other denizens of Hell, they are more accustomed to being slaves without property, and when they need things they will just barter, trade, or outright take it. But Yisterza are popular amongst sorcerers for intuitive grasp of the exchange rate of currencies throughout the face of Creation. They also make fine loan sharks, and fiduciary advisers. If a Demon Minter drains a being, Demon or mortal, of all their essence they may then hollow out their innards and lay a clutch of amber colored eggs, the size and shape of children\u2019s\u2019 marbles, within equal to that being\u2019s permanent essence. They then string up the corpse in a silk cocoon and after the first month of the New Year the eggs will hatch. If they are not separated their young will devour each other as they consume their cracked eggshells, and will grow to adulthood upon eating at least one sibling. Otherwise they will need to consume about an adults weight in silk and metals to achieve adult status.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252525\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><br /> <b>Summoning</b>:</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252525\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">(Obscurity 3/3)</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252525\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">When a coin that has exchanged hands between over a thousand people lands upon an insect crushing it, then a Demon Minter may hear this sound in their Hive Banks and follow it to Creation to offer their services those that appreciate the concept of coin.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252525\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><br /> <b>Motivation</b>: To encourage the circulation and use of all forms of currency. They possess intimacies of Counting (joy), Hording Money (disgust), Misers (hate), Dogs (shameful amusement)</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252525\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>Virtues</b>:</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252525\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Compassion 2, Conviction 2 , Temperance 4 , Valor 2 Willpower 6</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252525\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>Attributes</b>:</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252525\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Strength 3, Dexterity 3 , Stamina 3 ; Charisma 2 , Manipulation 3 , Appearance 3 ; Perception 3, Intelligence 3, Wits 2</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252525\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>Abilities</b>:</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252525\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Martial Arts 1 (Mandibles 2)</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252525\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Melee 1 (Money 3)</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252525\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Archery</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252525\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Thrown 1 (Money 1)</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252525\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">War 1 (Costs 1)</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252525\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Integrity 2</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252525\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Presence 2</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252525\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Performance 1</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252525\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Resistance 2 (Counting 3) Survival 1</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252525\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Medicine Investigation 2 (Finance 3) Craft Fire 3 (Minting 3), Craft Air 2 (Paper Bills 3), Craft Earth 1 (Weights and Measures 3)</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252525\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Occult 3 (Debts 1)</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252525\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Lore 4 (Numbers 3) Athletics 2 (Lifting 2) Awareness 2 Stealth 2 Dodge 2 Larceny 3 (Forging 3) Socialize 2 (debtors 3) Ride 1 Sail 1 Bureaucracy 5 (Cash 3) Linguistics</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252525\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>Backgrounds</b>:</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252525\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Backing 2, Resources 3, Contacts 2 (Demon Banking)</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252525\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>Charms</b>:</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252525\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">2<sup>nd</sup> Excellencies: Lore, Craft, Bureaucracy</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252525\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Measure the Wind- Those with higher essence can probably circulate money better.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252525\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Materialize</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252525\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Essence Plethora x3</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252525\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Touch of Divinity- Mote distribution</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252525\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Sense Domain- Applies to currency, exchange rates, and fiduciary concerns</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252525\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Tracking- They may track Hell Pesos</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252525\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Chrysalis of Preservation- To solidify motes into Hell Pesos. 10 motes from any source may be solidified into 1 motes worth of coin. The coins appearance can be whatever the Demon Minter desires, but its weight and numbering depend upon how many motes comprise it. Pesos collected in groups of over a hundred motes worth of value may crackle with essence discharge, and result in instances of omen weather when derived from Demon essence.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252525\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Calculated Order of Immediate Action- Minting of Coins and Scripting of Bills, though on small scale they can consume money and crap out change for free.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252525\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Stoke the Flames- used to instill avarice</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252525\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Animating Management- they can make money sort and count itself</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252525\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Landscape Hide- in money</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252525\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Bread of the Weak Spirit- to collect motes for minting</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252525\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Fruit of Living Essence- to remove taxes and tithes of essence for minting</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252525\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Meat of Broken Flesh- Sometimes they have to collect taxes and tithes the hard way</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252525\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Spice of Custodial Delectation- whenever counting, minting, or dealing with money</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252525\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Thaumaturgy: Alchemy 2 (They often learn the procedures to smelt Magical Materials)</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252525\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>Essence</b>: 3</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252525\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><br /> Soak 5L/7B Metallic Carapace 4L/4B</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252525\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">HEALTH: One -0, Four -1, Four -2, One -4, Incapacitated</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252525\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Mutations: They often possess the extra limbs mutations, as well as having variable armored hide and fang/claw mutations (in the form of mandibles and pincers).</span></span></span><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-22T20:29:32-08:00","id":1269969,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://web.archive.org/web/20160314202538/http://rathess.xi.co.nz:80/exalted/index.php/Characters:Zippi_the_Tailors_of_Sighs\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://web.archive.org/web/20160314202538im_/http:/rathess.xi.co.nz/exalted/resources/assets/poweredby_mediawiki_88x31.png\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://web.archive.org/web/20160314202538/http://rathess.xi.co.nz:80/exalted/index.php/Characters:Zippi_the_Tailors_of_Sighs\" target=\"_blank\"> Characters:Zippi the Tailors of Sighs - exalted official wiki - mirror from archive.org </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://web.archive.org/web/20160314202538/http://rathess.xi.co.nz:80/exalted/index.php/Characters:Zippi_the_Tailors_of_Sighs\" target=\"_blank\"> https://web.archive.org/web/20160314202538/http://rathess.xi.co.nz:80/exalted/index.php/Characters:Zippi_the_Tailors_of_Sighs </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div> <br /> <b>Zippi, the Tailors of Sighs.</b><br /><br /> <span style=\"color:#252525\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Zippi, the Tailors of Sighs.</span></span></span><br /> <b>Demons of the First Circle, Progeny of the Lake of Doubt</b> The Lake of Sighs is a living kingdom of somnolence amongst the Pantheon of the Yozi Yestoc the Traveler above the Horizon. From the beaches of Lake of Doubt occasionally fish like shapes will rise and walk on land and then take the form of one of the Tailors of Sighs. Each Zippi takes the form of a lanky seven foot tall humanoid each quaffed with a stylized pompadour of cottony crystalline sugar of any coloration. They are of any gender, and each has large black ovals for eyes which appear to be large fish eggs from which they hatched in the Lake of Doubt. Each has high cheek bones, and little is it recognized in the Age of Sorrows but each Zippi possess the voice of a specific 1st Age Singing Idol found on IAM. Their flesh appears like warm light violet marble with a deeper violet blush.<br /> <br /> Despite their height the Tailors of Sighs are viewed as amongst the most effete of demons. Though their reputation as dandies works to their advantage as they are greatly sought after as superb tailors, and due to the nature of their required ingredients they have become top notch gigolos and courtesans. For a Zippi has utmost integrity for what they will fashion into cloth so they take to working producing sighs of utter bliss from their courtesan duties, as well as sighs of utter relief from workers of Creation given amnesty from execution, to the cherished sighs of fond memories from old doddering dynasts. Zippi cannot stand to see nudity due to poverty, for they believe only in purposeful exposure of flesh, and thus have made it their duty to cloth Creation and the Demon City alike. All this however starts with the Zippi pioneering a new style out of their first sigh of relief after leaving the Lake of doubt with which to make their own nudity a thing of the past.<br /> Zippi will work as a prostitute and a tailor probono for the folk of the Demon City and Creation but they find they can achieve greater heights if they accumulate employment and resources. Summoners have found that these are amongst the more amiable demons to bid the presence of with thaumaturgy for they have a strong sense of duty to garb those who need garbing and to relax the populace. The clothes and fabrics they create are often exceptional if not outright perfect in quality, and even in the Blessed Isle it is common for a Dynast to receive a cape or curtains expertly tailored just for their sensibilities by a demon summoned months ago to pleasure them at a soir\u00e9e. Each Zippi possess a great pare of perfect silver shears with which to aid them in their works, but which they also put to good use upon individuals whom shirk the gift of clothing to lounge naked without the excuse of coitus. These victims are often found later lounging cold in a pool of their own blood having been snipped of their thumbs, if not other protrusions. Each Zippi will accumulate a point of limit for witnessing complete nudity with no signs of sexual congress, limit of one point a day. They also need to roll temperance to keep from assaulting the offenders with scissors. These Demons have been known to be commissioned to create simple Artifacts like Privacy Veils, Coats such as a Fur Merchant\u2019s Gift, and Silken Armor. They have been known to torture or frighten individuals just for sighs sighs of relief. And they will often spend time in the dungeons or torture chambers of Malfeas just to collect the sighs of the relief of death.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Summoning</b>: (Obscurity 2/3)<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> When a maiden weeps in the lambent light of a gibbous moon for a ruined or lacking dress a Tailor of Sighs may appear to craft for her a gown of exquisite beauty from the sigh of her relief.<br /> <br /> Once a year upon any of the nights of Calibration a Tailor of Sighs feels a unique emotion that if they desire will drive them to the nearest body of liquid, whether water or Kimbery, upon which they let out an inscrutable sigh which they cut on the spot forming a pillow unique to the occasion. Upon this pillow they remove one of their eyes, and two thumbs (each from a different being) and sew it into the Pillows seam. They place the pillow into the liquid and upon the first day of the New Year a new tailor is hatched. The parent may regrow their eye if they find the birth pillow and make an eye patch from it and wear it for at least one season, removing it upon the next Calibration revealing a new eye.<br /> <b>Motivation</b>: To Cloth Everyone in Sublime Fabrics Fashioned from Sublime Sighs.<br /> <b>Virtues</b>:<br /> <br /> Compassion 4, Conviction 3, Temperance 2, Valor 2 Willpower 7<br /> <b>Attributes</b>:<br /> <br /> Attributes: Strength 2 , Dexterity 4 , Stamina 3; Charisma 3, Manipulation 3, Appearance 4; Perception 3, Intelligence 3, Wits 2<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Abilities</b>:<br /> Martial Arts 1 (Slapping 1) Melee 2 (Shears 3) Archery Thrown 1 (Tailoring equipment3) War Integrity 3(Tailoring) Presence 3 (In new clothes 3) Performance 4(Graceful Walking 1, Pleasuring 2) Resistance 2 (Tailoring 3) Survival 1 Medicine 1 Investigation 1 (Fashion 3) Craft Water 1 (Leatherworking 3) , Earth , Wood 4 (Tailoring 5) , Air 1 (Fashion 3) , Magitech , Fire Occult 1 (Proper Demon Attire 3, Raksha Fashion 3) Lore 2 (Fashion History 3) Athletics 1 Awareness 2 (Fashion Errors 3) Stealth 2 (In Fashionable Cloths 3) Dodge 2 (In a Cloak 3) Larceny 2 (Disguises 3) Socialize 4 (Fashion 3) Ride Sail Bureaucracy 2 (Fashionable Items 3) Linguistics 2 (Native Old Realm, High Realm, one other)<br /> <b>Backgrounds</b>: Backing 1, Resources 3, Artifact 2 (Silken Armor)<br /> <br /> <b>Charms</b>:<br /> <br /> 2nd Excellency, Craft, Performance, Socialize<br /> Materialize<br /> Benefaction- Upon delivering a new suit or gown the recipient receives a die bonus to appearing Elegant at the next event they wear it at.<br /> Calculated Order of Immediate Action- Finest Fabrics and Silks may be created from honest sighs, which make for excellent exotic ingredients for crafting artifacts such as silken armor.<br /> Spice of Custodial Delectation- Tailoring gives them one essence per scene.<br /> Sheathing the Material Form: any suit they make they may sheath for 2B/1L<br /> <br /> <br /> Thaumaturgy: Alchemy 2 (Plenty of rare magic dyes and paint), Enchantment 2<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Essence</b>: 3<br /> <br /> Attacks: Treat Shears like a Perfect Knife<br /> Soak: L6/6B (Silken Armor 5/3)<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-22T20:30:09-08:00","id":1269970,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://web.archive.org/web/20160315091428/http://rathess.xi.co.nz:80/exalted/index.php/Characters:Jaemi_the_Harvesters_Under_The_Moon\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://web.archive.org/web/20160315091428im_/http:/rathess.xi.co.nz/exalted/resources/assets/poweredby_mediawiki_88x31.png\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://web.archive.org/web/20160315091428/http://rathess.xi.co.nz:80/exalted/index.php/Characters:Jaemi_the_Harvesters_Under_The_Moon\" target=\"_blank\"> Characters:Jaemi the Harvesters Under The Moon - exalted official wiki - mirror from archive.org </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://web.archive.org/web/20160315091428/http://rathess.xi.co.nz:80/exalted/index.php/Characters:Jaemi_the_Harvesters_Under_The_Moon\" target=\"_blank\"> https://web.archive.org/web/20160315091428/http://rathess.xi.co.nz:80/exalted/index.php/Characters:Jaemi_the_Harvesters_Under_The_Moon </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div> <br /> <b>Jaemi the Harvesters Under the Moon.</b><br /><br /> <span style=\"color:#252525\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Jaemi, the Harvesters Under the Moon.</span></span></span><br /> <b>Demons of the First Circle, Progeny of the Ivory Idol of Salt and Flame</b> The Frowning Idol of Salt and Flames created the first Harvester Under the Moon by incubating the blood of a sacrifice in a beast of Burden for a month. The method is now used by the Jaemi themselves who may produce new Harvesters by creating a pill of their own blood and using it to inseminate a beast of burden which will swell with a new Jaemi for one month and then burst open spawning a full grown Harvester.<br /> <br /> The Jaemi are often three or more yards tall with the head of an oxen and the snout of a boar complete with a brass ring etched with characters for Labor in Rocktongue. Their bodies are hunched lean and powerful with calluses and scars from a lifetime of labor and beige fur mixed with jet black thick hairs. Their arms are like a mix between badgers and an ape\u2019s. with three brass clawed fingers and a thumb. They often garb themselves in overalls and they wear a wide brimmed hat made of silver or brass straw to keep the harsh shining of Liger from their eyes. Their horns are brass and thickly grooved.<br /> <br /> The Jaemi were made to farm the brass and stone rubble of the Demon City. They have taken to both keeping a farm by themselves, or taking a mate and farming together, or even living in a demonic commune with each demon taking their role. The Jaemi have varied labors that they expect of themselves, and a single Harvester may farm Brass bread, heard Hell Cattle, collect silver and brass timber, and mine the jeweled bowels of the bones of Malfeas all in the same season. Though they find certain labors take priority in certain seasons, all for the sake of diversity, and they an irrepressible urge to only harvest each crop for one season a year. So in the Season of Fire they may harvest Brassbread for the Pastry Smiths at market, and then in the Season of Wood they may plant Bonecorn for the great milltowers to grind for use in tortillas.<br /> <br /> The Jaemi are masters at husbanding animals in hell. They often take to breeding with their cattle to create bloodlines of Hellbeast for superior meat, labor, and milk. They see it as their duty to do this ever few generations, and even when summoned into Creation a Sorcerer must take great pains to not have their Harvester breed with local livestock. This is particularly difficult during full moons, when the Jaemi are filled with the urge to \u201clabor\u201d and tend their animals till the sun rises. Much crops may be harvested, and bastards sown during these events.<br /> <br /> The Jaemi are rough backbones of Demon culture, they reap the fields to bring food to the markets of the Demon City, and cut lumber and quarry stone for the Hopping Puppeteers to rearrange into tenements, and they provide mined jewels for the Heranhals to make into brooches and rings. They collect Hellcattle milk to made into cheese and wine, and they fish for Kimbery spawn to feed the slaves of their betters. They provide shelter for Neomah to work their craft, and housing for Anuhles so they may harvest their silk, and food for Firmin so they may collect fashion tools for them. The Jaemi support the Demons of Hell so that they may continue their lives of toil and torture, for that is their nature. Most sacred to them is the Blood Red Moon of the Demon City which they worship as a Goddess of the Harvest. Sometimes their Patron even rewards the greatest of them with sacred tools of Orichalcum, Moonsilver, and even Starmetal tainted with Vitriol.<br /> Summoners are drawn to summoning the Jaemi to act as a diverse labor force for a multitude of projects whether it is a Lumber worker, harsh mining, or simple field work, animal sheparding, and even cooking; the Harvesters are familiar with them all and they are excellent brutes and thugs. They make excellent support for any number of other demon slaves.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Summoning</b>: (Obscurity 1/2)<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Sometimes during the Harvest Moon an empty farmstead with unharvested crops, and cattle in need of milking and shearing may find a Harvester Under the Moon crawling out of the lands well to tend the land.<br /> <br /> <b>Motivation</b>: To provide essential support for a community through diligent backbreaking labor.<br /> <b>Virtues</b>:<br /> <br /> Compassion 3 , Conviction 5 , Temperance 1 , Valor 3 Willpower 8<br /> <b>Attributes</b>:<br /> <br /> Strength 4 , Dexterity 3 , Stamina 6; Charisma 1 , Manipulation 1 , Appearance 2; Perception 2, Intelligence 1, Wits 2<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Abilities</b>: Martial Arts 3 (Grappling 3) Melee 4 (Farm Tools 3) Archery 1 (At Night 3) Thrown 1 (Rocks 3) War 1 (Herding 3) Integrity 2 (To Labor 3) Presence 2 (Intimidation 3) Performance 1 (Under the Moon 3) Resistance 5 (Under the Moon 3) Survival 4 (Farming 2, Animal Raising 1) Medicine Investigation Craft Water 1 (Following a Recipe 3), Earth 1(Mining 3) , Wood 2 (Farming 3) , Air 1 (Painting 1) , Magitech , Fire Occult 1 (Moons 3) Lore 1 Athletics 3 (Lifting 3) Awareness 2 (Intruders 3) Stealth 1 (Under the Moon 3) Dodge 1 (Under the Moon 3) Larceny 1(Black Market 3) Socialize 2 (Neighbors 3) Ride 3 (Cattle 3) Sail 1 (Rivers 1) Bureaucracy 1 (Economics 3) Linguistics (Native Old Realm)<br /> <b>Backgrounds</b>: Backing 1, Resources 2<br /> <br /> <b>Charms</b>:<br /> <br /> <br /> 1st Excellency Martial Arts, Melee, Ride<br /> 2nd Excellency Resistance, Survival, Craft, Athletics OxBody x2<br /> Landscape Travel (Doubles any travel on a Farm)<br /> Hurry Home (Back to their Farmhouse)<br /> Affinity (Water) Control (The Jaemi have learned the secrets of irrigation and with a watering can may channel water and Kimbery to feed crops)<br /> Meat of the Broken Flesh<br /> Spice of Custodial Delectation (Hard Labor gives them a mote every scene)<br /> TMA: The Jaemi have taken to spreading the Golden Harvest Style Martial Arts among their kind.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Essence</b>: 3<br /> <br /> Soak: L4/7B Thick Fur/Hair L1/B1<br /> NOTES: The Jaemi are often Armed with Exceptional Axes, Scythes, Sledges, Hoes, and Shovels. They also have a desire to start a family and will choose a neighbor to be their mate who they will constantly court for their hand in wedlock. They have an urge to keep at least two pets and will try to adopt from wild pigs, dogs, and cats. They must roll temperance to resist the urge to copulate with their cattle each month. Refraining from Labor for 25 hours results in one limit. Roll Conviction during a full moon and gain the successes in limit and willpower. They possess the Claws Horn and Hoof Mutations at varying levels spending 6 points of mutations on them. They will not eat dog, cat, or pig meat because they believe them to be pet animals rather than cattle. This does not extend to wolves, jackals, and large Predatory Cats, but it does extend to boars. Forcing them to eat or slaughter these beings for meat results in one limit added per day of slaughter.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-22T20:30:56-08:00","id":1269971,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://web.archive.org/web/20160314192641/http://rathess.xi.co.nz:80/exalted/index.php/Characters:Vlectics_the_Mother_Vines\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://web.archive.org/web/20160314192641im_/http:/rathess.xi.co.nz/exalted/resources/assets/poweredby_mediawiki_88x31.png\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://web.archive.org/web/20160314192641/http://rathess.xi.co.nz:80/exalted/index.php/Characters:Vlectics_the_Mother_Vines\" target=\"_blank\"> Characters:Vlectics the Mother Vines - exalted official wiki - mirror from archive.org </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://web.archive.org/web/20160314192641/http://rathess.xi.co.nz:80/exalted/index.php/Characters:Vlectics_the_Mother_Vines\" target=\"_blank\"> https://web.archive.org/web/20160314192641/http://rathess.xi.co.nz:80/exalted/index.php/Characters:Vlectics_the_Mother_Vines </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <b>Vlectics, the Mother Vines.</b><br /><br /> <span style=\"color:#252525\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Vlectics, the Mother Vines.</span></span></span><br /> <b>Demons of the First Circle, Progeny of All Hell.</b><br /> <span style=\"color:#252525\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Vlectics, the Mother Vines</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252525\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Much like the Anuhles the Mother Vines are less a specific species of Demon but are a common recurring archetype created by various demons throughout the Demon City. They serve the purpose of birthing broods of other demons to help proliferate the desirable populations for the various lords of Malfeas. Even the Yozis themselves will spawn the Mother Vines populate newly unfurled landscapes of their World Bodies.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252525\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">The Vlectics are created as seeds and placed into the ground and fed chalcanth which catalyzes their growth from a seed into an actual First Circle Demon. Each type of demon refined into chalcanth and fed to the growing seed modulates the fully grown Vlectic\u2019s capabilities allowing them to birth these demons after collecting enough essence and gestating them in seedeggs. Some Mother Vines are fed only one draught of halcanth as a seed resulting in a fully grown Mother Vine from the spot after a year has passed. If fed another dose of chalcanth the Vlectic will take a season to mature, and another dose will cut this time to only a month, with each additional dose cutting the maturation time in half.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252525\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Full grown Vlectics appear as a large knot of brass vines ranging from the size of a childs arm to that of the length and thickness of an Anaconda. Thicker older limbs have a mixture of scale like brass bark, and cutting them will cause them to bleed sweet smelling ichor that has potent alcoholic properties affecting those who consume it like two doses of strong liquor per dose. Their central mass appears much like a mixture between a pitcher plant, a Venus-flytrap and a clam. Appearing on the outside as tarnished brass with a green patina, and the inside of the mouth appears like a pile of meat from various demons and animals, preserved in various states ranging from fresh bloody kills, to rotten and maggot ridden. Foolish demons looking for an easy meal are lured in by the scent and the sweet music that drifts about, and the mouth finally snaps shut, grappling the demon and melting its essence with vitriol to be converted into nourishment for the eggfruit which ripens on the vine limps. The vine limbs often spread into the very ground, or wrap around any demon they can find to leech essence from, petrifying their corpse into brasswood lumps. Some limbs climb up or through the various buildings of the Demon City in their expansion of territory and search for nourishment. The central knot is the major consumer of the Demon\u2019s anatomy with the limbs manly working as structure, sensory organs, auxillary feeding mouths, and most importantly as budding stages for the growth of egg fruit which hatch into demons they are programed to spawn.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252525\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Each eggfruit grows from a tiny cherry sized greyish bulb to a bright scarlet corrugated pumpkin-like shape of the size necessary to hatch the particular demon. It normally takes a month from conception of the eggfruit for it to hatch. 10 motes are committed for each level of Essence the newborn of the Demon\u2019s type typically possesses and a willpower point is also needed to initiate the grow. Everyday each eggfruit needs 3 motes of essence spent to feed it, which ideally will come from a grappled and petrified demon. During this month of growth mutations may occur if beings with and essence of 5+ are fed into the eggfruit, or if other specifically tamper with it to instigate mutation in the newborn. If the Vlectic is attuned to a manse or demesnes that is not aspected to Malfeas or Vitriol mutations often occur in the newborn if explainable by the foreign essence. For instance a Bloodape hatched from a Vlectic attuned to a Kimbery demesnes may have amphibious mutations, or a Neomah fed by a Solar Manse in Creation may be born with the extra limbs (arms) mutation in emulation of the Unconquered Sun. If the Vlectic has access to hearthstones or cults such essence respired from these sources may mutate some of their eggfruit as well, or alter the standard traits of the demons born from their essence, such as changing languages based on the prayers of the cult, and specialties tied to the cult or manses.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252525\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">The Mother Vines are amongst the oldest of the 1st Circle Demons, and they are very primal expressions of the urges of Hell to devour, grow, and spawn.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252525\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>Summoning</b>:</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252525\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">(Obscurity 2/4)</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252525\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Any mother deceased but with a stomach swollen still with child, living or unborn, buried with a trinket of brass may have a Mother Vine grow from their grave when the dawns first light shines upon it. For this reason it is viewed as bad luck to bury women with brass in many places throughout creation, including such things as pets that died in childbirth buried with a brass bell.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252525\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Sorcerers primarily summon Mother Vines as a method to produce other demons in Creation, and some rather enjoy growing one within their layer just simple for the sheer intimidation factor of having a man-eating demon factory in their dungeons. They make exquisite security systems. Wise sorcerers know not to summon more than one Mother Vine, because if one were ever to eat another they would gain the ability to spawn eggfruit containing other Mother Vines and may over run their domain with a demon plague beyond their capabilities to contain. Mother Vines gain one limit every day they do not have at least one victim petrified upon their vines. They also treat releasing any captured prey as an unacceptable order.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252525\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><br /> <b>Motivation</b>: To spread, coil, and devour to bring forth children far and wide.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252525\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><br /> <b>Virtues</b>: Compassion 5 , Conviction 4 , Temperance 1 , Valor 2</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252525\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Willpower 8</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252525\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>Attributes</b>: Strength 6, Dexterity 2 , Stamina 5 ; Charisma 1 , Manipulation 1 , Appearance 2 ; Perception 4, Intelligence 1, Wits 1</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252525\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><br /> <b>Abilities</b>:</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252525\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Martial Arts 3 (Grapple 3) Melee Archery Thrown War Integrity 1 Presence 1 (Her Children 3) Performance 2 (Dancing 1, Singing 2) Resistance 3 Survival 3 (Hunting 1, Traps 1) Medicine Investigation 1 Craft</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252525\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Occult 2 (Demon City 1, Creation Myths 2)</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252525\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Lore 1 (History 1) Athletics 4 (Crushing 3) Awareness 2 (Prey 3) Stealth Dodge 1 (Vines 3) Larceny 1 (Slight of Vine 2) Socialize 1 (Her Children 3) Ride Sail Bureaucracy 1 (Her Children 3) Linguistics (Native Old Realm)</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252525\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>Backgrounds</b></span></span></span><br /> <br /> Backing 1, Cult 1 (Their Children are born with intimacies to spread prayers to their Mother, and will spread this if they escape to Creation) <br /> <span style=\"color:#252525\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><br /> <b>Charms</b>:</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252525\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">2<sup>nd</sup> Excellency: Martial Arts, Survival, Performance</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252525\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Essence Plethora x2</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252525\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">(Increased as they grow and expand)</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252525\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>Materialize</b> (The Mother Vines are rarely Dematerialized, usually only doing so when finding a place to take root)</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252525\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>Measure the Wind</b> (Used to measure the succulence of their prey, and to see if their Children have grown)</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252525\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Reserve of Will x1</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252525\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Principle of Motion(8 extra actions are usually saved, and used to grapple with multiple vines)</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252525\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>Endowment</b> (Endowment is used to mutate or add traits to an eggfruit, usually those obtained from the natures of devoured spirits, this counts as a training effect and is permanent)</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252525\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>Amethyst Awareness</b> (The vines smell and taste the essence of their environment)</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252525\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>Intrusion Sensing Method</b> (Senses intruders to devour)</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252525\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>Memory Mirror</b> (They Devour the memories of their Prey)</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252525\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>Call</b> (Mother Vines may call those they have birthed into this world)</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252525\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>Impromptu Messenger</b> (They may sing through the mouths of their Children)</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252525\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>Chrysalis of Preservation</b> (Food trapped in their vines are petrified in brass to be slowly drained to feed their young)</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252525\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>Host of Spirits</b> (Unique version of the Charm that allows them to Create a Demon of the Type of any Chalcanth they have Tasted, as well as other Mother Vines if they have eaten another one. Commit 10 motes for each level of essence of the demon, and spend one willpower. If these are fed 3 motes every day they survive to the next day. If they survive a month they hatch into a Demon. One eggfruit may be conceived only when the Mother Vine devours someone in her central knot)</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252525\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>Calculated Order of Immediate Action</b> (The Vine Mother Creates meat from past prey in her central mouth to lure new prey)</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252525\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Bread of Weak Spirit</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252525\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Meat of Broken Flesh</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252525\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Fruit of Living Essence</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252525\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>Ox-Body x 2</b> (More are purchased as the spirit expands)</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252525\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>Paralyze</b> (used to stun their prey when gripped by the Vine)</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252525\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>Essence</b>:</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252525\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Essence: 4</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252525\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Soak 6L/11B Brass Scalebark 4L/6B</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252525\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">HEALTH: Two-0, Nine -1, Eight -2, -4, Incapacitated</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252525\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Mutations: Extra Limbs can represent clusters of vines, Fangs, Armored Hide blight, and at least one level of Large mutation amongst others. Often the Vlectics mutate as they grow, often gaining the blight Penatrating Strike to bore through walls with their vines, and the affliction natural missile to represent thorns shooting towards prey.</span></span></span><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-22T20:32:57-08:00","id":1269972,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://web.archive.org/web/20160315091433/http://rathess.xi.co.nz:80/exalted/index.php/Characters:Jyeontelleaveau_the_Screaming_Man_Parade\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://web.archive.org/web/20160315091433im_/http:/rathess.xi.co.nz/exalted/resources/assets/poweredby_mediawiki_88x31.png\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://web.archive.org/web/20160315091433/http://rathess.xi.co.nz:80/exalted/index.php/Characters:Jyeontelleaveau_the_Screaming_Man_Parade\" target=\"_blank\"> Characters:Jyeontelleaveau the Screaming Man Parade - exalted official wiki - mirror from archive.org </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://web.archive.org/web/20160315091433/http://rathess.xi.co.nz:80/exalted/index.php/Characters:Jyeontelleaveau_the_Screaming_Man_Parade\" target=\"_blank\"> https://web.archive.org/web/20160315091433/http://rathess.xi.co.nz:80/exalted/index.php/Characters:Jyeontelleaveau_the_Screaming_Man_Parade </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <b>Jyeontelleaveau the Screaming Man Parade.</b><br /><br /> <span style=\"color:#252525\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Jyeontelleaveau, the Screaming Man Parade.</span></span></span><br /> <b>Demons of the First Circle, Progeny of the Grinning Murdernaut</b> Mydwryths, ghosts, and especially humans are long sought after, but often rare and protected prey. A prey the Grinning Murdernaut weeps melancholy just imagining his demon brethren never get to realize the joy of slaughtering such a child of the earth, even while he slaughters the same demon brethren he weeps for. When his tears mix with their gore and viscera out will sprouts the Screaming Man Parade. And they have spread throughout the Demon City with the very desperate desire the citizens of Malfeas have to duplicate the experience of a human victim, or consort or slave.<br /> The Jyeontelleaveau have the same range in height as a human ranging from pygmy height of barely under a yard off the ground to looming height of nearly three times that, but while humanity has stabilized their height to a more medium range that varies in populations, the Jyeontelleaveau often vary randomly with each generation. Each has a thick elephant like skin which ranges from pinkish grey hue of a hippo, to a pale corpse white, to a dull greyish blue of a frostbite sufferer near death. They have simple features with four rough digits and no noticeable articulation for wrists or hips. Their feet are simple and stump like without toes, and they only possess a single eye on their thumb like heads. A deep grove follows from the deep eye socket much like the shape of a thunderbolt or root all the way down to their pelvis. Roughly where their bellybutton would be they possess another larger eye. This fissure pulsates whenever they speak. They do not start with any method to chew food so they pour slurry into an opening along this fissure. Both eyes are large and oddly colored and appear more like the eye from a whale or squid.<br /> The Scream Man Parade are born believing themselves to be humans. Their knowledge however of the human condition is grossly inaccurate. For instance they desire to consume any organic substance from Creation believing everything from bear droppings to owl bones must be human foods and a delicacy somewhere in Creation. In Malfeas they take any rumors and news then can get modeling their looks after what they believe humans would wear and style themselves after. If they find humans they intensely ape their habits with a stern eye. They will start to form their features into the rough features of humans they witness, and when they can they will perform amateur surgery to remove human organs and insert it into themselves, they replace it with anything nearby at hand, whether a baby\u2019s rattle, or a live mouse. Their mistaken belief is that more organs equal more humanity. The Screaming Man Parade with greater amount of organs are given the greater respect, and can often imitate human form and speech with greater accuracy and precision then their fellows. However they appear morbidly obese as they are literally stuffed with stolen organs, and any close physical examination (Perception + Medicine roll difficulty 1) may reveal medical oddities such as additional hearts or stomachs in the wrong area. They may only steal one organ from a human, and the theft is never fatal as long as they find any replacement. Though expect reduced traits and or deficiencies if for instance they replace a womans left hemisphere of the brain with a small wooden horse.<br /> Tradition has it that humans breed with other humans. So the most organ heavy Jyeontelleaveau will find one or more others heavy in organs. They will then each donate at least one stolen organ, with one member also donating enough skin to contain it, and the rest filling the sack of skin and organs with blood. They all may add essence, and at least one must spend a willpower until they have collected 20 motes and 1 Willpower point, and a new Screaming Man Parade is born. Those parents wealthy in organs may produce multiple children in one go. They believe this is how humans are made, totally missing the details of how families work besides the fact that they are congregations of humans. It is also worth noting the Jyeontelleaveau are hermaphroditic.<br /> The Screaming Man Parade make excellent apprentices and sorcerers often summon them with this in mind. They will start with very general knowledge of humans, but if exposed to what they believe are humans they will often latch onto a perceived template that is given to them, and thus apprenticeship is a natural calling for those who want to shape their own gullible apprentice. They often take information about humanity given to them as truths, with contradictions easily confusing them. They will dress as they believe their roll calls for. In Hell they make natural slaves and victims of violence or hunger as that is their first notion on what being a human is all about. They have an irresistible urge to steal organs from a human if they are left alone with one who is either sleeping, or injured with an open wound, they cannot be commanded not to do this and will treat such orders as unacceptable unless the their masters are in the same room as them. Proving to the Screaming Man Parade that they are not human will force them to roll their Willpower, and receive a point of limit for each success.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Summoning</b>: (Obscurity 1/3)<br /> <br /> When person loses their identity and everything of importance they may speak to offer one of their organs to their reflection in a mirror or pool of water for companionship. A Screaming Man Parade who is also gazing at their reflection in the Demon City may hear this and accept this offer in person walking out of the reflection.<br /> <br /> <b>Motivation</b>: To prove my humanity. <b>Virtues</b>:<br /> <br /> <br /> Compassion 2 , Conviction 2 , Temperance 2 , Valor 1<br /> Willpower 5<br /> <b>Attributes</b>:<br /> <br /> Strength 3, Dexterity 2 , Stamina 3 ; Charisma 2 , Manipulation 2 , Appearance 1 ; Perception 3, Intelligence 2, Wits 3<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Abilities</b>:<br /> <br /> Martial Arts 1 Melee 1 Archery Thrown 1 (Rocks 2) War 1 (Other Jyeontelleaveau 3) Integrity 2 (Perceived humanity 3) Presence 2 (Screaming 3) Performance 2 (Screaming 3) Resistance 3 (Toiling 3) Survival 1 (Farming 1) Medicine 1 (Organ Transplants 3) Investigation 1 (Finding Human Facts 3) Craft Water 1 (Recipes 1), Earth 1 (Mining 1) , Wood , Air<br /> Occult<br /> Lore Athletics 2 (Running 3) Awareness 2 (Humans 3) Stealth 1 (Alone 3) Dodge 3 (While in Work Clothes 3) Larceny Socialize 1 (Other Jyeontelleaveau 3) Ride Sail Bureaucracy Linguistics (Native Old Realm)<br /> <b>Backgrounds</b>: Backing 1, they enjoy collecting Contacts, Allies and Resources amongst other perceived Humans, and if having perceived humans with pets may develop Familiars with animals or lesser hellbeasts/demons.<br /> <br /> NOTE: Give one that has found apprenticeship or has had enough time to stalk humanity 6 additional skill dots divided around for their perceived role, and 4 specialty points.<br /> <b>Charms</b>:<br /> <br /> 1st Excellency Resistance, Athletics<br /> 2nd Excellency (Develops an Excellency pertaining to their perceived role in Humanity)<br /> Materialize<br /> Call- Other Jyeontalleaveau<br /> Shapechange- May crudely change features to appear more human. With one organ skin tone may be slightly darkened or adjusted. With ten organs they may mimic a human body expertly, though with obvious signs of displaced and extra organs upon physical contact.<br /> Landscape Travel- May double running speed when screaming and flailing limbs wildly<br /> Meat of Broken Flesh- this activates when performing surgery to steal an organ. Each organ also gives them one experience point. Having more stolen organs then willpower makes them desire to reproduce with other Jyeontelleaveau.<br /> Divine Perogative- towards an intimacy involving their human role, including perceived family<br /> Scourge- used when stealing an organ reduces and appropriate trait<br /> Shatter- when cornered and frightened a scream of terror may shock their assailant, roll Valor + Essence + Charisma for damage, it is unblockable, and must have DV equal to or exceeding Screaming Man Parade\u2019s Valor + Charisma.<br /> <br /> <b>Essence</b>: 2<br /> <br /> Soak: 4B/2L Scab-like hide:1B/1L<br /> NOTES: Screaming Man Parades may develop like heroic mortals when they seem to have succeeded in proving their humanity. Some have developed mastery of TMAs to continue Mortal schools after their adopted families have passed. They have deep rooted fear of Demons, must succeed in a Valor roll once per scene in order to do anything other than obey an order given by a demon or run from a demon. Excess organs sometime result in the purchase of mutations.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-22T20:33:54-08:00","id":1269973,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://web.archive.org/web/20160315090046/http://rathess.xi.co.nz:80/exalted/index.php/Characters:Polaeko_the_Demon_Barbers\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://web.archive.org/web/20160315090046im_/http:/rathess.xi.co.nz/exalted/resources/assets/poweredby_mediawiki_88x31.png\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://web.archive.org/web/20160315090046/http://rathess.xi.co.nz:80/exalted/index.php/Characters:Polaeko_the_Demon_Barbers\" target=\"_blank\"> Characters:Polaeko the Demon Barbers - exalted official wiki - mirror from archive.org </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://web.archive.org/web/20160315090046/http://rathess.xi.co.nz:80/exalted/index.php/Characters:Polaeko_the_Demon_Barbers\" target=\"_blank\"> https://web.archive.org/web/20160315090046/http://rathess.xi.co.nz:80/exalted/index.php/Characters:Polaeko_the_Demon_Barbers </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div> <br /> <b>Polaeko, the Demon Barbers.</b><br /><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252525\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><br /> Polaeko the Demon Barbers.</span></span></span><br /> <b>Demons of the First Circle, Progeny of the Hundred Steps</b> Polaeko, the Demon Barbers, Progeny of the Hundred Steps<br /> In the Demon City there are entire races spawned for any service a man could want. The parlors, salons, and small businesses of the Demon City have numerous types of Demons all competing over the same jobs. The Polaeko have earned the title of Demon Barber however not due to their singular skill in grooming but due to each one plying a multitude of other trades as all in the same parlor. While in Creation one may expect a barber to not just groom them but also provide dental services on the side the Demon Barbers are much more diversified in their available services. A Blood Ape after a hard day of paid murder can go to any Demon Barber\u2019s shop for a trim and expect to also be served exotic liqueurs, hear the newest jingle, and receive a \u201chappy ending\u201d before they pay, and that is not usually enough to receive a tip. The Polaeko take pride in diversifying. Some may pool their resources together into their Shop, offering enough diversity to please any customer without even having to dip into hiring other species of Demons, though they find nothing wrong with supplementing their store with the occasional Anuhle sweeper, or Angyalka playing in the corner. Others go out on their own and work stands in the corner of the streets, offering shave and a haircut, a cheap quicky, and general freelance labor. Others have regular work as the personal stylist and confidant/concubine of a 2nd Circle or other Citizen. They can be found as employer or employee in equal amounts. One thing they all hold dear from their Progenitor, the 3rd Circle soul of Qaf, the Hundred Steps is that in Hell you need to work for a living!<br /> <br /> The Demon Barbers appear like humans with red hair,and skin the grey of old monochrome parchment, though they often dye their hair a number of colors. The males often appear to be past their prime but still quite handsome, and they sport a well-tended handle bar mustache with waxed tips. The females on the other hand appear to be in their 20-30s, and they sport a much more expansive set of haircuts including what would be defined as tribal or ethnic styles. The females enjoy tattoos and piercings and will often offer such services themselves. The Polaeko often dress in a fashion similar to barbers in Creation, with the males sporting red and white stripes. They find the number four auspicious and if forming partnerships they will usually have four members in their business ventures of running a babershop. Both Itinerant Demon Barbers, and those who settle in a shop will prefer to form a quartet if they are not going to work alone. Their ministrations as a quartet have even helped them when looking for work contract killers, and as many demons have found their synchronized singing annoying as there are those who adore it.<br /> <b>Summoning</b>:<br /> <br /> (Obscurity 2/3)<br /> If a barbershop collects a decade of unswept hair, and finally sweeps the floor into a pile and burns it a Demon Barber may follow this scent through the Endless Desert and into Creation. Sorcerers often resort to summoning Polaeko when they desire a versatile servant, or simply a good barber or stylist. They are hardworking and loyal, and have often developed extensive contacts. However a wise Sorcerer knows that a demon confident most work for them until their death, as they have often collected far too many of their personal secrets.<br /> Polaeko receive one point of limit a week if limited to only one job, rather than plying multiple trades. They also receive one point of limit a scene if forced to sing in a group, unless it adds up to four members. The Polaeko reproduce irregularly. When they feel it is time, one of them will sweep the hair from their parlor and gather it in a pile with 2 other Demon Barbers and they will sing their sacred Genesis tune while they burn it with the fourth member emerging from the flame to aid them in the song.<br /> <b>Motivation</b>:<br /> <b>Virtues</b>:<br /> <br /> <br /> Compassion 2, Conviction 4 , Temperance 3 , Valor 2<br /> Willpower 7<br /> <b>Attributes</b>: Strength 2, Dexterity 4 , Stamina 3 ; Charisma 3 , Manipulation 2 , Appearance 3 ; Perception 3, Intelligence 2, Wits 3<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Abilities</b>:<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Martial Arts 1<br /> Melee 3 (Scissors 1, Straight Razor 1, Contract Killing 1)<br /> Archery<br /> Thrown 1<br /> War<br /> Integrity 3 (Confidentiality 2)<br /> Presence 2<br /> Performance 4 (Singing 1, Quartets 1)<br /> Resistance 2<br /> Survival 1<br /> Medicine 1 (Dentistry 2, Bleeding 1)<br /> Investigation 1<br /> Craft Wood 3 (Grooming 3), Craft Water 1 (Drinks 2), Craft Air 1 (Tattoos 1)<br /> Occult 1 (Demons 2, Demon City 1)<br /> Lore 1 (Weather 1)<br /> Athletics 1<br /> Awareness 2<br /> Stealth 1<br /> Dodge 3<br /> Larceny 2 (Sleight of Hand 1, Forgery 1)<br /> Socialize 3 (Patrons 2, Confidentiality 1)<br /> Ride 1<br /> Sail 1<br /> Bureaucracy 1 (Business 2)<br /> Linguistics 2 (Native Old Realm, Two other Languages)<br /> <b>Backgrounds</b>:<br /> Backing 1, Resources 2, Contacts 5(Common Patrons), Allies 3 (Patrons and other Polaeko), Artifacts (Some may have Demon Ink Tattoos)<br /> <b>Charms</b>:<br /> 1<sup>st</sup> Excellency- Performance, Socialize, Melee<br /> <br /> 2<sup>nd</sup> Excellency- Craft<br /> <br /> <b>Essence Plethora x1</b><br /> <b>Hurry Home-</b> To their barber shop<br /> <b>Materialize-</b><br /> <b>Measure the Wind-</b> to gauge their customers<br /> <b>Reserve of Will x1</b><br /> <b>Benefaction-</b> Customers receive a bonus die to Presence, Socialize, Performance, or Stealth for a day after getting a haircut. This can only benefit an individual once a week.<br /> <b>Stoke the Flame-</b> After a Haircut the customer may have a feeling of bravery, amorousness, or general excitement<br /> <b>Animating Management-</b> their scissors, shaving blades, or brooms may be animated<br /> <b>Spice of Custodial Delectation-</b> Motes gained for working or managing their stand or shop<br /> <b>Spirit Cutting Attack-</b> Their Shears and Straight Razor may cut dematerialized beings<br /> <b>Bane Weapon-</b> Does aggravated damage to Hare and Rabbit Spirits.<br /> <b>Essence</b>:<br /> 3<br /> <br /> <br /> Soak 3L/4B Barbers Apron 2L/1B<br /> HEALTH: One -0, Five -1, Four -2, One -4, Incapacitated<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-22T20:34:34-08:00","id":1269974,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://web.archive.org/web/20160314203426/http://rathess.xi.co.nz:80/exalted/index.php/Characters:Cia%E2%80%99nydanhephaenae_the_Empty_Madness\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://web.archive.org/web/20160314203426im_/http:/rathess.xi.co.nz/exalted/resources/assets/poweredby_mediawiki_88x31.png\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://web.archive.org/web/20160314203426/http://rathess.xi.co.nz:80/exalted/index.php/Characters:Cia%E2%80%99nydanhephaenae_the_Empty_Madness\" target=\"_blank\"> Characters:Cia&rsquo;nydanhephaenae the Empty Madness - exalted official wiki - mirror from archive.org </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://web.archive.org/web/20160314203426/http://rathess.xi.co.nz:80/exalted/index.php/Characters:Cia%E2%80%99nydanhephaenae_the_Empty_Madness\" target=\"_blank\"> https://web.archive.org/web/20160314203426/http://rathess.xi.co.nz:80/exalted/index.php/Characters:Cia%E2%80%99nydanhephaenae_the_Empty_Madness </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <b>Cia'nydanhephaenae, the Empty Madness.</b><br /><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252525\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><br /> Cia\u2019nydanhephaenae, the Empty Madness.</span></span></span><br /> <b>Demons of the First Circle, Progeny of the White Zone</b> The Empty Madness have become amongst the favorite victims of the Ebon Dragon. Though they are not descended from his soul hierarchy being the progeny of a third circle Demon of Elloge, the Ebon Dragon so favors their madness and suffering that he has adopted them as foster demons of his soul hierarchy, even going so far as to \u201cencourage\u201d at least 4 2nd circle demons descended from him, including the Keeper of the Forge of Night, to produce and spread their numbers. The Empty Madness originally came to being in a fold in Malfeas\u2019s space called the White Zone, which was a 3rd Circle Soul of Elloge expressed as a 2 dimensional singularity.<br /> The Cia\u2019nydanhephaenus have derived their name, according to demon lore, from the original 4, some say 3, species of demon native to the White Zone. They take the form of humanoid shaped beings, though simplified to the extreme. They normally possess a spherical head and an ovoid shaped torso with four skeletal thin limbs. Their limbs usually appear as sticks or pegs with no discernable digits visible unless they specifically spread their fingers, and some do not possess fingers instead they will have mitten like hands, and other will have digits ranging from 3 to 5 in number. These limbs appear to thin and black and stretched taut over their simple skeletons, though when cut they appear to bleed as if they possess arteries or veins. Though extremely simple on the outside, their internal anatomy seems quite similar to humans. Normally females are the only ones to possess hair, but various males have mutated to possess elaborate quaffs of their own. The vast majority of their males however are bald, though they indeed have hair follicles upon their faces and may even grow beards. Most of the species possesses a pale pinkish skin, but others have diversified, through mutation or the inclusion breeding with humans, to include the various shades of Creations skin and hair tones . Where their eyes should be they have empty sockets which function in the same manner, and even bleed if poked. Virtually none however possess noses.<br /> The communities of the White Zone are often harshly segregated into roughly four major populations based off of common characteristics. One population, known as the Sirk Race, for instance possesses a much larger head, but with a short 3-4 foot sized body with close together tiny eyes and mouth at the bottom of the quadrant of their heads, and square-like torsos. They have a subpopulation, known as the Evad Nation, that possess longer legs making them appear around 5 feet in height. Another population, known as the Bor Tribe, is usually a little over 5 feet in height with larger eyes and square torsos. The Tam Culture is often over 6 feet in height with oblong shaped torsos and eye sockets. The last major group is made out of many populations of sub-species that have gathered into communities of their own and are known simply as the Tseug. The Tseug have often come from refugees that immigrated to the White Zone from communities that evolved in other areas of the Demon City.<br /> While in the White Zone they appear as two dimensional individuals, but outside the White Zone they still retain their appearance of two dimensions but follow all the rules of three dimensional space. They have even bred beasts similar animals and plants of Creation, but that have simplified to varying degrees such as themselves. Some of these are demons as well and may be capable of speech, and the others simple animals or Hellbeasts. Their populations have grown, and many have adopted specific regional dialects from Creation, with Malfean Old Realm being the tongue shared by all. With the languages of Creation they have also adopted the cultures of the languages they have stolen, only emulating varying periods of their history when they stole the language and cultural habits. What is perhaps most notable about their language however is that they speak in written words. When they speak no sound comes out but instead their dialogue emerges as written word, each distinguishable as different handwriting, just as most humans will have their own distinguishable voices. Some appear as bubbles containing their dialogue in sentence form, and others speak and a line of essence points from their mouth to their words above. Some make no mention of this, and others may specifically point out or interact with their solidified speech. Many of their cities have developed into Industrial level technology and make use of advanced crossbow and algarel weapons. Their clothes mimic styles from Creation only modified to fit their frames, so that many from Creation cannot tell the small slip of cloth that they wear as shorts as being different from their shirts which are often the most prominent and visible portion of their garments.<br /> They regarded as fools and madmen to the rest of the Malfeas. However much of their overall population are psychologically indistinguishable from mortals and heroic mortals found in Creation. However \u00bc to 1/3 of their population lacks a motivation completely and often possess arbitrary and often dangerous intimacies. They have been known to throw their lives away on a whim and are profoundly gullible, with some taking things only literally. Some will literally rip their limbs off if asked for a hand, and some may appear normal and even competent even filling roles as hitman or savant until they are paid to kill themselves which they do without hesitation. Many of them are sexually deranged and will find attraction to only the dead or animals, but many more are likely to be unpicky and will copulate with anyone. What most do not realize is that while they appear two dimensional they actually perceive space and time distinctly compared to humans. They see the immediate past and future of a scene along with the present as a different location. As such they may see themselves as they were seconds ago but to the left and or above, while they see the future often to the right and or below the group. Despite this, or maybe because of this, they are regarded as having an inability to think ahead, and their lack of foresight has colored their impressions with the rest of Malfeas and Creation. Due to their communities being divided only by appearance rather than mental condition the sane individuals are indistinguishable from the mad, and they are often tortured just as much as a human population would be by the random acts of sociopathy, madness, and carnage inflicted by their hollow souled brethren. For this reason they are the favored of the Ebon Dragon for he drinks deep from their suffering and for this reason they are known as the Empty Madness.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Summoning</b>: (Obscurity 2/4)<br /> If simple effigies are drawn in a scenario where they interact with the reader it may resonate with a scene that actually happened five days ago in the White Zone in Malfeas and will draw forth these Demons across Cecylene to take the places of the images, however if they do not have the power to shapeshift or reduce their size they will remain as tiny as the images drawn and possess physical attributes at one. Sometimes however when large murals are painted Cia\u2019nydanhephaenae may also be summoned five or more yards high. Sorcerers often summon the more Mad and deranged members of the White Zone to perform suicide missions such as strapping themselves with algarel or fire dust and exploding in a town square, or to murder and sow panic in a village at night. Many savants are curious about the fact that these Demons often refer to Creation as the Real World, and the act of interacting with it or being summoned to it as breaking the 4th Wall. At first this was taken as a simple curiosity but some Savants in the First Age had similar notes about Raksha making these same remarks, and have been quite disturbed to find out that many Raksha seem to speak to the Empty Madness on the same level when discussing the subject. Sometimes when speaking of this outside the White Zone they may attract the attention of The End of All Wisdom, who promptly makes them into one of the stars of Malfeas. This has been one of the most baffling mysteries of all time.<br /> The Empty Madness often aren\u2019t sure how more of them are made, with some believing in random wild theories that Creation tells their children such as babies come from the Stork, or believing that they come from birds having sex with bees. Perhaps the most popular belief is that they reproduce like humans. In truth whenever a female gets splashed with the heart\u2019s blood of one of their kind they will become pregnant sometime within that month. Since violent mass murder is common in the White Zone often times multiple females will get pregnant and produce enough children to more than compensate for the casualties throughout their lives. Rare occasions even males become pregnant. Those who become splashed with the heart\u2019s blood of other demons may develop mutations, and the same with those who are exposed to the Heart\u2019s blood of being from Creation. All of their young conceived while in Creation often bare traits of the areas they were in in Creation, and may instinctively learn those languages. Their young usually gestate and grow into adult hood at roughly the same pace as humans.<br /> <br /> <b>Motivation</b>:<br /> <br /> Motivations may vary and often are comparable to those found in extras and mortals of Creation. Some however are simplistic to the extreme such as \u201cMake a Point.\u201d, or appear completely random and deranged such as \u201cStab an eye while wearing a purple shirt.\u201d And many possess no Motivations at all, and take even their deaths lightly. <b>Virtues</b>:<br /> <br /> Their Virtues may vary just as much as humans in Creation. These are just a sample of common Virtue ratings Compassion 2, Conviction 2 , Temperance 2 , Valor 2<br /> Willpower 4<br /> <b>Attributes</b>:<br /> Strength 2, Dexterity 2 , Stamina 2 ; Charisma 3 , Manipulation 3 , Appearance 1 ; Perception 3, Intelligence 1, Wits 3 (But may vary wildly)<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Abilities</b>:<br /> <br /> Martial Arts 2 (Random Violence 1, Sucker Punch 1)<br /> Melee 1 (Murder 1, Beating the Defenseless 1)<br /> Archery 1 (Crossbows 2, or Flame Weapons 2)<br /> Thrown 1 (Rocks 1, Books 1, Victims 1)<br /> War 1 (Mobs 1)<br /> Integrity 1 (Straight Face 3)<br /> Presence 2 (Jokes 2, Anger 1)<br /> Performance 2 (Jokes 2)<br /> Resistance 1<br /> Survival 1 (White Zone 1)<br /> Medicine 1 (Cancer 1, Pregnancy 1)<br /> Investigation 1<br /> Craft One (Two points to spend anywhere and two appropriate specialties)<br /> Occult 1 (The 4th Wall)<br /> Lore 1 (3 Specialties pertaining to random regions or time periods)<br /> Athletics 1<br /> Awareness 2 (Being Watched 3)<br /> Stealth 1<br /> Dodge 1<br /> Larceny 2 (3 Specialties divided amongst any Specialties. Common ones are Stealing, Forgery, and Gambling.)<br /> Socialize 1 (3 Specialties with their Native Population such as Sirk or Tam)<br /> Ride (White Zone Mount 1, Artifact Vehicle 1)<br /> Sail<br /> Bureaucracy 1<br /> Linguistics 1 (Native Old Realm, one language from a region of creation with a specialty in it)<br /> <b>Backgrounds</b>:<br /> Backing 1, Resources 2, Contacts 3(Other Tribesman), Allies 2 (Other Tribesmen)<br /> <b>Charms</b>:<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>1<sup>st</sup> Excellency and 2<sup>nd</sup> Excellency- Any three Excellencies</b><br /> <b>Materialize-</b> Most of the time when Dematerialized they express their Intangibility through being 2 Dimensional.<br /> <b>Hand of Destiny-</b> these are often wild insane visions of the mad futures they work towards, and is most assuredly not derived from fate, and often works antagonistically with fate forming cruelly humorous irony or coincidence.<br /> <b>Natural Prognostication-</b> Reflects the queer visions of the White Zone instead of fate, and often involves the unique perceptions of Space/Time that the Empty Madness experience.<br /> <b>Sense Domain-</b> Used to actually notice their own Word Speak that other beings naturally notice, as well as to sense irony and coincidence, as well as to sense Cancer and Venereal Disease.<br /> <b>Call-</b> Other of the Demon Tribe<br /> <b>Chrysalis of Preservation-</b> used to Solidify their Speech into tangible form which may then be used as an improvised weapon or raw materials.<br /> <b>Loom Stride-</b> This is related to their perception of Time being related to space and involves them stepping into the immediate future.<br /> <b>Harrow the Mind-</b> Often used on their fellows, who usually do not spend willpower to resist, especially if they have no motivation. They take advantage of their kinds nature of extreme gullibility.<br /> <b>Bread of Weak Spirit</b><br /> <b>Words of Power-</b> The Spirits Words Materialize to Cut or Crush<br /> <br /> <b>Essence</b>: 2<br /> <br /> <br /> Soak 1L/2B<br /> HEALTH: One -0, Two -1, Two -2, One -4, Incapacitated<br /> <br /> Mutations: Many Mutations are common such as Large or Gargantuan, as well as Short. Often these are noticeable in a community. All will possess debilities such as phobias and derangements, and many possess multiple ones to express their insanity.<br /> NOTES: Terrestrial Martial Arts are commonly learned in various dojos in their towns and cities, and even some Celestial Martial Arts made for Spirits such as the 4 Arguments of Virtues Styles, Black Claw, and Hellfire Ballet Style. Due to the White Zone being beyond The End of All Wisdom\u2019s jurisdiction some of the denizens there have developed Sorcery and Necromancy. Due to their population being in the hundreds of thousands in each Major Tribe, if not in the outright tens of millions, there are plenty of anomalies amongst their population as far as abilities, traits, and charms. Most stay at essence 2 however. Some even possess radical artifacts and technology, and thaumaturgy is common for their savants. In lots of ways their societies at least superficially mimic Creations, and often times with strange differences as if they were honestly missing the point of jobs such as teacher, scientist or police.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-22T20:35:17-08:00","id":1269975,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://web.archive.org/web/20160314202822/http://rathess.xi.co.nz:80/exalted/index.php/Characters:Pipaepu_the_Publisher_Imps\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://web.archive.org/web/20160314202822im_/http:/rathess.xi.co.nz/exalted/resources/assets/poweredby_mediawiki_88x31.png\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://web.archive.org/web/20160314202822/http://rathess.xi.co.nz:80/exalted/index.php/Characters:Pipaepu_the_Publisher_Imps\" target=\"_blank\"> Characters:Pipaepu the Publisher Imps - exalted official wiki - mirror from archive.org </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://web.archive.org/web/20160314202822/http://rathess.xi.co.nz:80/exalted/index.php/Characters:Pipaepu_the_Publisher_Imps\" target=\"_blank\"> https://web.archive.org/web/20160314202822/http://rathess.xi.co.nz:80/exalted/index.php/Characters:Pipaepu_the_Publisher_Imps </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div> <br /> <b>Pipaepu, the Publisher Imps.</b><br /><br /> <span style=\"color:#252525\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Pipaepu, the Publisher Imps.</span></span></span><br /> <b>Demons of the First Circle, Progeny of the Discoverer of Horizons</b> Vedderhart once wept tears of languid refulgence in his incapacity to share the wonders of beyond with the rest of Malfeas. So the Discoverer of Horizons beseeched Nesquick, his Automaton Concubine, to collect the tears and percolate them within her Seven Miracle Membrane Layers and spawn the first generation of Publisher Imps to spread the wonders to be found Beyond!<br /> <br /> With bodies similar to Creation born chimpanzees, with fur the shade of azure one finds in the bright mornings in the shallows of the neck, and pale skin the color of salt the Pipaepu are a diminutive species. They possess large dactylic wings formed from mud on bones of sleet that when fully outstretched possess a length in excess of two yards. Their teeth are made of wood and pyrite, with tongues of reddish quicksilver, and eyes made of polished eburnean buttons. They all possess an inborn intimacy towards fancy hats and vests, and the rest may or may not garb themselves in clothing. Most, fearing violent muggings that are commonplace in the Demon City, carry a portable crossbow or Hellpiece in their purse, as well as a backup mace formed from brass.<br /> <br /> Publisher Imps are born with lifetimes of memories, all not theirs, and so they publish biographical stories from these memories, as well as the dreams they have slumbered. Most consider the Publisher Imps habitual liars or at least delusional, but the Imps feel they speak nothing but the truth, at least that is their claims whenever they are interrogated during their intoxicated revels at pubs after finishing a project. They work to have these stories of a thousand lifetimes, in a thousand different worlds produced on dispensable media such as books, and during the First Age in Teleplay format on IAM. Sorcerers have been known to produce great works of fiction through the employ of Publisher Imps, combined with a human or other demon working as editors and developers. And Publisher Imps have constant employ as Playwrites, and professional dreamstone dreamers. Some Sorcerers upon reaching the abrupt end of novel series centuries after the original author have died have learned that it is very likely that a Publisher Imp can be summoned to continue the adventures of their favorite literary characters having dreamed their adventures upon birth or at some point in slumber in their lives. They make excellent storytellers, and many have been summoned to entertain settlements in those long harsh winters in the North.<br /> <br /> Many have learned languages that have never been spoken upon the shores of Malfeas or under the Sun\u2019s light in Creation. And through their memories the Pipaepu have learned languages that are virtually extinct, such as Rocktongue, Earthtongue, and Pelagial. They have even learned alien languages such as Autochthonian and the Stych of the Shadetailed Menders. They have been sought out for their Primers published and enhanced with charms to teach and spread fluency in these languages. Some alien/extinct languages have been used or taught for secrecies sake. Pipaepu have a desire to work on their Magnum Opus at the end of their lives, and will seek hermitage to set this great work to writing. Once they complete their project they consume it before anyone has a chance to read it, including themselves, after which they slumber under a pile of stones. The beings that awaken from this pile of stones are a single young male, and a single young female Publisher Imp. It is said the Final works of a Publisher Imp contain great secrets of the Universe and any who reads one before the Imp consumes it would attract the attention of Orabilis and be starbound.<br /> <br /> <b>Summoning</b>: (Obscurity 2/4)<br /> <br /> <br /> Sometimes a mortal author will die by candlelight before they have completed penning their last work. Sometimes before the last flicker of the candle goes out a Publisher Imp will place a new candle made of Bloodape fat, and finish scribing the great work for distribution in Creation. Publisher Imps will gain Limit once per day if forced to change the facts in their story. They will also gain limit once per day if forced to dispose of the arms in their purse. Every 25 hour period of not writing or telling a story from their Dreams to an audience will cause a Pipaepu to roll their Conviction and each success becomes a limit point.<br /> <br /> <b>Motivation</b>: To spread the tales from their dreams through pen and word.<br /> <b>Virtues</b>:<br /> Compassion 2 , Conviction 4 , Temperance 2 , Valor 1 Willpower 6<br /> <b>Attributes</b>: Strength 2 , Dexterity 4 , Stamina 3 ; Charisma 3 , Manipulation 3 , Appearance 2 ; Perception 3, Intelligence 3, Wits 3<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Abilities</b>:<br /> <br /> Martial Arts 2 (Strike at the Eyes 2, Below the Belt 1)<br /> Melee 1 (Mace 3)<br /> Archery 3 (Crossbow 3, or Algarel 3)<br /> Thrown 1 (Scrolls and Books 3)<br /> War 1 (3 points of Specialty divide amongst any terrain)<br /> Integrity 2 (Journalistic Integrity 3)<br /> Presence 2 (Jokes 3)<br /> Performance 2 (Storytelling 5)<br /> Resistance 3 (Working by Candlelight 3)<br /> Survival 1 (Nests 3)<br /> Medicine 1<br /> Investigation 1 (Interviews 3)<br /> Craft Water 1 (Recipes 3), Earth 1 (Alien Architecture 2) , Wood , Air 2 (Calligraphy 3)<br /> Occult 4 (Raksha 1, Underworld 1, Zen Mu 1)<br /> Lore 4 (Alternate Histories 3)<br /> Athletics 2 (Flying 3)<br /> Awareness 2 (Birds eye view 3)<br /> Stealth 3 (In Groups 3)<br /> Dodge 3 (While holding writing 3)<br /> Larceny 1 (stealing 2)<br /> Socialize 3 (Other Writers 3)<br /> Ride 1<br /> Sail 1<br /> Bureaucracy 1 (Publishing 3)<br /> Linguistics 6 (Native Old Realm, 6 other languages often they are Languages unknown to Creation, 10 points of Specialties divided into 10 different dialects)<br /> <br /> <b>Backgrounds</b>: Backing 1, Resources 2, Contacts 3 (Demon Publisher Companies), Allies 3 (Other Publisher Imps).<br /> <br /> <b>Charms</b>:<br /> <br /> 1st Excellency Archery, Performance, Craft<br /> 2nd Excellency Occult, Lore<br /> Materialize<br /> Benefaction- May give a one die bonus to those who just read a primer, instruction manual, or cookbook they penned, or just listened to an hour of storytelling.<br /> Endowment- May use Endowment as a training effect to teach a language to those who read their Primers. Publisher Imps use this to expand their population of potential readers.<br /> Dreamscape- Publisher Imps often enter the dreams of mortals and demons to spread the tales from beyond hoping they will inspire their writings when they awaken.<br /> Impromptu Messenger- Publisher Imps may speak out of the mouths of any slumbering creature.<br /> Calculated Order of Immediate Action- Publisher Imps may create copies of works they have already written, or Tales they have told.<br /> Form Reduction Technique- Imps often reduce themselves to the size of an apple to sneak copies of their scrolls to distinguished playwrites and journalists, or to sneak into the rooms of dreamers.<br /> Landscape Travel- Double Flight Speed<br /> Subtle Whispers- Often used to convince Mortal and Demon Publishers to accept deals.<br /> Animating Management- Publisher Imps often possess pens to write on their own.<br /> Wine of Infinite Heartbreak- used on their audience for continued storytelling.<br /> Spice of Custodial Delectation- Writing their Tales.<br /> NOTES: Some Publisher Imps have learned Sorcery through their memories and the Salinian Workings, these are rare and often race to complete their Magnum Opus before Orabilis handles them. However this same line of reasoning may mean that a very rare few have learned of Necromancy rather than Sorcery, and thus spread their tales through the Labyrinth. These Imps have Whispers as well.<br /> <br /> <b>Essence</b>: 3<br /> <br /> <br /> Soak: 3B/1L<br /> <br /> <br /> Note: This is a comment by the Author in response to their fixations on hats and vests. [quote=Eldagusto]<br /> Yeah I wanted the desire for hats and vests to reflect some inborn nature of civility for them. Since they would wear vests in place of other clothes they would make sure they are good attractive vests that display their individuality. Same with the hats, since they are a culture that flies over things they view having to look down upon each other they see a hat first, so they want the hat to make a good first impression. I guess it came off as silly though. I got idea from often seeing Imps and wee folk wearing colorful clothes, like little Djinn wearing those Aladdin pants and pointed shoes. The purse thing was after hearing about heterosexual men sometimes wearing purses, so this would be a unisex thing for the Imps. And it would also be important since they value possessions like writing implements, weapons that make them feel safe. Ultimately the accessories and clothes were to show the Imps individuality and professionalism compared to some species that just go commando.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-22T20:35:54-08:00","id":1269976,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://web.archive.org/web/20160315091423/http://rathess.xi.co.nz:80/exalted/index.php/Characters:Cik_the_Frantic_Chefs_of_the_Fallen\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://web.archive.org/web/20160315091423im_/http:/rathess.xi.co.nz/exalted/resources/assets/poweredby_mediawiki_88x31.png\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://web.archive.org/web/20160315091423/http://rathess.xi.co.nz:80/exalted/index.php/Characters:Cik_the_Frantic_Chefs_of_the_Fallen\" target=\"_blank\"> Characters:Cik the Frantic Chefs of the Fallen - exalted official wiki - mirror from archive.org </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://web.archive.org/web/20160315091423/http://rathess.xi.co.nz:80/exalted/index.php/Characters:Cik_the_Frantic_Chefs_of_the_Fallen\" target=\"_blank\"> https://web.archive.org/web/20160315091423/http://rathess.xi.co.nz:80/exalted/index.php/Characters:Cik_the_Frantic_Chefs_of_the_Fallen </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div> <br /> <b>Cik, the Frantic Chefs of the Fallen.</b><br /><br /> <span style=\"color:#252525\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Cik, the Frantic Chefs of the Fallen.</span></span></span><br /> <b>Demons of the First Circle, Progeny of the Horned Oak</b> War is the pastime of the Demon City, and afterwards the landscape is littered with the carnage of the fallen. Many are the demons who have no desire to let the corpses go to the Demon Winds, and hunger for their fallen brethren to satisfy and affirm their own merciful continued existence. Deblodiah the Horned Oak is taken aback by notion that the Demon Winds absconding with any of the resources of the Horned Oak\u2019s Dominion, so the Horned Oak\u2019s sulfurous seeds were planted and the Frantic Chefs of the Fallen were set force to prepare feasts of the fallen so that the survivors may no longer envy the dead and reap succulent repast from their remains! Their popularity in their home dominion resulted in them being smuggled and planted en mass throughout the Demon City by covetous lords.<br /> <br /> The Cik have sharp angular features, and beet colored skin. They have thin limbs with flesh stretched taut against oddly jointed arms and legs. Their noses are like caricatures of the longest of human noses, taking up over half of their heads. They have pronounced hunches from constantly bending over to prepare their meals. They have four fingered hands, with each finger sharp like scalpels, to aid in cutting the meat from the bone, but possessing no nails the edge originates from the finger bones\u2019 edges emerging from the skin. Their bandy legs end in feet thinner than any birds; they appear as though they are standing up flexible pitchforks. Their cuspate boned ears take up most of the remainder of their head, with beady little eyes with the square pupils of a goat but with unnatural coloring unique to each Cik. Their miniscule mouths are filled with three rows of black aciculate teeth, and they have a prominent overbite due to having a diminutive jaw. They possess a black forked tongue, with keen taste buds, that flicker to taste the dead to make sure they are properly deceased enough to be superb ingredients. Their ten jointed tails are skinless, appearing only as spiny brass vertebrae and copper cartilage, ending in a stone arrow shaped tip. They are less than a man in length, and their tails are one and one half the length of the rest of the body. Their only clothes are usually leather aprons they are awarded as gifts of appreciation, or as uniforms of employment.<br /> <br /> Like carrion birds after massacre, the Frantic Chefs descend upon the plains of the dead in hordes, each singing in tune with their brethren as they cut and slice the dead and prepare flames for roasting and platters for display. Their youngest work to disperse the spices and prepare the serving mats, but the rest ceaselessly toils to make each feast grand. As soon as they ready one meal, the gathering assemblies of locals agree to first come first serve as law, they move to the next. They derive nourishment from the hunger of their guests, just as much as the fullness of the glutted.<br /> <br /> Cik spawn after their own deaths, which are served just like any other corpse. The entity that devours the largest portion of a Cik\u2019s tail incubates their young in their bellies, and eventually the tail grows into a beanstalk of copper and hair which usually kills the host demon/life form. The pods which grow upon the stalk are withered and within ten days of the tail being eaten the pods hatch. Normally two pods are the default for the stalk, but if the host died within the essence rich boundaries of a manse, or a pool of Vitriol, then five pods may form.<br /> Cik gain limit everyday they cannot prepare a meal from the dead. They also receive one limit each scene they witness a demon being processed into chalcanth. They instinctually hate the chalcanth trade due to it removing corpses from which they may prepare a meal. If there is one thing the Frantic Chefs hate more than chalcanth, it is their own deep satisfaction upon imbibing chalcanth. Upon drinking Chalcanth the Frantic Chefs regain 5 Willpower, even raising it past their maximums, but at the end of the scene they also receive five limit points. Sorcerers often summon the Cik to serve as recyclers after their illness has struck a whole herd of cattle dead, as they are able to sanitize the dead as part of their preparation process. Some less scrupulous first Age sorcerers would be known to summon the Cik after famine wiped out half their kingdoms population, or after a massacre of their enemies.<br /> An interesting discovery made by the Cik is that upon seeing a ghost they have a distinct urge to shred and prepare them for consumption. Cik have actually formed raiding parties into the Underworld via shadowlands, in order to make their denizens into meals either for the locals of the shadowlands or for accompanying bands of ravenous demons. This tradition has formed into an organization all its own with members from numerous demon races, including a sizeable Blood Ape and population to devour during the raids, Firmin to skewer the meals for transport, and Jaemi to transport the rest to markets for sale. They are known as the Bones into Bread Tradition.<br /> <br /> <b>Summoning</b>: (Obscurity 1/4)<br /> <br /> If members of a group die from starvation while others still live hungry and no carrion eating birds reach them, upon the first time a moonbeam shines upon the corpses then a Frantic Chef of the Fallen may walk upon the moon beam to prepare the corpse into a sumptuous feast for the living.<br /> <b>Motivation</b>: To feed the hunger of the living with the prepared meat of the dead.<br /> <b>Virtues</b>: Compassion 3, Conviction 4, Temperance 2, Valor 3<br /> Willpower 8<br /> <b>Attributes</b>:<br /> <br /> Strength 3 , Dexterity 5 , Stamina 4 ; Charisma 3 , Manipulation 2 , Appearance 2 ; Perception 3, Intelligence 2, Wits 3<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Abilities</b>: Martial Arts 3 (Claws 3) Melee 1 (Cutlery 3) Archery Thrown 1 (Cutlery 3) War 1 (Leading the Hungry 3) Integrity 2 (Chalcanth resistance 1, Chalcanth addiction 1) Presence 3 (Yelling in a crowd 3) Performance 2 (Singing 3) Resistance 3 (Work till job is done 3) Survival 3 (Foraging Dead 3) Medicine 1 (Dead 3) Investigation 1 (Find Dead 3) Craft Water 4 (Meat 3), Earth 1 (pits 1, eateries 2) , Wood , Air 1 (Folding 2) , Magitech , Fire 1(Cutlery 1, Dinner equipment 2) Occult 1 (Ghosts 1, Shadowlands 1, Demon City 1) Lore 1 (Recipes1, Geography 2) Athletics 2 (Climbing 3) Awareness 2 (Dead 3) Stealth 3 (Amongst the Fallen 3) Dodge 3 (While work is needed 3) Larceny 1 (Sleight of Hand 3) Socialize 3 (The Hungry 3) Ride 1 Sail 1 Bureaucracy 1 (Food 3) Linguistics 2 (Native Old Realm, Two other languages)<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Backgrounds</b>:<br /> Backing 1, Resources 1, Contacts 3 (Hungry Demons, Members of a Demon Army, Demon Market), Allies 3 (They make plenty of friends amongst the denizens of Hell). <br /> <b>Charms</b>:<br /> <br /> 1st Excellency Martial Arts, Craft,<br /> Materialize<br /> Sense Domain- may sense the fallen ready for cooking.<br /> Call- They ring a brass triangle and scream \u201cSoup on you\u201d in a dialect from before the Primordial War summoning the Hungry Demons of Malfeas.<br /> Landscape Travel- Double Speed on the Fields of the Fallens<br /> Bane Weapon- The Dead feel their cuts deeply<br /> Spice of Custodial Delectation- Preparing the dead for eating<br /> Benefaction- Cast upon each dish, all who eat gain a die to battle rolls<br /> Calculated Order of Immediate Action- creates an array of disposable silverware, plates, cups, and napkins for the feast.<br /> Host of Spirits- They split into a host of chefs to prepare the dining array, and help with cooking, and serving.<br /> Stoke the Flame- is used to command everyone to eat the feast!<br /> Fruit of Living Essence- may imbue the dishes with lingering essence of the flesh; dividing motes equal to the fallen\u2019s essence + willpower amongst those who consume it. It also makes the meal nourishing and nonlethal to consume.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Essence</b>: 3<br /> <br /> <br /> Soak: 6B/4L Kiss the Cook Appron 2B/2L<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-22T20:36:42-08:00","id":1269977,"title":"","content":"<b><span style=\"font-family:Linux Libertine, Georgia, Times, serif\">https://web.archive.org/web/20160314193247/http://rathess.xi.co.nz:80/exalted/index.php/Characters:Havatie_the_Drums_of_Fear</span></b><br /><br /> <b>Havatie the Drums of Fear.</b><br /><br /> <span style=\"color:#252525\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Havatie, the Drums of Fear.</span></span></span><br /> <b>Demons of the First Circle, Progeny of the Obstinate Malikah of the Gilded Frown</b> Havatie, the Drums of Fear, progeny of the Obstinate Malikah of the Gilded Frown<br /> Born from the seeds Vriggan spit into the stool of Melon Scourge, the Drums of Fear are grown on thick yellow green stalks. They ripen on the vine as melon colored eggs which crack after precisely three seasons of growth. By the time they hatch the eggs are the size of a Cherak Clydesdale, and they have been drained of their color. From their melon shells emerge horned beetles the size of a large horse which march forth hungry for raucous. They may appear as gigantic versions of any number of horned beetles, each with a lustrous carapace with wither stripes or spots of rich verde and ebony. After another season their first carapace molts off and they often grow into the size of a bull rhino, but with thick growths on either side. Their backs form grooves befitting of a natural saddle, and just above their side growths appear a fourth set of limbs. These limbs harshly strike the growths in rhythm with their marching.<br /> <br /> The Havatie often gather in herds as large as they can manage. Their drumming has unnatural echoing qualities around Brass, often causing the bones of Malfeas to hum and whole buildings to vibrate. When they are in herds, or alone they have an instinct to drum while marching into populated areas, either crowded hamlets of Malfeas and Creation, or confronting rival herds of Rhino and Zebra in creation. Their drumming stirs fear in those who hear, unless they also are riding a Havati themselves, or are also playing an instrument. The effects are amplified when surrounded by other forms of mobile life such as when in cities, or around densely populated ecosystems. The Havatie feed off of the fear and panic, respiring essence from it, and if they vacate an area completely they may stay for a time to nibble off of the grass and the dirt. During these times the Havatie will rut and form into threes. When they form into threes during these times they will first challenge each other with drum beats. These challenges are acoustic versions of the popular Shogunate game Earth, Wood, Fire, with the player choosing Earth losing to the player choosing Wood, but winning if the other player chooses Fire. After a series of rounds the losing Havatie will burrow into the ground and the two winners will copulate fiercely, to the point of cracking their shells and bleeding ichor upon the ground. Eventually the herd continues its endless migration, and three seasons later stalks with melon eggs (one for each Essence Dot of the buried parent) containing the next generation of the Drums of Fear will grow from the spot of the gravewomb and form into one or more herds themselves. Vriggan grows vast herds of the Drums of Fear in her Ranch of the Horned, and she delights in spreading their herds whenever she camps for the night with Melon Scourge.<br /> <br /> The Drums of Fear are popular mounts cattle in Malfeas. Since they double as transportation/beasts of burden as well as noisemakers to repel the Silent Wind they find easy employment in the legions and communities of Malfeas, and can be found in locals such as the Silver Forest, the Shores of Kimbery, and even within the carnivorous Swamps and Sargassos of Metagos. Havatie who have obtained employment have a habit of collecting any sort of jewelry, accessories, or baubles to hang around their drums and saddles, the gaudier the better. A popular drink sold throughout Malfeas comes from the bloodmilk of the Havatie, which naturally cools as it ferments and is sold as melon smoothies in stands and taverns of the Demon City. Each cup this drink works as a dose of hard liquor but with the side effect of negating a meals worth of nutrition, but does nothing to effect hydration. This was popular in High First Age as an option over the vomitoriums, where wealthy patrons would drink this cool spirit to make room in their stomach for more feasting. As famine became more common in Creation after the Usurpation most civilizations have forgotten this rare import, however some indulgent outcastes in the Far South still partake of this treat during feast days. Some degenerate Dynasts have discovered this drink and have a laugh when they offer it to starving thirsty peasant children only to see their joyous faces turn to horror and then fears as they starve at the Dynasts feet. More than one slave has sold his own freedom just for a loaf of bread after being offered one of these spirits, just so they wouldn\u2019t painfully starve to death on the spot. Canny Guildsmen have taken to using thaumaturgy to harvest this milk for use as a dietary supplement for overweight city folk.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Summoning</b>: (Obscurity 2/3, In the Southwest and North it is 1/3)<br /> <br /> If an entire herd is driven to stampede off a cliff to their doom, three stalks from Malfeas may grow backwards in the ground and emerge from the slaughter and bones of the herd in Creation. This has enforced the taboo of making sure a hunters do not drive entire herds off of cliff, and when they do they are encouraged to harvest all of the herd, bones meat and skins, or else they will be plagued by the Drums of Fear, which will naturally cause more herds to stampede off of cliffs and eventually desolate whole plains. This taboo is common amongst both the Southeastern plains and the North. Sorcerers will often summon the Drums of Fear to route other armies, or as terrible mounts they ride through conquered lands as they sack and pillage. Some with an eye for market summon the Havatie for their delicious Melon Spirits.<br /> <br /> <b>Motivation</b>: To drum up fear, and profit from the panic. <b>Virtues</b>:<br /> <br /> Compassion 2 , Conviction 2 , Temperance 1 , Valor 4<br /> Willpower 5<br /> <b>Attributes</b>:<br /> <br /> Strength 7, Dexterity 2 , Stamina 5 ; Charisma 3 , Manipulation 2 , Appearance 3 ; Perception 2, Intelligence 1, Wits 2<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Abilities</b>:<br /> <br /> <br /> Martial Arts 3 (Stampede 3) Melee Archery Thrown 1 (Spitting 2) War 1 (Routing 3) Integrity 1 Presence 2 (Intimidation 3) Performance 2 (Drumming 3) Resistance 3 (Marching 1) Survival 2 (After Drum Panic 2) Medicine Investigation Craft Air 1 (Baubles 1)<br /> Occult 1 (Scary Stories 1)<br /> Lore Athletics 2 (Stampeding 3) Awareness 2 (Prey 3) Stealth Dodge 1 (Stampede 3) Larceny 1 (Baubles 2) Socialize 1 (Herd 2, Other Mounts 1) Ride Sail Bureaucracy Linguistics (Native Old Realm)<br /> <b>Backgrounds</b>: Backing 1<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Charms</b>:<br /> <br /> <b>First Excellency: Presence, Performance, Athletics</b><br /> <br /> Materialize<br /> <br /> Principle of Motion<br /> <b>(Typically 5 saved actions)</b><br /> <b>Sense Domain</b> (They typically sense any sort of group panic whether a riot or stampede)<br /> <b>Call</b> (Other Drums of Fear)<br /> <b>Impromptu Messenger</b> (Any sleeping mortal who hears their drumming whispers ominously that \u201cThey\u201d are coming, this drumming can be heard for a mile for each dot of Essence a Havati possesses.)<br /> <b>Divine Decree</b> (Used to cause lesser Demons to panic, riot and stampede)<br /> <b>Weather Control</b> (They may cause clouds to gather at stampedes and roar with Thunder most deafening)<br /> <b>Paper Tiger Arrangement</b> (Used to create an illusion of other Drums of Fear to bolster their numbers, and images of already stampeding and panicked local fauna)<br /> <b>Landscape Travel</b> (Double Speed when stampeding or within a stampede)<br /> <b>Harrow the Mind</b> (When hearing their drumming others feel the End is near)<br /> <b>Stoke the Flames</b> (Fear and Panic are induced with the drumming cacophony)<br /> <b>Spice of Custodial Delectation</b> (When causing a stampede or Riot)<br /> <b>Meat of Broken Flesh</b> (Supplements trampling victims)<br /> <b>Ox Body Technique</b> x1<br /> <b>Shatter</b> (Their cacophony shatters windows, doors, and dwellings)<br /> <b>Words of Power</b> (Their Drumming can harm their victims)<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Essence</b>: 3<br /> <br /> <br /> Soak 6L/9B Lacquered Carapace 4L/4B<br /> HEALTH: Two-0, Four -1, Three -2, -4, Incapacitated<br /> Mutation: Large (Health and stats already included in write-up ) Horns Affliction, Armored Hide Blight<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-22T20:37:30-08:00","id":1269979,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://web.archive.org/web/20160314192635/http://rathess.xi.co.nz:80/exalted/index.php/Characters:Bromwheelers_the_Catapult_Turtles\" target=\"_blank\">https://web.archive.org/web/20160314...tapult_Turtles</a><br /> <br /> <b>Bromwheelers, the Catapult Turtles.</b><br /><br /> <span style=\"color:#252525\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Demons of the First Circle, Progeny of the Prolific Engineer of the Transmundane.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252525\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">These massive creations of the Prolific Engineer of the Transmundane are often mistaken for Behemoths by those who first encounter them. They resemble stout turtles of cyclopean stature. They possess shells the size of large wagons and each possesses a siege weapon upon or within its shell. The Prolific Engineer of the Transmundane hammers their shells and skeletons from the vitriol-fused bones of the fallen demons that litter the Demon City\u2019s rubble, along with an undershelling of brass-bamboo varnishing. Due to their dense structure and their pressurized fluid-filled organs, Bromwheelers each weigh well over 5 tons and several of them have the large mutation or a greater variant of it. Their necks are wrinkled to accommodate expansion, and their heads are like a combination of snake and turtle heads with ears resembling those of a coyote. Their eyes are hemispheres of silver liquid hovering within their deep eye sockets. Their clawed feet seem to possess the qualities of a strong magnet and can tightly grip metals for bracing. Their scales appear as citrine colored brass, their underbellies are shine like haematite, and the tops of their shells are grooved with obsidian and plated with stone. The type of stone varies from Bromwheeler to Bromwheeler, with some having shells covered with polished marble and others having shells covered with lapis lazuli mixed with grey slate.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252525\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><br /> Catapult Turtles are perhaps the most successful export from the territories of the Prolific Engineer of the Transmundane. They first spread throughout the Demon City as living siege engines that Warlords such as the Living Tower bartered ample resources for in order to sample populations to breed in their domains. Due to their success rival Warlords throughout the layers of Hell rustled and looted enough of the Catapult Turtles that after the Bromwheelers had been on the Markets for 108 years their progenitor no longer had a monopoly on them. Mother Vines and Neomah were all that was needed to bolster their swelling numbers. Recently their inventor Geezeirbo received the blessing of the Trout that Swims Through Time as the Unquestionable reanimated the bones of the first and largest Catapult Turtle, the gargantuan Proterrapin. With his living siege fortress operational for the first time since the Low First Age Geezeirbo has taken to bolstering the numbers of the Catapult Turtles beyond all precedent, in preparation for what he says is a turning of the ages that will put the Usurpation to shame.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252525\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><br /> A Catapult Turtle may fire or launch anything it can lift at least 500 yards out of its shellborne apparatus, and some can manage a distance of miles with proper calculation. They still have the same limitations on firing as a normal siege engine, although they normally have about 45 degrees of tilt without having to move their entire forms. They have excellent aim, and enjoy hurling as a pastime when alone. When in groups they can be playfully competitive. Their tendency to fire without foresight is a significant problem for their masters, as Sorcerers need make sure that they summon Bromwheelers only into regions that they don\u2019t mind having demolished the moment they leave the Catapult Turtles to themselves. Every period between the sun setting or rising in which a Catapult Turtle doesn\u2019t get to use its siege engine forces the Bromwheeler's summoner to roll a die and to add the results plus one to their limit. When left to their own devices within the confines of the Demon City Catapult Turtles naturally attempt to socialize with each other by seeing who can project something closest to Ligier. This game involves hurling ammo or stray demons sunwards, and those who have their shots blasted out of the sky by the Green Sun or some other mighty being are treated as champions among their communities. However most come short usually resulting in a great deal of property damage throughout the surrounding area as boulders, shrapnel, and pedestrians rain down upon the wretched populace of Hell\u2019s City.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252525\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><br /> Catapult Turtles have a second limiting factor and that is their prodigious capacity for consumption. Catapult Turtles require their weight in meat or vegetation (Brass Bamboo works just as well as bark from an oak) as well as at least one ton of any liquid (hydraulics are an essential part of their musculature every day to support their siege engine metabolism, and they will gain 1 point of limit each day if not sufficiently fed. They will also loose the use of their siege weapons until nourished. Curiously, the pungent liquids that Bromwheelers disgorge through their mouths are perhaps the closest thing to potable water a human is likely to find in the sprawls of the Demon City. Some mortals in Malfeas have learned to convince Catapult Turtles to spit into basins, thereby filling the basins in question with water that can be boiled into potability.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252525\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><br /> <b>Summoning</b>:</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252525\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><br /> (Obscurity 2/2)</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252525\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">A favorite amongst Sorcerers in need of a quick and mobile siege engine that can produce its own ammo, the Catapult Turtles saw great use during any times of war when damage to ones surroundings is a desirable outcome. If a fire burns a units only siege weapon and they attempt to douse it with the last of their water supply, a Catapult Turtle may sense it is needed and stagger into creation as a replacement. A convenient form of travel for flying demons, as well as the sturdier denizens (or those with advanced crashpods), of Hell is to have a Catapult Turtle launch one\u2019s self a mile towards where they want to go and glide safely to their destination. Though this method is rarely used by Creation in the Age of Sorrow during the High First Age they made excellent shuttle points for small sky vessels or sturdy Exalts. The Daimyo of the Shogunate adapted the use of Catapult Turtles as a method for launching Warstrider ambushes from above after a mysterious Earth Aspect nomad by the name of Asphalt Mantis claimed to witness the maneuver used by an elite Hellstrider unit during his travels in the Demon City.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252525\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><br /> They also make excellent beasts of burden to haul or pull cargo, as well as slow but unstoppable mounts, as long as one can ensure they do not launch their cargo or rider. Filling them with the proper broths and cooking them alive makes for an expensive classic Demon City recipe called Hardshell Soup, and it a delight to gourmands everywhere from Heaven, Hell, and the Bordermarches in between.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252525\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><br /> If two or more Catapult Turtles quarrel, then the victor will crack open the shells of the defeated and vomit a clutch of leather eggs the size of small boulders into the shell cavity of the fallen. After a season, during which the Bromwheeler will guard its clutch, the eggs will hatch resulting in a number of young equal to the essence rating of the incubating corpse. These young will gorge themselves upon the scraps of their incubator\u2019s shell and will usually quickly swell at least to the size of a hippo before they start to develop their own siege weapons. Due to many areas not having a dense population of Catapult Turtles it is common for a festival to occur every four years so that interested parties may bring their Bromwheelers together at a designated fair grounds to have their Catapult Turtles duel it out with the winner getting the rights to the new clutch of eggs. Some however choose to increase their numbers by arranging for the Neomah\u2019s Sword Dance Ritual, or distilling their Catapult Turtle into Chalcanth and feeding it to a Mother Vine.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252525\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>Motivation</b>:</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252525\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">To hurl to its heart's content. Bromwheelers often have intimacies towards competition (Pride), and eating (Joy)</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252525\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><br /> <b>Virtues</b>:</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252525\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Compassion 2, Conviction 3 , Temperance 1 , Valor 3</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252525\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Willpower 6</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252525\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><br /> <b>Attributes</b>:</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252525\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Strength 10, Dexterity 1 , Stamina 7 ; Charisma 3 , Manipulation 1 , Appearance 3 ; Perception 5, Intelligence 1, Wits 1</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252525\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><br /> <b>Abilities</b>:</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252525\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Martial Arts 1 (Biting 2)</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252525\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Archery 7 (Taking Aim Actions 3)</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252525\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Thrown 7 (Taking Aim Actions 3)</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252525\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">War 1 (Routing 2)</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252525\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Integrity 3</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252525\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Presence 1</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252525\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Performance 1 (Singing 1, Dancing 1, Sex 1)</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252525\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Resistance 5 (While Encumbered 3)</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252525\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Survival 2 (Foraging 3)</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252525\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Craft Water 1 (Spit Soup 1), Wood 1 (Carvings 1)</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252525\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Occult 1 (Demon Sky 3)</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252525\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Lore 1 (Calculating Trajectories 5)</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252525\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Athletics 3 (Lifting 10)</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252525\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Awareness 2 (Sight 2, Vibrations 1)</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252525\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Stealth 1 (In Liquid 3)</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252525\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Dodge 0 (Too Heavy to Dodge)</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252525\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Socialize 1 (Other Turtle Demons 3)</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252525\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Sail 1 (Sky Vessels 2)</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252525\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Linguistics 0 (Native Old Realm)</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252525\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><br /> <b>Backgrounds</b></span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252525\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Backing 1</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252525\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><br /> <b>Charms</b>:</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252525\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">First Excellency: Resistance and Athletics</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252525\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Second Excellency: Archery and/or Thrown (Bromwheelers have an Excellency for each Ability that is used for one of their siege weapons.)</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252525\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Abstract Body Crystallization: The Catapult Turtles are dense and naturally solid.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252525\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Sense Domain: Bromwheelers have an instinctual awareness of where their projectiles land. This allows for perfectly aimed repeat fire to the same location. It also allows Catapult Turtles to sense areas by firing towards them.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252525\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Landscape Travel: Allows for movement even when fully encumbered with maximum weight.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252525\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Ox-Body Technique: x3 (They tend to purchase as many as their essence can support)</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252525\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Calculated Order of Immediate Action: This charm may be used to create ammunition or Algarel for the Bromwheelers' siege weaponry.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252525\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><br /> <b>Essence</b>:</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252525\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">3</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252525\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><br /> Mutations: Many develop Large+ (the Legendary Proterrapin had the Gargantuan Abomination), Hide, +</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252525\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Fangs (which actually become a sharp serrated beak)</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252525\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">and Claws. Some bloodlines are born with Massive Horns and thick spinal columns, and this is reflected by allowing them to use a natural battering ram, as found in Scroll of Kings. Mutations that adapt them to Kimbery, or the Underwater are very common. They also possess the Natural Missile mutation that represents their high pressure spitballs. Though each spit removes usually 300-500 pounds of their bodily hydration, causing them to drink more.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252525\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Soak 10L/14B (Carapace of Brass and Stone 7L/7B (This is without adding layers of the armored hide Mutation))</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252525\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">HEALTH: One -0, Seven -1, Six -2, One -4, Incapacitated</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252525\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Bite: Martial Arts + 1 Accuracy, Strength + 3 Damage (This is without Fang Mutations)</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252525\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Spit: Dexterity + Thrown Accuracy, Strength Damage, Range 10</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252525\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Notes: Each Bromwheeler is grows its own unique array of Siege Weaponry. Normally they choose either a Light Ballistae, Sailcutter, Siege Sling, a Light Onager, Trebuchet, Light Steam Cannon, a Light Flame Cannon (actually it uses Algarel), Fire Projecter (uses Algarel), or a Light Eruptor. If they have the mutation they may instead choose one heavy version of the Steam Cannon, Onager,Eruptor, Flame Cannon or Ballistae or two Ballistaes or Cannons. With another Size Increase they may have Gigantic Steam Cannons, Flame Cannons or Erruptors. Some are born with a Battering Ram Skull and Horns, the size depending on the size of the Catapult Turtle.</span></span></span><br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-22T20:38:08-08:00","id":1269980,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://web.archive.org/web/20160314203431/http://rathess.xi.co.nz:80/exalted/index.php/Characters:Ebidreul_the_Sky_Drumming_Imps\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://web.archive.org/web/20160314203431im_/http:/rathess.xi.co.nz/exalted/resources/assets/poweredby_mediawiki_88x31.png\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://web.archive.org/web/20160314203431/http://rathess.xi.co.nz:80/exalted/index.php/Characters:Ebidreul_the_Sky_Drumming_Imps\" target=\"_blank\"> Characters:Ebidreul the Sky Drumming Imps - exalted official wiki - mirror from archive.org </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://web.archive.org/web/20160314203431/http://rathess.xi.co.nz:80/exalted/index.php/Characters:Ebidreul_the_Sky_Drumming_Imps\" target=\"_blank\"> https://web.archive.org/web/20160314203431/http://rathess.xi.co.nz:80/exalted/index.php/Characters:Ebidreul_the_Sky_Drumming_Imps </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <b>Ebidreul the Sky Drumming Imps.</b><br /><br /> <span style=\"color:#252525\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Ebidreul the Sky Drumming Imps.</span></span></span><br /> <b>Demons of the First Circle, Progeny of the Effulgent Conductor</b> Born from the phosphorescent blood of the Effulgent Conductor which pelts the ground during his frantic works zipping across the Demon City, the Sky Drumming Imps emerge from cracks in the streets of the Demon City ready to make their music but without a drum to play. The first thing a Sky Drumming Imp does is find something sharp to slowly flay the coarse pale skin from their newborn hides. When they are finished removing their skin in one clean piece they work it into leather with which they fashion into an elegant drum. These drums are their source of pride and their method of survival. They play these skin drums with a pair of brass pummel sticks which they wrap the tips of with the remaining bits of their drum leather.<br /> <br /> The Sky Drumming Imps appear as short ugly goblin like creatures with bandy legs. Many of them are potbellied and flabby though some are emaciated with taut muscles. After they removed their birth skins their hides are slick and with tones ranging from pink to brown and grey. They have large wide set eyes with two simple nostrils between their eye sockets. Their eyes appear as shiny translucent orbs filled with deep scarlet blood. Their heights range from the smallest being barely over two feet with their tallest members a head shorter than a grown man. Their massive ears are often heavily pierced for decorations to indicate employment or affiliations with different bands.<br /> <br /> <br /> The Ebidreul have poor eyesight and don\u2019t distinguish colors. Most only recognize movement; instead they rely off of their excellent hearing with their heavy drumbeats providing something similar to echolocation when received by their massive ears. The bombastic music which they constantly drum has a unique resonance with the clouds in the sky and their drumbeats tug down a nimbus like a hungry fisherman catching a carp. A single Ebidreul can form a simple fog over the ground enough to obscure the inside of a barn or an entity as large as a yeddim, with two or more they can drum enough clouds to cover an entire farm. The clouds they summon have a unique echoing quality which not only enhances the Ebidreul\u2019s senses but also reflect and refract Anima\u2019s and other strong lights. The Ebidreul use this field of blindness to take advantage of their foes which they frantically beat with their pummel stick, and a band of Ebidreul can drum themselves into a frenzy clubbing their confused foes as they caper between each other, and then feeding upon their fallen forms eating their fill and lapping their blood and fluids from the dirt.<br /> <br /> <b>Summoning</b>:<br /> (Obscurity 2/2, with a rating of 1/2 in the South)<br /> Some sorcerers choose to summon the Sky Drumming Imps due to their fondness for their passionate, loud music, and in the Demon City they are always appreciative of loud musicians to drive the Silent Wind away. Other summoners choose to release the Demons upon their foes to route and confuse them with their blinding fogs and deafening beats, leaving them vulnerable to a fierce beating by the Ebidreul or a volley of arrows from the Summoner\u2019s forces. Afterwards some have developed a tradition of having the Ebidreul play music for their victory parades upon their return home. In the South these demons have found use by thaumaturgist who desire to have them drum as many clouds as they can to the ground so that the condensation within may be harvested for thirsty cattle and crops. Cattle rustlers have also enjoyed summoning the demon for their capacity to blind and distract others while they smuggle entire herds.<br /> When a person is flayed, and their skin tanned as a single piece outdoors is pelted by rain then a Sky Drumming Imp may frolic about tugging the rain cloud with them and taking the skin for spawning young. The Ebidreul flay human and demons alike, harvesting their skin in one piece. If two or more Sky Drumming Imps gather each with a tanned hide, they may work together to fashion a single massive drum from the hides. They then enter a frenzy, lasting 25 hours per each member who contributes a skin, and pummel the drum together in a loud bass. When they are finished the drum eventually falls apart and a newborn Sky Drumming Imp is spawned for each member of the birthing ritual who contributed a skin. Stealing or breaking their drum will instantly cause them limit break. They roll a die and add the number to their limit for every 25 hour period they go without getting to drum for a scene.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Motivation</b>: To live my life in an orgy of noise. They all have an Intimacy of Birthskin Drum (Pride), Cruelty (Joy), Music (Love). <b>Virtues</b>:<br /> <br /> Compassion 1, Conviction 2 , Temperance 1 , Valor 2<br /> Willpower 4<br /> <b>Attributes</b>:<br /> <br /> Strength 3, Dexterity 4 , Stamina 4 ; Charisma 3 , Manipulation 2 , Appearance 1 ; Perception 5, Intelligence 1, Wits 2<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Abilities</b>:<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Martial Arts 1 (Out Numbering their Foes 3)<br /> Melee 3 (Pummel Stick 1, Within Fog 2)<br /> Archery<br /> Thrown<br /> War 1 (Coordinated Attacks 3)<br /> Integrity 2<br /> Presence 1 (Cowardice 2, Cruelty 1)<br /> Performance 5 (Drum 2, In group 1)<br /> Resistance 4 (Drumming 3)<br /> Survival 2 (Traps 1, Foraging 1)<br /> Medicine<br /> Investigation<br /> Craft Water 3 (Leathworking 3)<br /> Occult 2 (Songs 3)<br /> Lore<br /> Athletics 3 (Jumping 3)<br /> Awareness 2 (Sound 3, Sight -3)<br /> Stealth 2 (In Fog 3)<br /> Dodge 2 (In Fog 3)<br /> Larceny<br /> Socialize 1 (Bands 3)<br /> Ride 1<br /> Sail 1<br /> Bureaucracy<br /> Linguistics 1 (Native Old Realm, Firetongue)<br /> <br /> <b>Backgrounds</b>:<br /> Backing 1, Resources 1, Contacts 1(Musicians), Allies 1 (Demon Band)<br /> <br /> <b>Charms</b>:<br /> <br /> 1st Excellency: Melee, Performance<br /> Principle of Motion<br /> Sense Domain: They may sense the fear and confusion of those within their fogs.<br /> Call: Their Drum Beats can be sense even past the noise of Hell by other muscians.<br /> Weather Control: They may use this charm with their drum beats to pull down existing clouds to ground level and condense or spread them as fog. The fog\u2019s unique resonance with the Anima banners of Exalted cause their light bounce and refract from within the cloud, and those within the fog must roll their Resistance + Stamina with a difficulty equal to the Essence rating of the Exalt with the highest Essence rating and an anima at the 8+ level. If they fail the roll they are blinded until they leave the fog for their essence rating actions as a crippling effect. The fogs may be up to the Demon\u2019s Essence X 50 yards, and each additional Ebidreul using this charm adds their Essence to the calculations.<br /> <br /> Spice of Custodial Delectation: Drumming may replenish their motes.<br /> <br /> <b>Essence</b>: 2<br /> <br /> Soak 2L/4B<br /> HEALTH: One -0, Two -1, Two -2, One -4, Incapacitated<br /> Mutations: All possess the Sonar mutation, many possess the fangs mutation, and some possess the horns mutation.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-22T20:38:42-08:00","id":1269981,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://web.archive.org/web/20160314201319/http://rathess.xi.co.nz/exalted/index.php/Characters:Iz_the_hunger_of_Bygone_Ages\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://web.archive.org/web/20160314201319im_/http:/rathess.xi.co.nz/exalted/resources/assets/poweredby_mediawiki_88x31.png\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://web.archive.org/web/20160314201319/http://rathess.xi.co.nz/exalted/index.php/Characters:Iz_the_hunger_of_Bygone_Ages\" target=\"_blank\"> Characters:Iz the Hunger of Bygone Ages - exalted official wiki - mirror from archive.org </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://web.archive.org/web/20160314201319/http://rathess.xi.co.nz/exalted/index.php/Characters:Iz_the_hunger_of_Bygone_Ages\" target=\"_blank\"> https://web.archive.org/web/20160314201319/http://rathess.xi.co.nz/exalted/index.php/Characters:Iz_the_hunger_of_Bygone_Ages </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div> <br /> <b>The Iz, the Hunger of Bygone Ages.</b><br /><br /> <span style=\"color:#252525\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>The Iz, the Hunger of Bygone Ages.</b></span></span></span><br /> <b>Demons of the First Circle, Coalescence of Yozis Essence</b> The Iz are an ancient race of demons that legend claims, like the Angylkae, predate the banishment of those that would become the Yozis from Creation. Back in the primeval dawn of Creation the Iz roamed the vast plains of the Southwest. They were famine given form upon the earth like the locusts were to the air and the piranha to the waters. Tyrant lizards, humans, and even Cacti and grass alike would learn to avoid the fields of white moving white teeth or they would learn to leave behind colorless bones if anything at all..<br /> In those days the Iz were the bleach white of the bones of their prey. But after their banishment they were stained by the defeat of their masters to the color of dark ink. This helped them for they no longer gathered in waves of teeth but dwelled in the shadows of the Demon city as natural lackeys and hangers on looking for any meat to eat, and while swarm tactics were still their favorite they adapted and learned of ambush from the darkness. The Iz Formed from the pooled blood of the Yozis. Essence congealed and tainted with their Hunger for freedom twisted into a hunger for meat and blood. The Iz are often the size of a raccoon and simple eyeless black heads filled with rows of crooked grinning teeth and with small apelike hands emerging from behind their head, and comically oversized feet below their chins. They leave a signature inkblot stain when killed.<br /> Now in the age of Sorrows everyone from the Sorcerers on the Blessed Isle to the thug bosses of Malfeas keep crews of Iz for they have a natural talent for going unnoticed for infiltration, murder, and kidnapping. They are naturally sadistic, and will work loyally as lackeys as long as their master doesn\u2019t mind their habitual nature of eating every living thing in sight, and torturing everything at their mercy. When given articles of clothing they may appear as an unassuming local of whatever area they inhabit thus allowing them to walk the streets of the Imperial City when given the wigs of old women, or take the roll of Mercenaries Peacekeepers in Nexus when carrying batons and a cap.<br /> <b>Summoning</b>: (Obscurity 1/3)<br /> Sometimes the Iz will find tunnels into Creations alleys when a person new to a city is reduced to disassociative catatonia due to the brutality city life. Sometimes an Iz will eat the remains of at least five other Iz with one season, and when this happens their form will bloat and upon their next meal they will burst into a birth explosion of ten newborn Iz.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Motivation</b>: Eat Meat<br /> <b>Virtues</b>: Compassion 1, Conviction 4, Temperance 1, Valor 2<br /> <b>Attributes</b>: Strength 3, Dexterity 4, Stamina 3; Charisma 2, Manipulation 3, Appearance 2; Perception 3, Intelligence 1, Wits 3<br /> <b>Abilities</b>:<br /> Martial Arts 3, Melee 2, Archery, Thrown, War 1, Integrity, Presence 2, Performance 1, Resistance 2, Survival 3, Medicine, Investigation 1, Craft, Occult 1, Lore, Athletics 3, Awareness 1, Stealth 3, Dodge 4, Larceny 3 (Stealing 1), Socialize 1, Ride, Sail, Bureaucracy, Linguistics (Native Old Realm)<br /> <b>Backgrounds</b>: Backing 1<br /> <b>Charms</b>:<br /> 1st Excellency Martial arts, Athletics<br /> 2nd Excellency Survival, Stealth, Larceny, Dodge<br /> Materialize<br /> Measure the Wind (To best find who to toady up to)<br /> Call<br /> Mirror of Infinite Wardrobe (They need two separate articles of clothing to appear as a certain type of individual)<br /> Landscape Travel (Doubles Speed traveling in the shadows of a City or town)<br /> Bread of Weak Spirit<br /> Meat of Broken Flesh<br /> Spice of Custodial Delectation: Spirit gains essence for doing Henchwork <b>Join Battle</b>: 4<br /> <b>Attacks</b>:<br /> Bite: Speed 5, Accuracy 8, Damage 4L, Parry DV -, Rate 2 Clinch: Speed 6, Accuracy 7, Damage 4L (P), Parry DV -, Rate 1 <b>Soak</b>: 1L/3B<br /> <br /> <b>Dodge DV</b>: 5 (They receive a smallness bonus making it 6 to things bigger then them) <b>Willpower</b>: 5<br /> <b>Essence</b>: 2<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-22T20:39:28-08:00","id":1269982,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://web.archive.org/web/20160314192323/http://rathess.xi.co.nz:80/exalted/index.php/Characters:Gumbla_the_Fungal_Marchers\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://web.archive.org/web/20160314192323im_/http:/rathess.xi.co.nz/exalted/resources/assets/poweredby_mediawiki_88x31.png\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://web.archive.org/web/20160314192323/http://rathess.xi.co.nz:80/exalted/index.php/Characters:Gumbla_the_Fungal_Marchers\" target=\"_blank\"> Characters:Gumbla the Fungal Marchers - exalted official wiki - mirror from archive.org </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://web.archive.org/web/20160314192323/http://rathess.xi.co.nz:80/exalted/index.php/Characters:Gumbla_the_Fungal_Marchers\" target=\"_blank\"> https://web.archive.org/web/20160314192323/http://rathess.xi.co.nz:80/exalted/index.php/Characters:Gumbla_the_Fungal_Marchers </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div> <br /> <b>Gumbla,the Fungal Marchers.</b><br /><br /> <span style=\"color:#252525\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>Gumbla the Fungal Marchers.</b></span></span></span><br /> <b>Demons of the First Circle, Orphans of Malfeas</b> The Fungal Marchers are the progeny of a 2nd Circle Lord lost to history, some say he was slain by a Lunar Blacksmith who crafted Armor from his bones, and others say she was crushed by Equitable Resolution and thus explaining why Octavian possesses the lion\u2019s share of the Fungal Marchers loyalty. And at least one apocryphal tale posits they are the debased result of a union of Vitriolic and Wood essence. Regardless the Gumbla have spread throughout the layers of Malfeas and even into Deserts of Cecylene and the Silver Forest of Szerony\u2019s sky roots.<br /> <br /> Gumbla about three feet tall on average but weigh as much as an adult human. They appear to be large brown fungal growths the color of rich sewage with one side of their body covered in jagged teeth and their oddly human eyes in a perpetual scowl. They have two feet that naturally grow leathery and appear much like laceless boots. They are constantly treading this way and that on their pitiably short legs and to halt for even a moment actually causes them pain and physical fatigue similar to a human exerting herself past her endurance.<br /> <br /> Gumbla have the natural ability keep their riches in Elsewhere pockets within their body. They may keep Resources or Artifacts worth up to their Essence in Background points within an Elsewhere pocket within their body by consuming it. They also may hide resources within manmade structures such as carved stone or wood, and given free time they often hoard their own riches or that of their masters throughout the territory they wander. These may be released by causing damage to the object or structure. All throughout Octavians quarter stone blocks are often smashed in battle releasing everything from loot plundered from Creation, to fine Malfean ales, and even Chalcanth.<br /> <br /> When Gumbla survive long enough to raise their essence they double in size with each additional Essence raised, though most of this goes into width and weight rather than size. All Gumbla have a soft spot on their head and striking that spot, Plus 3 external penalty, causes the Gumbla Aggravated Damage. If a Gumbla is higher essence then normal the penalty is reduced by 1 for each extra Essence point. If enlarged Gumbla are slain they instantly split into two gumbla of one essence lower than their progenitor. Thus extremely large Gumbla may be split into a horde, and some sorcerers specifically summon them for such a purpose, but they must be aware that these offspring are not under the same bindings, but Gumbla are naturally inclined to be minions and have intimacies of obedience to their Progenitor\u2019s master. Some Gumbla grow wings for an unknown reason, and those that do so refrain from growing larger and instead have a unique ability to create Gumblings. Gumblings are essence one spirits that appear like normal Gumbla but the size of apples and with attributes of only one. These winged Gumbla often have a motivation to explore and eventually the Gumblings get separated from their progenitor and if provided with food grow to full Gumblas.<br /> <b>Summoning</b>: (Obscurity 1/2) When a person dies from marching brown poisonous mushrooms may form at her last breath. If left to grow they may form legs and become a Gumbla.<br /> <b>Motivation</b>: To March. Winged Gumbla will have the Motivation To Explore.<br /> <b>Virtues</b>: Compassion 2, Conviction 4, Temperance 3, Valor 1<br /> <b>Attributes</b>: Strength 2, Dexterity 2, Stamina 4; Charisma 1, Manipulation 1, Appearance 2; Perception 3, Intelligence 1, Wits 2<br /> <b>Abilities</b>:<br /> <br /> Martial Arts 3<br /> Melee<br /> Archery<br /> Thrown<br /> War<br /> Integrity 2<br /> Presence 2<br /> Performance 1 (Dancing 1, In a group 2)<br /> Resistance 1<br /> Survival 3 (Foraging 3)<br /> Medicine<br /> Investigation<br /> Craft Earth 1, Craft Wood 1<br /> Occult 1<br /> Lore<br /> Athletics 2<br /> Awareness 2<br /> Stealth 1<br /> Dodge 2<br /> Larceny (Stealing 1, Hiding Things 1)<br /> Socialize 1 (Other Gumblas 2)<br /> Ride<br /> Sail 1 (Air Vessels 2)<br /> Bureaucracy 1<br /> Linguistics 2 (Native Old Realm, River Tongue, and Forest Tongue)<br /> <b>Backgrounds</b>: Backing 1<br /> <b>Charms</b>:<br /> <br /> 1st Excellency Resistance, Athletics, Martial Arts<br /> Spice of Custodial Delectation (Patrolling territory)<br /> Call (Other Bound spirits or fellow minions)<br /> Fruit of Living Essence<br /> Materialize<br /> Essence Bite <b>Join Battle</b>: 4<br /> <b>Attacks</b>:<br /> Bite: Speed 5, Accuracy 6, Damage 3L, Parry DV -, Rate 1 Clinch: Speed 6, Accuracy 5, Damage 3L (P), Parry DV -, Rate 1 <b>Soak</b>: 2L/4B<br /> <br /> <b>Dodge DV</b>: 3 (They receive a smallness bonus making it 4 to things bigger then them) <b>Willpower</b>: 5<br /> <b>Essence</b>: 2<br /> <br /> <br /> NOTES: Winged Gumbla have motivations to Explore, and they have the Wings Abomination. Each Essence past two a Gumbla has causes them to acquire and Oxbody, and a Large Mutation. Even without hands Gumbla make excellent Tireless workers and will pull objects with harnesses or pick them up in their mouths. Activating Elsewhere Pockets uses 3 motes of essence. Winged Gumbla spend 1 Willpower and 10 Essence to Create a Gumbling, and the Gumbling are often able to cling to their Mother when she takes flight, but the Mother often loses the Gumblings as they are attracted to other moving objects or food.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-22T20:40:08-08:00","id":1269983,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://web.archive.org/web/20160314202806/http://rathess.xi.co.nz:80/exalted/index.php/Characters:Bluugath_the_Devourers_of_Filth\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://web.archive.org/web/20160314202806im_/http:/rathess.xi.co.nz/exalted/resources/assets/poweredby_mediawiki_88x31.png\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://web.archive.org/web/20160314202806/http://rathess.xi.co.nz:80/exalted/index.php/Characters:Bluugath_the_Devourers_of_Filth\" target=\"_blank\"> Characters:Bluugath the Devourers of Filth - exalted official wiki - mirror from archive.org </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://web.archive.org/web/20160314202806/http://rathess.xi.co.nz:80/exalted/index.php/Characters:Bluugath_the_Devourers_of_Filth\" target=\"_blank\"> https://web.archive.org/web/20160314202806/http://rathess.xi.co.nz:80/exalted/index.php/Characters:Bluugath_the_Devourers_of_Filth </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div> <br /> <b>Bluugath the Devourers of Filth.</b><br /><br /> <span style=\"color:#252525\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Bluugath the Devourers of Filth.</span></span></span><br /> <b>Demons of the First Circle, Progeny of the Grinning Murdernaut</b> Feces, rot, and filth of all sorts lay in the wake of the Demon known as the Grinning Murdernaut. When the Grinning teeth are seen shining in the darkness of Malfean allies, the first substance is found, and when the Murdernaut leaves the other substance is created. Thus the Murdernaut found it wholly a benevolent for its beloved Malfeas to create the Devourers of Filth to sweep the streets and sewers cleans. Since that time Millenia ago the Devourers of Filth have grown numerous and have spread throughout the Demon city as common citizens throughout the different environments, with the exception of the Endless desert where they are not welcome.<br /> <br /> Bluugath are one of the demon species spawned by Mother Vines, a species of first circle demons created to spawn other demons. The Bluugath are boneless slugs with a system of cartilage like solid nerves. They are hunched over possessing no legs, only a torso ending in a flabby tail. They possess two muscular arms rippling with blubber, and ending in three fingered mitts with with large suction cups on the palms. They possess no jaw but rather the roof of their mouth clefts into two mandibles with citrine colored cilia filling their entire mouths. Their outer flesh is translucent and they shimmer and glow with the filth that is visible within. Their faces above their mouths are filled with two large black eyes that appear much like a saggy membrane encasing a deep pool. Their tongues are muscular and three pronged, while also able to be elongated into a third arm-like appendage. The Devourers of Filth range roughly from the size and weight of a camel to a hippo.<br /> <br /> Bluugath exude clear slime all over their body that emits a rich sugary aroma that attracts insects. They are constantly hunger for feces, and may consume waste, sewage, urine, and even rot soil and industrial waste. Upon digesting vast quantities of such filth they start excrete heavy flows of a processed oily black substance that acts as an extremely nutrient rich fertilizer. Mushrooms and insects grow numerous and fat upon consuming this sludge, and if boiled to kill life forms contained within it even works as an extremely richly sweet gruel that some Sorcerers in Creation use as emergency rations or primary food source for their slaves. Plants and fungi grown with the sludge have increased size, similar to the Large Mutation, but not Wyld based. Bluugath may track the scent of sewage and filth across any medium whether underwater (Lakes of filth being some of their natural habitats), or over air. Single Devourers of filth may serve a whole legion with expedient and efficient Latrine duty. When employed to service the sewers or mass graves of Creation their eventual habitation may result in such areas being overgrown with heavy undergrowth or marshes. This is why wise summoners either transport the the filth to be disposed of into an area they plan to cultivate, or they apply the Bluugath in teams eating their fill and ejecting the rich fertilizer elsewhere. The Bluugath are simple creatures motivated by sloth and gluttony, it is said once they had a higher culture when lead by heroes of their kind who fought for their rights but that time was long ago and short lived as they devolved back into their simpler lifestyles after their few and far between heroes where slain for acting against the descending hierarchy.<br /> <br /> The succulent nutrient rich flesh of the Bluugath are a popular delicacy in the Demon city with fresh Bluugeth saut\u00e9ed alive with Hellcattle butter being referred to a classical dish called Megacargo, and dried preserved Bluugath flesh being a popular food for storing for emergencies and tea made from such works as a common cure all for demons under the weather. Sometimes a Bluugath presented with too much filth to successfully eat in one sitting they may consume so much they burst, resulting in two new Bluugath who will consume their parents corpse and continue their meal. Some Bluugath who feel their time is up, or who feel depressed may purposely consume so much they explode, and when intentionally doing so they may create three spawned young rather than just two.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Summoning</b>: (Obscurity 1/2) When in Creation over a thousand humans move their bowels in unison a Bluugath may crawl from the resulting confluence of Filth. While less common in the age of Sorrows this such occurrences happened frequently in the high first age, and during intermission for certain sporting events transmitted Creationwide, through IAM, hundreds of millions of mortals have been known to use the time to void their bowels and thus creating the greatest migrations of the Bluugath who swarmed into the sewers of Creation in the hundreds of thousands resulting in alarms going off in the security stations of Heaven causing weeks of intense overtime for the celestial employees.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Motivation</b>: To appease their Endless hunger for feculent delicacies.<br /> <b>Virtues</b>:<br /> <br /> Compassion 2 , Conviction 2 , Temperance 1 , Valor 2 Willpower 8<br /> <b>Attributes</b>:<br /> Strength 4 , Dexterity 1 , Stamina 4 ; Charisma 1 , Manipulation 1 , Appearance 1 ; Perception 3, Intelligence 1, Wits 1<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Abilities</b>: Martial Arts 1 (Suckbite 2) Melee Archery Thrown War Integrity 2 (Depression 1) Presence 1 Performance 2 (Mating Calls 1, Filth Dances 2) Resistance 2 (Holding in their bowels 2) Survival 3 (Waste 3) Medicine 1 (analyzing Waste 3) Investigation 1 (Sewers 3) Craft Water 1 (Boiling the waste into gruel 2), Earth , Wood , Air 1(Sewage Painting 3) , Magitech , Fire Occult 1 (Fecal Lore) Lore Athletics 2 (Swimming 2, Climbing 1) Awareness 2 (Waste 3) Stealth 3 (Sewers 3) Dodge 3 (Covered in Filth 3) Larceny 1 (Smuggling 3) Socialize 1 (Sewer Dwellers 3) Ride Sail 1 Bureaucracy Linguistics (Native Old Realm)<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Backgrounds</b>: Backing 1<br /> <br /> <b>Charms</b>:<br /> <br /> 1st Excellency, Survival, Stealth<br /> Materialize<br /> Track- Those whose waste they have sampled<br /> Hurry Home- To their Sewer Nests<br /> Essence Plethora 1<br /> Ox Body 1<br /> Intrusion Sensing Method, may detect Intruders into the Sewers, or influx of waste<br /> Sense Domain, they may sense Waste and Sewers<br /> Call- They may call for aid in consuming massive deposits of waste<br /> Landscape Travel- Double speed in Filth<br /> Essence 2<br /> Soak: 6B/2L Slimy Hide 2B/0L<br /> Note: Bluugath receive 1 Limit Each day they are not able to Devourer their Weight in Filth. Bluugath waste adds three to Survival rolls for growing, and foraging for food. Dried Bluugath flesh add 2 to resistance rolls for recovering from sickness or poison.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-22T20:40:45-08:00","id":1269984,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://web.archive.org/web/20160314202517/http://rathess.xi.co.nz:80/exalted/index.php/Characters:Haegle_the_Spite_Ogres\" target=\"_blank\">https://web.archive.org/web/20160314...he_Spite_Ogres</a> <br /> <b>Haegle The Spite Ogres.</b><br /><br /> <span style=\"color:#252525\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>Haegle The Spite Ogres .</b></span></span></span><br /> <b>Demons of the First Circle, Coalescence of Malfeas</b> True rage is omnipresent in Malfeas for that is the emotion least distressing to the Fallen King. Rage and Vitriol fulminate in geysers of violence throughout the most densely populated areas of the demon city, and sometimes the carnage that remains after an essence detonation coalesces into the form of a Haegle. The Spite Ogres are beings of simple thoughts but intense rage. They range from about one and a half to three people high. Their frames are rippling with grotesque muscles that sometimes split out of their oily luteous hides forming thick growth scars. They appear as primitive humanoids often with over extended jaws, large sloping foreheads and always with massive hands and feet much larger than normal for human or even ape proportions. Teeth reach out of their gums like angry towers and regrow in doubled rows when broken. Though some eschew garments most find simple slacks or loincloths desirable, especially when attracting mates. Curiously most fabrics and leathers not crafted into an artifact seem to be tainted purple from their rage filled auras.<br /> <br /> Spite Ogres pride themselves off of their strength, particularly in being stronger than others, and any culture developed by a gathering of them revolves around violence upon those weaker than themselves. Whenever they find themselves in Creation they naturally take advantage of their ability to produce offspring with humanity and the sunlight of Creation seems to keep them in a perpetual rutting season. Demon slayers are most often beseeched to avenge a village that has had all their youths captured by a Spite Ogre seeking to form a spontaneous harem.<br /> <br /> Virtually all Spite Ogres are of the standard emerald shade and they are dull witted but roughly of human intelligence, perhaps more akin to the commoner jadeborn or goblin\u2019s intelligence but with massive mood swings and little to no self-restraint. Their rage fuels their strength. However rarely some Spite Ogres are born of birth fulminations during the Malfean nights when the Ebon Dragon hides Ligier\u2019s light and this results in the birth of a Grey Spite Ogre the color of thunder clouds. These breed of Spite Ogres are free to raise their intellect but at the cost of their peerless might. While still strong enough to crack stone and break an ox the Grey are often no taller than 8 feet in height, with a prominent hunch from the thick back muscles that all Spite Ogres possess. The Grey are still hostile but they are more cunning and driven by avarice to the point of finding positions as leg breakers or prized thugs to Citizens of Malfeas, and even Guildsmen of Creation. And rarer still are the Crimson Spite Ogres born from birth fulminations that follow after the wake of the Silent Wind. These are share much of the traits of the Grey but while the Grey find themselves driven by greed the Crimson Ogres find themselves driven by cold vengeance. They will hunt down and physically rend any who catch their eye as offensive. Cannibalism is perhaps the trait that all three breeds share similar enthusiasm for.<br /> <b>Summoning</b>: (Obscurity 2/4)<br /> <br /> A Spite Ogre may find their way into Creation when a planned explosion or demolition is interrupted due the intervention of a wondering youth. Spite Ogres not born directly from Fulminating Malfean Essence are created when a Spite Ogre mixes its blood into the blood of a mortal, resulting in the mortals body transforming into a new Spite Ogre. This fact was discovered by surprise when a Twilight was experimenting with Demon Blood transfusions in Mortals to develop new medicinal techniques. Few are privy to this obscure fact, and Haegle Demonblooded are far more prevalent then blood spawned get.<br /> Emerald Spite Ogres<br /> <b>Motivation</b>: Motivation: Prove I am the Strongest There Is!<br /> <br /> <b>Virtues</b>: Compassion 2, Conviction 4, Temperance 1, Valor 5<br /> <b>Attributes</b>: Strength 8, Dexterity 3, Stamina 8; Charisma 1, Manipulation 1, Appearance 3; Perception 2, Intelligence 1, Wits 2<br /> <b>Abilities</b>:<br /> <br /> Martial Arts 4 (Those who Insult Me! 3)<br /> Melee 1 (Improvised Weapons 3)<br /> Archery<br /> Thrown (Scenery 3)<br /> War<br /> Integrity 1(Being Stubborn 1)<br /> Presence 2 (Rage 3)<br /> Performance 1(Roaring 2)<br /> Resistance 5<br /> Survival 2<br /> Medicine<br /> Investigation<br /> Craft<br /> Occult<br /> Lore<br /> Athletics 5 (lifting 3)<br /> Awareness 2 (Those who piss me off)<br /> Stealth<br /> Dodge 1<br /> Larceny<br /> Socialize<br /> Ride<br /> Sail<br /> Bureaucracy<br /> Linguistics (Native Old Realm) <b>Crimson and Grey Spite Ogres</b><br /> <br /> Motivation: (Grey) To have it All. (Red) Kill Any Who Piss Me Off!<br /> Valore 4, Conviction 5, Compassion 1, Temperance 1<br /> Strength 6<br /> Dexterity 3<br /> Stamina 6<br /> Charisma 3<br /> Manipulation 3<br /> Appearance 3<br /> Intelligence 3<br /> Wits 4<br /> Perception 3<br /> Martial Arts 4 (Dirty Fighting 3)<br /> Melee 1 (Improvised 3)<br /> Archery 1<br /> Thrown 2 (Scenery 3)<br /> War 1<br /> Integrity 2 (Stubborn 1)<br /> Presence 2 (Intimidation 3)<br /> Performance 1<br /> Resistance 4<br /> Survival 2<br /> Medicine<br /> Investigation 1<br /> Craft<br /> Occult 2<br /> Lore 2<br /> Athletics 3<br /> Awareness 2<br /> Stealth 3<br /> Dodge 3<br /> Larceny (Stealing 1)<br /> Socialize 1<br /> Ride 2<br /> Sail 2<br /> Bureaucracy 1<br /> Linguistics 2 (Native Old Realm,Two other Languages including maybe Guild Cant)<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Backgrounds</b>:<br /> <b>Charms</b>:<br /> <br /> 1st Excellency Martial Arts, Thrown, Resistance, Athletics<br /> Ox Body x4<br /> Essence Plethora x2<br /> Materialize<br /> Landscape Travel (Double Leaping)<br /> Bread of Weak Spirit<br /> Meat of Broken Flesh<br /> Shatter (Shockwave from Clapping or striking the Ground)<br /> Martial Arts Charms (Often Spite Ogres will Learn Martial Arts that revolve around grappling or vicious hand to hand attacks, and some even become masters of CMAs).<br /> (Infernal Monster Style Charms are learned as Spirit Charms by the Spite Ogres)<br /> <br /> <b>Join Battle</b>: Emerald: 4 Crimson/Grey: 6<br /> <b>Attacks</b>: Emerald<br /> Kick: Speed 5, Accuracy 7, Damage 10B, Parry DV 4, Rate 2 Punch: Speed 5, Accuracy 8, Damage 8B, Parry DV 5, Rate 3 Clinch: Speed 6, Accuracy 7, Damage 8B (P), Parry DV -, Rate 1 Grey/Crimson<br /> Kick: Speed 5, Accuracy 7, Damage 8B, Parry DV 4, Rate 2 Punch: Speed 5, Accuracy 8, Damage 6B, Parry DV 5, Rate 3 Clinch: Speed 6, Accuracy 7, Damage 6B (P), Parry DV -, Rate 1 <b>Soak</b>: Emerald 4L/8B Crimson/Grey 3L/6B<br /> <br /> <b>Dodge DV</b>: Emerald 4 Crimson/Grey 5 <b>Willpower</b>: 10<br /> <b>Essence</b>: 4 (They increase with age and experience until brutally slain.)<br /> <br /> <br /> Notes: Spite Ogres treat their Essence Pool as Peripheral and have Anima Banners much like Exalted, with their Iconic effects being Explosions or Disasters. Emerald Spite Ogres have an Anima power of adding Valor in successes instead of dice when channeling their Valor while their Anima is flaring. Crimson Spite Ogres have Anima effects similar to Fire Aspect Dragonblooded. Grey Spite Ogres don\u2019t have Anima\u2019s. Spite Ogres have been known to raise their Essence but often they are slain by the armies of the 2nd Circles, or even earning death at the hands of the Unquestionable before they reach the higher peaks of essence. Some whisper of transformations similar to that of elementals upon reaching greater awareness of essence\u2026<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-22T20:41:21-08:00","id":1269985,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://web.archive.org/web/20160314195923/http://rathess.xi.co.nz/exalted/index.php/Characters:Odeles_the_pastry_smiths\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://web.archive.org/web/20160314195923im_/http:/rathess.xi.co.nz/exalted/resources/assets/poweredby_mediawiki_88x31.png\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://web.archive.org/web/20160314195923/http://rathess.xi.co.nz/exalted/index.php/Characters:Odeles_the_pastry_smiths\" target=\"_blank\"> Characters:Odeles the Pastry Smiths - exalted official wiki - mirror from archive.org </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://web.archive.org/web/20160314195923/http://rathess.xi.co.nz/exalted/index.php/Characters:Odeles_the_pastry_smiths\" target=\"_blank\"> https://web.archive.org/web/20160314195923/http://rathess.xi.co.nz/exalted/index.php/Characters:Odeles_the_pastry_smiths </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div> <br /> <b>Odeles, the Pastry Smiths.</b><br /><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252525\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Odeles, The Pastry Smiths.</span></span></span><br /> <b>Demons of the First Circle, Progeny of the Scumwhaler</b> Tireless the forges of the Odeles pumps out sweet smelling prismatic smoke along with a tinkling tune and deep bass thumping, thus serving the dual purpose of sweetening the acrid and often caustic air of Malfeas and keeping the Silent Wind at bay. The Scumwhaler Sings the Pastry Smiths to life by flying over the Smiths and Foundries of Malfeas and scratching upon an array of two turning discs while bleating a secret melody of hunger that only the brass hammers of Malfeas may hear over an artifact phonic rod. This creates an urge for smiths to clap their hands, and if they do their hammers nearby will get up and flee to hammer their own bodies into being out of the brass flesh of Malfeas. The Scumwhaler only collects a few of the newborn Odeles to produce for him confectionary delights while he endlessly scumwhales.<br /> The animated hammers eventually hammer entire bodies for themselves which appear like rough chunks of brass with pointed ears and crude bumps for facial features. They will first acquire boots and an apron through the fastest means available and then will set to work finding employment hammering delicious and intricate pastries into being. Over the by the first year their eyes and mouth form and the accrue facial features and appear more like living creatures as their Brass flesh refines itself with their experience. They eventually grow beards and hair the varying from tarnished black, to dull rusted red, or a light green patina. The hammer which they spawned from is actually grown out of their very arm. The Pastry Smiths with little experience seem to have crude bludgeons for arms with maybe a simple bough indicating an elbow, but the most refined and experienced maestros actually develop hands fingers and fingerprints that may switch their birthhammers into their other hand.<br /> <br /> As Pastry Smiths they are able to apply their knowledge of the crafting of cakes and baked goods through the use of their hammer and anvil. They may hammer the impurities from any substance transforming them into a number of delicacies enjoyed from Creation, to Yu-Shan, and rarely seen, much lest tasted, outside the courts of Rakshastan. If their starting ingredients are actual substances others can produced pastries with using conventional cooking then they may produce the results with their hammer and forge at half the speed it normal takes to bake. If using ingredients not normally edible then it may takes hours longer than making them using conventional cooking and conventional ingredients. The Pastry Smiths constantly sing each with their own independent style, and the striking of their hammers release sounds similar to multiple instruments in unison, and in the First Age many an Exalted Diva has been angered to find that the Pastry Smiths have been producing acoustic wonders for centuries similar to what they have innovated over their lifetime. Some have taken this with glad heart and mass imported the Pastry Smiths to Little Malfeas communities across Creation, and others have taken them as a slight and have expunged hundreds personally from the forges of Demon City.<br /> The Odeles have been valued for their Glittering treats that have looked like the Faberge Eggs of Exalted Craftsmen but that taste like the finest sweets in Heaven. It has been taken as amongst the greatest slights in Hell to kill a Demons Pastry Smith. Traditionally assassinating anothers Pastry Smith is the calling card of 2nd Circle Duelists indicating that if they win the feud they will purge the Demon City of the entire Dominion of their foe, including even their most valued Courtesans and Slaves.<br /> Pastry Smiths have developed a common culture and appreciation of others of their species, and have taken to seeking employment as bands so that they may flavor their pastries with the melodies that they hammer out of the air onto all their dishes. Pastry smiths have been known to hammer whole cookies using only their notes when denied resources or ingredients. Traditionally they hammer a cookie or tart out of a simple song as a calling card or in place of a resume when searching for a new employer, or a place with a band of other Pastry Smiths. Some Employers are delighted when they find that their new chef may even hammer crumpet\u2019s flavored with the tortured scream of Mortals freshly imported from Creation, while still others have them only flavor their deserts with the prayers of their Cults worship hymns.<br /> When no available employers are found, however, some may be displeased to find a Pastry Smith having squatted in their tenements and having hammered their jewelry, weapons and even livestock into wedding cakes and cream-puffs.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Summoning</b>: (Obscurity 2/4)<br /> <br /> Some desperate mortals on the brink of starvation have taken to eating their shoe, but if the take to trying to cook them first and at least one other has already died of starvation a Pastry Smith may appear from the smoke of the cook fire to hammer their shoes into Gingerbread, and if no one stops the Odele they will continue on and hammer their fallen comrades into a funeral cake and serve them with a smile. Sometimes settlements will have a perfectly amiable relationship with a Pastry Smith living amongst them, however few actually know the true story of how they came to deliver a failing settlement from the brink of starvation or what their first celebratory meal was.<br /> There comes a time when a Pastry Chef finds themself content from a lifetime\u2019s worth of work. When this happens they will find themselves hammering a new hammer into shape, the very moment they make their last strike the hammer seems to wield itself and starts the birthing process of hammering themselves a new body from the nearest lump of base metal. Those who find themselves with constant work seem to feel these urges to birth (At most once a year) more often than those without much work (which may be once every handful of decades).<br /> <b>Motivation</b>: To Smith Pastries of the Highest Caliber for a Hungry World. <b>Virtues</b>: Compassion 4, Conviction 3, Temperance 2, Valor 2<br /> Willpower 7<br /> <b>Attributes</b>:<br /> <br /> Strength 4<br /> Dexterity 4<br /> Stamina 6<br /> Charisma 4<br /> Manipulation 1<br /> Appearance 2-4<br /> Intelligence 2-4<br /> Wits 1<br /> Perception 3<br /> <br /> <b>Abilities</b>:<br /> <br /> <br /> Martial Arts 1 (Hammer Arm 3)<br /> Melee 3 (Hammer 3)<br /> Archery<br /> Thrown 1 (Cakes and Pies 3)<br /> War<br /> Integrity 2 (Perfectionist 3)<br /> Presence 2 (Those who Eat your Pastries 3)<br /> Performance 3-6 (Making Music 3)<br /> Resistance 4 (Tireless)<br /> Survival<br /> Medicine<br /> Investigation 1(Finding Ingredients 3)<br /> Craft Water 5-8(Pastry Smithing 3), Craft Vitriol 1 (Chalcanth Frosting 3)<br /> Occult 2 (Mystery Flavors 3)<br /> Lore<br /> Athletics 3<br /> Awareness 2 (Tunes 3)<br /> Stealth<br /> Dodge<br /> Larceny 1 (Making Disguises out of Pastries 3)<br /> Socialize 1 (Other Pastry Smiths 3)<br /> Ride<br /> Sail<br /> Bureaucracy 1 (Contracts 3)<br /> Linguistics 1 (Native Old Realm, Other Language what Employer speaks)<br /> <b>Backgrounds</b>: <b>Charms</b>:<br /> <br /> 2nd Excellency Craft, Performance, Melee<br /> Materialize<br /> Spice of Custodial Delectation (While Pastry Smithing)<br /> Meat of Broken Flesh (Can hammer Spirits and living things into essence refilling Sweets)<br /> <br /> Affinity (Flavor) Control (The Pastry Smiths may hammer the emotions from sounds into unique flavors)<br /> Bane Weapon (Their Hammers may Deal Aggravated Damage to those who Criticize their Meals)<br /> Calculated Order of Immediate Action (Pastry Smiths may hammer their own songs into their signature flavors)<br /> <br /> <b>Essence</b>: 3<br /> <br /> <br /> They receive one Limit Each Day they hear Criticism of their work. The Secret of their Pastry Smithing lies in the song in their Quicksilver Hearts.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-22T20:41:52-08:00","id":1269986,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://web.archive.org/web/20160315090001/http://rathess.xi.co.nz/exalted/index.php/Characters:Iegionnaires_the_Fruit_of_Arms\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://web.archive.org/web/20160315090001im_/http:/rathess.xi.co.nz/exalted/resources/assets/poweredby_mediawiki_88x31.png\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://web.archive.org/web/20160315090001/http://rathess.xi.co.nz/exalted/index.php/Characters:Iegionnaires_the_Fruit_of_Arms\" target=\"_blank\"> Characters:Iegionnaires the Fruit of Arms - exalted official wiki - mirror from archive.org </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://web.archive.org/web/20160315090001/http://rathess.xi.co.nz/exalted/index.php/Characters:Iegionnaires_the_Fruit_of_Arms\" target=\"_blank\"> https://web.archive.org/web/20160315090001/http://rathess.xi.co.nz/exalted/index.php/Characters:Iegionnaires_the_Fruit_of_Arms </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div> <br /> <b>Iegionnaires The Fruit of Arms</b><br /><br /> <span style=\"color:#252525\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>Iegionnaires The Fruit of Arms.</b></span></span></span><br /> <b>Demons of the First Circle, Progeny of the Tree of Arms</b> This varied race of demons holds promise of infinite use in Malfeas, and beyond. The Tree of Arms breathes dreams from the very air of Malfeas, and sips them from the light of the Burning Stars of Malfeas, and drinks deep from the spilled blood in Malfeas. They grow into the Fruits of Arms, each the shape of weapons found in the dreams, and each baring a singular burning hatred towards their foe.<br /> <br /> The Shapes of the Fruit of arms numerous and each has a driving hatred for something dreamed of before they were born. The Demons of Malfeas have spread the fruits throughout the Layers of the Demon city as they have found them quite useful in the wars of their Masters as many have grown Hatred towards other Demons. As the shapes of the Fruit of Arms can look as any armament though often they are twisted and frightening with spikes and blood found in a nightmare, but some are glorious and bright from dreams of conquest. Each Fruit of Arms may track the subject of their Hatred and thus of the sorcerers who know of them in Creation find great use in summoning a Fruit of Arms that Hates the subject of their attention. They thus serve a dual purpose as a tracker and weapon.<br /> <br /> Many of the Fruits have taken up singing from their travels with different masters and the Theaters and Halls of Malfeas have joyfully embraced Operas in which the Fruit of Arms sings majestically while their wielder performs elegant Katas or ritualistic execution. It has also grown popular among the more benevolent Tyrants in Malfeas to accept final requests of being executed by the Fruit of Arms while they sing their favorite song. And some Fruit of Arms have actually acquired Battle experience and can make coordinated attacks and may be wielded by subordinates of their Demon Armies.<br /> <br /> The Fruit of the Tree of Arms each have the qualities of Perfect Equipment and while most take the form of Melee weapons some speak of Assassins in Malfeas armed with Singing Algeral fueled Hellwands and Crowsbows which scream threats when fired. And some say certain Elder Fruits of Arms have resolved their motivation and gained the shape of their slain Nemesis\u2026<br /> When a Fruit of the Tree of Arms survives a battle that results in the death of one of their Wielders they may leak a viscous clear flood into a puddle of their heart\u2019s blood then a sapling may grow from it soaking up the ambient essence in the remains. A new Fruit of the Tree of Arms may bud from this sapling that may take the form of any sort of tree or plant. Like its parent the new Fruit of the Tree of Arms may be of any shaped dream.<br /> <br /> <b>Summoning</b>: (Obscurity 3/4) When someone has lost everything except Vengeance or Anger a Fruit of Arms may drop from a fruit tree they pound on thrice in impotent despair and then slumber under.<br /> <b>Motivation</b>:<br /> <b>Virtues</b>: Compassion 1, Conviction 3, Temperance 1, Valor 4<br /> <b>Attributes</b>: Strength 3, Dexterity 2, Stamina 3; Charisma 3, Manipulation 1, Appearance 1-6; Perception 3, Intelligence 2, Wits 2<br /> <b>Abilities</b>:<br /> <br /> Martial Arts 2 (Their Nemesis 3)<br /> Melee 2 (There Nemesis 3)<br /> Archery<br /> Thrown<br /> War 1-4<br /> Integrity 1<br /> Presence 3 (Their Nemesis 3)<br /> Performance 2-6 (Singing 3)<br /> Resistance 1<br /> Survival 3 (Their Nemesis 3)<br /> Medicine<br /> Investigation 1 (Their Nemesis 3)<br /> Craft<br /> Occult 2<br /> Lore 1<br /> Athletics 1<br /> Awareness 2<br /> Stealth 2<br /> Dodge<br /> Larceny 1 (Gambling 2)<br /> Socialize 1 (Opera fans 3)<br /> Ride<br /> Sail<br /> Bureaucracy 1 (Arms price)<br /> Linguistics 1-5 (Native Old Realm, but some have learned languages as Exotic as High Holy Speech and Peliagial just to carry on their music)<br /> <b>Backgrounds</b>: Backing 1<br /> <b>Charms</b>:<br /> <br /> 1st Excellency Presence, Performance<br /> 2nd Excellency Martial Arts, Melee, Survival<br /> Spirit Cutting<br /> Shattered Adamant Attack<br /> Words of Power<br /> Bane Weapon (Their Nemesis, maybe a type such as Redheads, or even an Individual, or a Species of Demon or Animal, or Plant)<br /> Essence Bite (Used on those not authorized to wield them)<br /> Tracking (Their Nemesis)<br /> Meat of Broken Flesh<br /> Hurry Home (Towards their Authorized Wielder/Partner)<br /> Materialize<br /> <b>Join Battle</b>: 4<br /> <b>Attacks</b>:<br /> <br /> Use the traits of a Perfect Weapon <b>Soak</b>: Depends on the Arms<br /> <br /> <b>Dodge DV</b>: Arms Parry Not Dodge <b>Willpower</b>: 7<br /> <b>Essence</b>: 2 (Being Prized throughout Malfeas, well used, many have raised their Essence, especially if their Motivation was against a specific individual which they succeeded on Slaying)<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-22T20:42:27-08:00","id":1269987,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://web.archive.org/web/20160314200415/http://rathess.xi.co.nz:80/exalted/index.php/Characters:Oxel%27xip_the_Shadetailed_Menders\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://web.archive.org/web/20160314200415im_/http:/rathess.xi.co.nz/exalted/resources/assets/poweredby_mediawiki_88x31.png\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://web.archive.org/web/20160314200415/http://rathess.xi.co.nz:80/exalted/index.php/Characters:Oxel%27xip_the_Shadetailed_Menders\" target=\"_blank\"> Characters:Oxel'xip the Shadetailed Menders - exalted official wiki - mirror from archive.org </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://web.archive.org/web/20160314200415/http://rathess.xi.co.nz:80/exalted/index.php/Characters:Oxel%27xip_the_Shadetailed_Menders\" target=\"_blank\"> https://web.archive.org/web/20160314200415/http://rathess.xi.co.nz:80/exalted/index.php/Characters:Oxel%27xip_the_Shadetailed_Menders </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div> <br /> <b>Oxel'xip, the Shadetailed Menders.</b><br /><br /> <span style=\"color:#252525\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Oxcel'xip, the Shadetailed Menders.</span></span></span><br /> <b>Demons of the First Circle, Progeny of the Oramus Device</b> Oxel\u2019xip, Shade Tailed Menders, Progeny of the Oramus Device<br /> Amongst the ruins outside the territory of Oramus a 2nd circle Demon named Vedderhart the Dicoverer of Horizons has found an indescribable wonder. Vedderhart has not uttered this secret to anyone and has secreted this miracle of sprockets and tubes of eleven undreamt colors, what Vedderhart has named the Oramus Device, onto his floating Skyvessel the Knightsailor. Upon attempting to translate what is believed to be the Instruction new beings are plucked from the Mirrored monitor of the Oramus Device. These are the diminutive yet ingenius Shade Tailed Menders.<br /> They appear as squirrels under two feet in height with distinctly simian like features and a vast array of fur and pigment marks. They appear from the Oramus Device wearing think uniformed suits that appear to be fashioned from artificial materials and alloys not seen since the first age, and advanced mechanisms throughout the suit. They claim their native tongue is Stych and they only speak Old Realm due to it being uploaded as part of their Acclimation Protocols. They claim the reason why they are spirits has much to do with this Acclimation Protocols birthing them into a form native to Malfeas, and thus why they are bound by summons. They believe perhaps that the Calamity they were fleeing from may have converted their very beings into Data, which the Oramus Device translated into the Essence of Creation forming them into Malfean Demons, and their consciousness is born in a spirit body composed of their original bodies and suits preserving as much as possible with their Acclimation Protocols.<br /> <br /> They claim to be a people lost not just in time and space but Dimensions. They are purportedly travellers from another Universe. Much of their collective memory is lost but they believe their homeland may have been in danger or possibly even eradicated and that they are nomads seeking a new home for their populace, which they are uncertain of the exact magnitude of the survivors. They believe the Oramus Device must have created a Wormhole into whatever Cataclysm they were caught in. So far none of the Oxel\u2019xip have recognized each other but they believe it may be due to memory loss combined with the potentially numberless amount of the refugees of their people. One radical theory is the Oramus Device may actually pluck a Shade Tailed Mender from a different Universe each time, with each Universe only having one Crewmember survive whatever Calamity they were fleeing. They have formed a Civilization to incorporate newly Acclimated Oxel\u2019xip. They have formed an association where a number of their kind serves the Discoverer of Horizons, in hopes of translating more of their number with the Oramus Device, with careful plans to wait for a time when they may take it as their own without suffering the wrath of a more powerful denizen of Hell. The larger population is working to discover any method that may allow them to find their way back home. But the largest amount of them has taken to the ideal of Oxel\u2019tot, meaning a new home. Many have spread throughout Malfeas in hopes of finding secrets to making a new home.<br /> <br /> The Oxel\u2019xip have discovered the hard way about Orabilis and his displeasure of forbidden knowledge when he hurled one of their greatest Scientists, Wiseeyes, into his new home as a star of Malfeas. They have taken to accumulating only portions of the Glass Libraries into each individual, or converting the data they find there into portable and separate media. Those that find their way into Creation seek to tread new horizons in hopes of finding Home. They have members currently seeking the mysteries of Creations Underground, as well as the Wyld, which is their greatest hope for finding home. Some have even made forays into the Underworld and Labyrinth. They have learned Creation holds amnesty from the horrors of Malfeas, and safety for induction into Sorcery, though they know most likely course into Creation is through Slavery, and so they are wary of Humanity and Spirits native to Creation\u2019s shores. Their wisest seek a plan involving thaumaturgy to smuggle their civilization out of Hell, while many of the Shadetails work as Menders throughout Malfeas working for Citizens and 2nd Circle Demons rising in position, while secretly acting as spy for their civilization.<br /> <br /> The entire species varies in abilities but they all show a minimum competence in Lore, and enough Craft to have at least one dot in Magitech. They claim this is due them being Marines aboard some sort of exploration vessel. But this has resulted in all who know of them in Malfeas to refer to them as the Shadetailed Menders, due to them being usually at least competent enough to maintain and repair First Age Magitech. But the desires of Demons in Malfeas are blunt and most have found them to be easily overpowered pray, and they have spread the popular word that these Shadetails are delicious, which has yet to be proven a fallacy even in Creation. Each Shadetail fancy\u2019s themselves an expert in a certain field, and in that area they have obtained heroic regard in, resulting in 5 dots in at least one ability.<br /> Shadetails have taken to finding or creating artifacts for use as an edge for their civilization. They have engineered repeating crowsbows, and even artifact Assault Crossbows. They have also taken to hording any artifacts they can find. Due to their spirit natures they have realized they may push their bodies to heights that would have been considered supernatural in their original forms. Their exemplars have taken to learning Thaumaturgy, and Sorcery when they leave Malfeas, and members in all realms have taken to dispersing Martial Arts knowledge amongst their civilization.<br /> Shadetails have found that their new spirit natures have rendered them infertile to their normal breeding practices. They have however applied their knowledge of cloning to create a randomized clone of themselves to reproduce. They have discovered the data potential of both their parents lies within their essence and have developed Artifacts to randomize another specimen of that data. They do not refer to these as their children rather they refer to them as their brother or sister due to them being effectively a new potential child birthed from the potential of the donors own parents. These are incubated and awaken fully grown with genetic memory and soon develop their favored Ability to five. Some amongst Creation having been separated from their kind for too long have made the discovery that they can procreate with Mortal Squirrels, and at least one ata-beast epic talks of an ata-beast squirrelmaiden falling for a strange squirrel from beyond the horizon and starting the Stareye clan.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Summoning</b>: (Obscurity 3/7)<br /> <br /> <br /> Sometimes when Mortals cause a Manse to explode during a meteor shower a Shadetailed Mender may be found amongst the rubble confused but proud to be out of Malfeas.<br /> <br /> <b>Motivation</b>: To Find Home.<br /> <b>Virtues</b>:<br /> <br /> Compassion 3, Conviction 4, Temperance 2, Valor 2(Members have variable numbers of virtues this is just the most common.) Willpower 7<br /> <b>Attributes</b>:<br /> <br /> <br /> Strength 1<br /> Dexterity 4<br /> Stamina 2<br /> Charisma 2<br /> Manipulation 2<br /> Appearance 3<br /> Intelligence 4<br /> Wits 4<br /> Perception 3<br /> <br /> <b>Abilities</b>:<br /> <br /> <br /> Martial Arts 2 (Fighting in tiny spaces 3) (Some Commandos have a rating of 5)<br /> Melee 2 (Fighting Bigger foes 3) (Some Commandos have a rating of 5)<br /> Archery 3 (In cramped spaces 3) (Some Security Officers may have 5)<br /> Thrown 1 (In cramped spaces 3) (Some Commandos may have a 5)<br /> War 1 (Some Security Officers or Commandos may have up to 5, and a 3 specialty in Guerrilla combat)<br /> Integrity 2 (Perfectionist 3)<br /> Presence 2 (Motivation 3) (Captain\u2019s and Commanders may have 5)<br /> Performance 2 (Starlets may have a 5, with specialities)<br /> Resistance 2 (Some Engineers may have 5 with specialty 3 in Tireless)<br /> Survival 3 (Shelter 1, Tracking 1, Foraging 1) (Commandos may have 5)<br /> Medicine 1 (Medical Officers may have 5)<br /> Investigation 1 (Some Science Officers may have 5 with a Specialty of Magitech 3)<br /> Craft Air 2, Craft Fire 2, Earth 1, Magitech 1 (Some Engineers, Chefs, and Technicians may have 5 in these or any other Crafts deemed appropriate)<br /> Occult 1 (Some Explorers have a specialty of 3 split between Raksha, Demons, or Ghosts, Dimensional Science Officers may have 5 )<br /> Lore 2 (Repair 3) (Science Officers and Technicians may have 5)<br /> Athletics 2 (Security Officers, or Commandos may have 5)<br /> Awareness 2 (Pilots and Commandos may have 5)<br /> Stealth 1 (From bigger things 3) (Commandos may have 5)<br /> Dodge 2 (From Bigger things 3) (Commandos and Security Officers may have 5)<br /> Larceny 1 (Spy\u2019s may have 5 with specialties divided amongst Forging, Stealing, Locks)<br /> Socialize 1 (Other Oxel\u2019xip 3) (Captains may have 3)<br /> Ride 1 (3 a particular first age device) (Pilots may have 5)<br /> Sail 2 (Magitech Vessels 3) (Pilots may have 5)<br /> Bureaucracy 1 (Trade 3) (Ambassadors and Captain may have 5)<br /> Linguistics 1 (Native is claimed to be Stych, all know Old Realm Specialty in Translating 3) (Language Officers may have 5) <b>Backgrounds</b>:<br /> <br /> Backing1-5 (Oxel\u2019xip rank from Ensign to Admiral), Artifacts 1+ (Artifacts are common with all having an integrated Resplendent Personal Assistant, and their Envirosuits are often Magitech Armor from 2-5), Resources 3 (with their Science they have made a point of outfitting each Shadetail with emergency precious metal and gems for trade), Some have a Familiar or Artifact Automaton <b>Charms</b>:<br /> <br /> (Charms often stem from their Biomechanical Nature)<br /> All have a 2nd Excellency in Craft and Lore. Most will also have at least two other Excellencies.<br /> Call: They may activate Distress beacons for aid.<br /> Measure the Wind, the Visors of the Shadetails can measure the motonic powerlevel of a creature<br /> <br /> Amethyst Awareness, their Visors are nigh infinitely articulate and precise and may detect across multiple dimensional wavelengths<br /> Hurry Home (The Shadetails may activate their transporters to beam them back to their nearest base, or vessel)<br /> Materialize Spirit Cutting Strike (They can harmonize their Dimensional Frequency to harm other Energy Beings) Essence Plethora Reserve of Will<br /> Host of Spirits- this is a unique version of the charm that allows them to make their cloned siblings, it requires the commitment of 15 Motes, 1 Willpower and 7 hours a day worth of work setting up a Genesis Tube Relay for the Newborn to form in. After a season of tending, a new Shade Tailed Mender will awaken from the Genesis Tube Relay upon the next Calibration, when the motes uncommit. Due to inconvenience of such a long commitment new Shade Tailed Menders are usually only created in the safety of a Colony where others may protect the Genesis Tube Relay and the progenitor.<br /> <br /> <b>Essence</b>: 2 (more experienced heroes raise their essence and traits, but clones fresh from Randomization are at 2)<br /> <br /> <br /> NOTES:<br /> Some Shadetails will have Terrestrial Sorcery Particularly Swift Messenger, and Food from the Aerial Table, and Water from Stone, and defenses vary.<br /> Some have mastered a TMA or even Spirit based CMAs like the 4 Virtue Styles.<br /> Thaumaturgy is popular with the Dimensional Officers often trading knowledge in them amongst the different outposts of Shadetails, and Spys constantly seeking to obtain knowledge of such.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-22T20:42:57-08:00","id":1269988,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://web.archive.org/web/20160314201410/http://rathess.xi.co.nz:80/exalted/index.php/Characters:Gildempru_the_Gastronomic_Alchemists\" target=\"_blank\">https://web.archive.org/web/20160314...mic_Alchemists</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#252525\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">In the arts of excess Malfeas is second to none. Malfeas is home to many an exotic flavor for all of the human senses and the many senses unique to the Demon City. The boxlike frame of the Gildempru contain ingeniously intricate processes that is a wonder of the demon city. Their organs are often more adequate then a first age lab. These miracles of the demon city are praised by all who can tempt one into servitude or enslave one outright. For anything the Gastronomic Alchemists consume with their ducklike bills they may disgorge into their component substances or even rearrange into different compositions.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252525\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Feed one a bucket of rusty nails and they may defecate a small pyramid of iron and a smaller oval of oxidized dust followed by a pill contained the dye used to paint the characters for nails on the bucket. But that is just the simplest display of their natural digestive wonders. Their passion is for tastys, be they sweet sweets or savory saut\u00e9ed Erymanthus flank. For the processes of preparing and cooking can all be achieved internally for Gildempru, and they often employed as Sushi Chefs; by consuming quantities of rich golden sewermarsh rice of the Demon City, a sampling of ivory kelp, and the flesh of fresh Kimberyspawn they can shat out an impressive spread fit for a 2nd Circles wedding, as noted in the First Age Travel Journal of Pyreseus No Hammer a much experienced No Moon travelling Food Critic.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252525\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">The Gildempru achieved notoriety for Sorcerers using them as poison tasters secretly before Calibration fetes. Under the orders to consume the entire feast in secret, analyze the meals internally for poisons and proportion the meal out in such a manner as to poison the unsuspecting poisoners favored dish. The Twilight Caste Goldsleeves was once criticized by his Solar guests for not warning them ahead of time when the court Gildempru converted the toxins from the wine into the favored honeycakes of his treacherous Circlemate, resulting in the week long coma of his Circlemate and the gruesome deaths of his seven new Goldchild nieces and nephews. Goldsleeves however found the whole affair hilarious enough to try again at the next Calibration, but was disappointed at his guests\u2019 lack of appetite.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252525\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">The Sap of Feuds scribed the Gildempru from his own sap handpainted onto his own amber in characters noting the 108 secret herbs and spices for his favorite recipe for Malfean Lemon Gruel. By the time the calligraphy is complete the sap hardens into amber it implodes into a newborn Gastronomic Alchemist. The Sap of Feuds have found them to be a ragging successes; pointing out in Hell Salons with pride that Lawgivers have joyfully savored the artfully decorated product of his children\u2019s bowel movements for centuries and he has yet to receive so much as a stern glance or a death threat from them! He was noted as having a foul mood for a century and a day after the Usurpation, due to the less uniform appraisal of the Shogunate culture towards having Demonic Chefs crap out their dishes. Though many have discovered they make perfectly adequate chefs even when resorting to using conventional cooking equipment.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252525\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Gildempru are about the size and rough shape of bears but with a definitely cube like shape to their torso and shoulders. They are furless but their brown rippling skin creates the illusion of fur. They possess hands similar to mitts and their eyes for some reason remind mortals of a gentle pony. Their professionalism demands do their work fully dressed in a chefs uniform of any culture, even when this covers their translucent stomachs which one may see the convoluted system of tubes, churners, and other less identifiable processes. They have found work as Chefs, but also as fine sentient breweries or as laboratory assistants with a built in lab laboratory function. They have a natural flesh layer over their nether regions appearing much like a skirt. These provide them with privacy while they defecate out their banquets. As long as they are allowed their flesh curtain worth of privacy they don\u2019t mind producing meals, but if they are aware of anyone looking under their curtain they will flying into an angry fit. Them may receive one point of limit everyday someone glances under their skirt. There rectum unfolds into a natural conveyer belt that places their food under their large beaver like tail.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252525\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>Summoning</b>:</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252525\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">(Obscurity 2/3, though pre Contagion era it was 1/3) In Creation Gastronomic Alchemists may emerge from the distended stomachs of gluttons who die of overeating when dining out and topping off their meal with an after dinner confection. Often their first act is to poop out a new meal made from the reassembled last meal of their fleshy doorway.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252525\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">When a Gastronomic Alchemist feels as if their life is up, they may search for another of their kind with similar sentiments about their life. One will crawling into the bill of the other, both will become extra malleable to allow one to fight inside the other. The bloated Gildempru will then look for a large amount of liquid to submerge themselves in. When fully submerged the liquid will boil and after 8 hours the hardened exterior of the Gildempru will crack and a number of newborn Gastronomic Alchemists will crawl out equal to the highest essence of the parents.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252525\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>Motivation</b>: To spread the wonders and joys of the World of 10,000 Tastes to all, with natural gusto.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252525\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>Virtues</b>: Compassion 3, Conviction 3, Temperance 2, Valor 2</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252525\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Willpower 7</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252525\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>Attributes</b>:</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252525\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Strength 6</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252525\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Dexterity 3</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252525\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Stamina 4</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252525\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Charisma 3</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252525\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Manipulation 2</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252525\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Appearance 3</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252525\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Intelligence 3</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252525\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Wits 2</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252525\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Perception 3 <b>Abilities</b>:</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252525\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Martial Arts 2 (Grappling 3)</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252525\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Melee 2 (Kitchen Equipment 3)</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252525\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Archery 1 (Basting 3)</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252525\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Thrown 2 (While cooking 3)</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252525\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">War 1 (Coordinating 3)</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252525\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Integrity 2 (Culinary Integrity 3)</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252525\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Presence 2 (Those you Cook For 3)</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252525\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Performance 2 (Hibatchi 3)</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252525\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Resistance 3 (Working in a Kitchen 3)</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252525\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Survival 2 (Foraging 3)</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252525\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Medicine 1 (Health Foods 3)</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252525\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Investigation 1 (Food 3)</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252525\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Craft Water 5 (Comfort 3)</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252525\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Occult 1 (Secret Recipes 3)</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252525\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Lore 1 (Measurements 1, Food 2)</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252525\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Athletics 1 (Lifting 3)</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252525\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Awareness 2 (Taste 3)</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252525\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Stealth 1</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252525\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Dodge 1</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252525\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Larceny (Gambling 3)</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252525\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Socialize 1 (Favorite Meals 3)</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252525\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Ride</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252525\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Sail 2 (With Full Stomach 2)</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252525\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Bureaucracy 1 (Ingredients 3)</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252525\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Linguistics 2 (Native Old Realm,Two other Languages including maybe Guild Cant)</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252525\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>Backgrounds</b>: <b>Charms</b>:</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252525\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">2nd Craft Excellency, 2nd Awareness Excellency</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252525\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Meat of Broken Flesh</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252525\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Spice of Custodial Delectation- Cooking gives them motes</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252525\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Materialize</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252525\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Affinity (Food) Control- Their internal organs may manipulate food and ingredients of wood and earth. Melodious Diagnostic Support- They may analyze anything they consume. Calculated Order of Immediate Action- They may create materials derivative of what they ate up to the amount in what they ate.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252525\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Essence Plethora</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252525\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Ox Body x2</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252525\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>Essence</b>: 2</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252525\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">NOTES:</span></span></span><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12952,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","user":"Accelerator","date":". 09-09-2020, 09:41 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-22T20:46:14-08:00","id":1269989,"title":"","content":"2 demons, by gardenerbrieaus<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://forums.sufficientvelocity.com/threads/general-exalted-thread.44/page-1713#post-9172826\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forums.sufficientvelocity.com/data/svg/20/1/1794123741/logo_icon.png\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://forums.sufficientvelocity.com/threads/general-exalted-thread.44/page-1713#post-9172826\" target=\"_blank\"> General Exalted Thread </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://forums.sufficientvelocity.com/threads/general-exalted-thread.44/page-1713#post-9172826\" target=\"_blank\"> https://forums.sufficientvelocity.com/threads/general-exalted-thread.44/page-1713#post-9172826 </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> I'd say dodge's Charms are a tad more synergy-heavy than Resistance Charms, rewarding you for taking a lot of them and using them together. If you're just planning a small dip to shore up your defense, then Resistance may be better. Dodge also come with some not strictly defensive things like... </div> </div> </div> <br /> A bulky creature, twice as tall as a man but almost three times as wide, which walks along the ground on a dozen stumpy, thick-skinned legs. Its body is guarded by <a href=\"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/09/SouthernThreeBandedArmadillo065b.jpg/220px-SouthernThreeBandedArmadillo065b.jpg\" target=\"_blank\">a thick, segmented shell dotted with downy tufts of fur</a> (which is actually immature sections of new shell in the process of growing to replace the old as it wears out), both of which take on the coloration &amp; texture of whatever the demon was eating at the time of its formation[1]. Their triangular, scaly-skinned heads bear a prodigious mane of fine, threadlike hairs, which serves as their primary sensory organ: each hair is prehensile &amp; has a fantastically fine sense of touch, smell, and taste, letting them passively strain the air around themselves for signs of danger or opportunity.<br /> <br /> When one of these demons finds a broken object or injured creature, these same hairs probe every inch of it - picking up things like poison or chemical corrosion by taste, identifying ruptured organs from the slight give in the skin that covers them, and mapping out the precise dimensions of cracks and cuts - before they unhinge their jaws and scoop it into their belly. The demons actually feed on the conceptual imperfection of damaged things, with the &quot;repairs&quot; happening as part of the damage being digested; once there's no more damage to eat, the demon vomits up the now-fixed thing like an owl pellet and moves on.<br /> <br /> So essentially, they're weird giant armadillo monsters that only repair things as an incidental consequence of their digestive processes, which I like as an expression of the &quot;demons as biopunk tools&quot; guideline. They don't heal people out of altruism or to bless them with the Yozis' power, they do it because injured people are full of tasty food and once they've finished getting the food out and spat up the waste material (i.e., the now-healthy person), they have no more concern for it than an elephant does for the piles of dung it leaves behind[2].<br /> <br /> <br /> [1] Having a variety of different colors and textures in one's shell is a minor mark of status for them, interpreted as a sign that one is strong enough to venture far and wide for different &quot;flavors&quot; despite the dangers of Malfeas. Of course, the accuracy of that belief is rather suspect, considering members of the species who simply live in a demonic bazaar and make their way by fixing up others' wares often have quite spectacular shells, but it's still something a good number of them aspire to.<br /> <br /> [2] Which results in a lot of them becoming effectively livestock for other demons, who keep them as a way to quickly repair damaged equipment or heal injured allies/customers without needing to pay anything. The more independent ones tend to seek out parts of Hell where strange, exotic injuries occur - they wander the shores of Kimbery and pick up creatures that have been half-melted by her acid waters or poisoned by the beasts that live inside it, feast on strange Essence-based plagues and wounds in the nastier parts of the Ellogean blood bayous, sample the many ruins wrought on flesh by Malfean vitriol, or risk it all for the sublime culinary sensations of Metagaos' infectious creations: buildings being devoured by squirming moss, demons riddled with strange parasitic fungi, even swallowing segments of landscape where the grey jungle impinges on other Yozis' world-bodies to feed on its raw Metagoian flavor. These adventurous gourmands generally either become food for another, or become corrupted and warped by their ingestion of Hell's darker repasts<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> --------------------------------<br /> <br /> Distinctly oceanic beings, indicative of their Kimberian heritage: their lower bodies are vaguely crustacean, stout plugs of chitin studded with sturdy legs like that of a lobster. From the top of this sprouts an eye-studded column of slick gray flesh, crowned with a nest of many-jointed (yet oddly human) arms, each ending in a sort of bony syringe.<br /> <br /> These demons are cautious and subdued, preferring to act only once they have firmly grasped a situation - a temperament that only leads them to frustration, as the many dangers of Malfeas routinely force them act with what they consider unseemly haste. Further, they have a powerful distaste for things which are ill-made, unkempt, or otherwise riddled with imperfections, which is likewise inflamed by the way Hell's teeming masses generally must prioritize practicality over perfection. As a result, they are infamous grumblers and critics, much given to snide remarks and snappish critiques of those around them.<br /> <br /> What prevents the breed from being driven to utter madness (or wiped out by other demons as an annoyance) is their gift for maintaining, repairing, and improving that which affronts them so. Once one of them has completed its analysis of a subject's imperfections, they set to rectifying them with great enthusiasm. Their lower bodies contain organs filled with a thick Essence-infused slurry, which is then channeled up into the syringes on their arms and injected into the places where the subject's failings are most egregious. From there, the demon uses the injected slurry as a way to directly influence the subject and remove its flaws.<br /> <br /> A wall of basalt, worn and pockmarked from the scouring sands and molten rain of Cecelyne, pulses and throbs in a semblance of living tissue as it seemingly &quot;grows&quot; new stone to replace what time and neglect have taken away. Once the demon has finished, the crude brickwork has been transformed into perfectly fitted pentagonal stones, and the graffiti that marred its surface is replaced by painted prayer-murals and elegant bas-relief.<br /> <br /> A sickly mortal beggar is reborn as a paragon of health - milky eyes replaced by shimmering orbs of the polychromatic acid that has replaced his blood, the stump of a wrist now capped by a six-fingered hand with pearly protective chitin[3], pockmarks that sprawled across the bridge of his nose and the small of his back are replaced with Yozic prayer tattoos, rotted teeth scooped out and replaced with two ribbed curvatures of alabaster bone on the upper &amp; lower jaw (with etched prayers to the Olive-Lipped Preacher where they meet the gums, of course), diseased guts rewoven into a sturdy boiler of Malfean brass that can tear sustenance from bread and brick with equal ease.<br /> <br /> This version is rather more &quot;traditional&quot;, but the idea of chirurgeon anemones that treat fixing a bent spearhead and fixing a broken arm in the same way - particularly in the sense of freely mixing together organic and inorganic traits when doing their work - appeals to me somewhat. Also, they can perform actual improvements on the things they work with, rather than just removing damage.<br /> <br /> <br /> [3] And of course, the other hand has been replaced as well - the asymmetry would be unbearable otherwise, and the man's fingernails were utterly atrocious anyway.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-22T20:48:14-08:00","id":1269991,"title":"","content":"My stuff: <br /> <br /> <i><b>SARKANY, THE EVER-GROWING HOARD<br /> ~FIRST CIRCLE DEMON, PROGENY OF THE TEMPTER OF MEN</b></i><br /> <br /> Many are the riches of Malfeas. Trees of gold, are common here, the precious metal growing like plants. Shrubs of silver, where if you were not careful, you would cut yourself on the soft metal leaves. Demons, wonders, exotic and infernal fauna and flora, and the various substances composed from the world-bodies of the Yozis. <br /> <br /> But, amongst the most exotic of them are the Sarkany. Their blood when exposed to air becomes precious dragon-amber. Their scales, composed of precious jewels and metals. Their breathe stinking of brimstone and vitriol. Their hide, composed out of diamond and metal, impervious to nearly any weapon. Their minds, brutal and cunning. Their claws, dextrous and lethal. Yet, heroes constantly search for the Sarkany. For slaying one brings unimaginable riches. <br /> <br /> Each Sarkany starts out small. When young, they can fit into a man's hand, and they possess a single egg-sized jewel or talent of gold. It is weak, compared to other demons, and hides in a safe place. Perhaps an abandoned ruin, or a lonely mountain cave. Its scales dare shed, and during that, blood flows, and become coins and amber and precious stones. The bigger the dragon, the bigger the scales, and the greater the treasure. And as it grows in size and Essence, its intelligence grows. A Sarkany that has grown enough will begin to craft its hoard. Jewels are polished to a brilliant shine using the vitriol they drool from their mouth. Gold and silver are melted down under firey breathe, and under the work of surprisingly dextrous talons, they begin to work the metals. Under the infernal prowess of the demons, precious raw metal becomes intricate jewellery, whorls, chains, bangles, and other trinkets inset with the precious jewels and amber that also descended from the dragon itself. Each a Magnus Opus of a master mortal smith. The older the dragon, the more precious the trinkets and baubles in its pile.<br /> <br /> And most precious of all, are the artifacts. Shining arms and armour. Daiklaves and spears made of Electrum, and armour made of jade-steel. <br /> <br /> The greed of men know no bounds, and they would always try to steal the hoard of the Sarkany. Whether by stealth, force, guile, or speed. But alas, to no avail! A man, leaving his companions behind as a distraction, stole a chain inset with rubies the size of his eye. A month later, and he had been struck down with incurable leprosy, and no matter how much he spent he could not cure it, nor pay for the company of others. A thief in the night stole a gold coin, and dropped it. This drew the attention of one of his victims, and upon being caught, was sentenced to lose his hands. He now sits forlornly in the corner, looking at the gold coin which had cost him so much. The hoard of a Sarkany is cursed, and no one may profit it while it lives. Only by killing the beast, can the hero enjoy his reward. <br /> <br /> But it is no easy task to slay a first circle demon. The breathe of a Sarkany is terrible. Its eyes and ears and nose, sharp as razor wire. Its claws, terrible and rending. And to make it worse, the hoard it lays on can be counted on to be part of its body, and so the heroes have to contend with the fact that the very treasure they seek is now also trying to kill them. <br /> <br /> And so they die, and their corpses are devoured, along with any equipment they find. There, their lost hopes, their dreams, their bodies, and their souls, are alloyed with whatever they had on their bodies, and within the belly of the Ever-growing Hoard, something new is forged. Until with a burp and a cough, the Hoard spits out a new addition to its pile of treasure. Perhaps a shield made of Jade-steel. Perhaps a sword of Celestrium. Perhaps a sword of enchanted steel. No matter. More will always come. <br /> <br /> Summoning: Foolish sorcerers summon the Sarkany to gain their riches. Impossible, as they cannot lift the curse from their treasures nor give it away freely. More often, they are summoned as master jewellers and goldsmiths, or to analyse the worth of a treasure. The Sarkany find other uses as sentries and guards, their talents that let them defend their hoard also letting them fight off any number of attackers or spot any thief, unleashing wave after wave of molten gold and impossibly-hard diamond.<br /> <br /> --------------------------------------<br /> <br /> <i><b>SARKANY, THE EVER-GROWING HOARD<br /> ~FIRST CIRCLE DEMON, PROGENY OF THE TEMPTER OF MEN</b></i><br /> <br /> Many are the riches of Malfeas. Trees of gold, are common here, the precious metal growing like plants. Shrubs of silver, where if you were not careful, you would cut yourself on the soft metal leaves. Demons, wonders, exotic and infernal fauna and flora, and the various substances composed from the world-bodies of the Yozis. Scholars and adventurers know of these. But those in the know, wish for the Sarkany the most. <br /> <br /> The Sarkany are dragon-shaped demons, with a stink of sulfur and steel-hard scales. Their hide, impervious to nearly any weapon. Their breathe, full of fire and scorching acid. Their minds, brutal and cunning. Their claws, sharp and lethal. Yet, each Sarkany is sought after by fools and heroes alike, for the hoard they collect is known to be the richest of them all. <br /> <br /> Each Sarkany starts out small. A small dragon-shaped being, the size of a man's hand, could possess a single egg-sized jewel, or a block of gold. At this stage, it is fragile, and hides in a dark and deserted place. Like a deep mountain cave, or in a forest alcove. Then it becomes bigger, and the hoard grows. More gold and silver coins appear. Then it gets bigger and bigger, and as its size increases, so does its hoard. Until it becomes gargantuan, and its hoard becomes a mountain. And as its size increases, so does the precision and exquisiteness of the jewellery. The jewels are no longer the size of eggs. Now they glow with an inner fire, or show images of exquisite art when light is shone through them. The gold is no longer arranged in blocks, but instead in necklaces and chains, all in whorls and curves and decorations, each one the equivalent of a master goldsmith's magnus opus. <br /> <br /> But what draws attention the most, are the arms and armour. The greed of men know no bounds, and they would always try to steal the hoard of the Sarkany. Whether by stealth, force, guile, or speed. But they often fail, for even the greatest of mortal men are wheat before the scythe when face with a demon. And so they die, and their corpses are devoured, along with any equipment they find. There, their lost hopes, their dreams, their bodies, and their souls, are alloyed with whatever they had on their bodies, and within the belly of the Ever-growing Hoard, something new is forged. Until with a burp and a cough, the Hoard spits out a new addition to its pile of treasure. Perhaps a shield made of Jade-steel. Perhaps a sword of Celestrium. Perhaps a sword of enchanted steel. No matter. More will always come. <br /> <br /> Uses: Sorcerers will often summon the Sarkany for their hoard, to gain their riches. This is often foolish, for they consider handing over anything to be an unacceptable order. The sorcerer has to take the treasures, just like everyone else. Many are the tales of adventurers and explorers looking into abandoned demenses and sorcerous labs, only to find a Sarkany. The Sarkany find other uses as sentries and guards, their talents that let them defend their hoard also letting them fight off any number of attackers or spot any thief.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-22T20:48:52-08:00","id":1269992,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/533482-argatoi-the-brass-turtles-demons-of-the-first-circle\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/filedata/fetch?filedataid=1074\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/533482-argatoi-the-brass-turtles-demons-of-the-first-circle\"> Argatoi, The Brass Turtles, demons of the first circle. - Onyx Path Forums </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/533482-argatoi-the-brass-turtles-demons-of-the-first-circle\"> http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/533482-argatoi-the-brass-turtles-demons-of-the-first-circle </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> Came up with these while getting anxious for 3e to drop. Thought I would share and seek any advice people are willing to give. In particular some different ideas for the unbound slip into creation portion would be nice. Not certain that the current condition is even feasible in the wild except under </div> </div> </div> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"> <span style=\"font-family:inherit\"> <b>Argatoi, The Brass Turtles, demons of the first circle.</b><br /><br /> [COLOR=#6A6A6A !important]<span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\">05-30-2015, 02:05 PM</span></span></span></span></span></span><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><br /> </span><br /> </span></span>[/COLOR]<br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:inherit\">Came up with these while getting anxious for 3e to drop. Thought I would share and seek any advice people are willing to give. In particular some different ideas for the unbound slip into creation portion would be nice. Not certain that the current condition is even feasible in the wild except under extremely unlikely events.<br /> <br /> <b>Argatoi, the brass turtles, demons of the first circle</b><br /> These large six-legged, red leather and brass plated turtles are known for their appetite for coal as well as assistance in the forging of metal. Though they resemble turtles that are about the size of a wagon, they are generally faster than creations turtles, though they have difficulty running. They are strong and resilient and can be used as beasts of burden, though that is not their specialty in the demon realm. <br /> <br /> They consider coal to be a rare delicacy, and like most things they eat they heat it up in their mouth before consuming it. They can emit a strange green light from their tongues and throats which allow them to heat meals or breath a line of green light and fire in self defense. <br /> <br /> They are very skilled at maintaining an exact temperature when heating a meal, so they can be instructed to heat a mouthful of coal to very specific temperatures. Metal smiths learned long ago that they could bargain with an Argatoi to help them forge a piece of equipment in exchange for the coal used in the forging process. The brass plates that make up part of their shells can also function as anvils within easy reach. The various ridges, spikes, rounded, and flat surfaces offer just about any kind of shape required. A smith simply needs to be familiar with a particular Argatoi's shell and move to an appropriate part.<br /> <br /> At this point most Argatoi have witnessed and been a part of the forging of a great many metalworks, and smart summoners will prize them as much for their advice on craft projects as they do during the forging. Flattery and stoking their ego seem to work best when convincing them to impart advice, though the asker should be prepared to listen to a long-winded tale about a previous work. A summoner must remember to ask before starting a work as it can be rather difficult to understand a demon turtle who is speaking with a mouthful of coal and metal.<br /> <br /> Those who wish to make use of them should be careful. The heat and green light they emit increases the usual fatigue experienced when working the forge, so a smith should set aside ample time for rest. In addition prolonged exposure can cause strange blistering and an effect not unlike sunburn, and long-term exposure may cause temporary or permanent blindness. Many smiths cover themselves from head to toe, and wear darkened goggles when using the assistance of an Argatoi. These precautions will of course heightened the effects of fatigue experienced by the crafter.<br /> <br /> A pristine deposit of coal that is set on fire by natural occurrences may draw an Argatoi from the demon realm, mouth watering for a tasty meal.</span><br /> </span></span></span><br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-22T21:01:00-08:00","id":1269993,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1ec21_DUlm1NO6sWzwOn0M9tGXfohlqmYJmqw1WpJhiM/edit\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1ec21_DUlm1NO6sWzwOn0M9tGXfohlqmYJmqw1WpJhiM/edit\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1ec21_DUlm1NO6sWzwOn0M9tGXfohlqmYJmqw1WpJhiM/edit\" target=\"_blank\"> https://docs.google.com/document/d/1ec21_DUlm1NO6sWzwOn0M9tGXfohlqmYJmqw1WpJhiM/edit </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Qrsa9T2XMzWY_laBnu9ReLNPqUi6dVvCaJ8ScTKKXjM/edit\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Qrsa9T2XMzWY_laBnu9ReLNPqUi6dVvCaJ8ScTKKXjM/edit\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Qrsa9T2XMzWY_laBnu9ReLNPqUi6dVvCaJ8ScTKKXjM/edit\" target=\"_blank\"> https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Qrsa9T2XMzWY_laBnu9ReLNPqUi6dVvCaJ8ScTKKXjM/edit </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1FUqbQqjaCSpUci3-voQmdXp85swPgGM0xcyCZ8ZvNR0/edit\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1FUqbQqjaCSpUci3-voQmdXp85swPgGM0xcyCZ8ZvNR0/edit\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1FUqbQqjaCSpUci3-voQmdXp85swPgGM0xcyCZ8ZvNR0/edit\" target=\"_blank\"> https://docs.google.com/document/d/1FUqbQqjaCSpUci3-voQmdXp85swPgGM0xcyCZ8ZvNR0/edit </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-22T22:12:43-08:00","id":1270006,"title":"","content":"Accelerator you are a prince among men! I need to get s new laptop so I\u2019ve been using my phone but man I need to put up my demons on google so I don\u2019t keep having to look them up when a computer crashes or the wikis go down! I friggin hate it that I put up all the demons I gathered on the first thread ten years ago on 2 wikis and they both ended up dead wikis. And I had a list of Names of Demons I was going to do next but the list wasn\u2019t salvageable on the wayback machine.<br /> <br /> But man I need to update for 3rd ed, so far I only updated as I used them in major scenes, so I did Spite Ogres because I had them in a fight, and the Creeping Shelter because that was a pet/Mobilehome for my last group of PCs.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-22T22:27:31-08:00","id":1270008,"title":"","content":"Creeping shelter?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-22T22:39:38-08:00","id":1270010,"title":"","content":"Yeah there are a few more from the list.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/840448-eldagusto-presents-demon-index-3rd-edition\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/filedata/fetch?filedataid=1074\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/840448-eldagusto-presents-demon-index-3rd-edition\"> Eldagusto Presents: Demon Index 3rd Edition - Onyx Path Forums </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/840448-eldagusto-presents-demon-index-3rd-edition\"> http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/840448-eldagusto-presents-demon-index-3rd-edition </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> So I plan to make a Thread Gathering the Fanmade Demons for 3rd Edition. I need to convert my 2nd ed Demons, which I need to make time for but for now I will </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> The Tzargarduchi<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://rathess.xi.co.nz/exalted/index.php/Characters:Tzargarduchi_the_Creeping_Shelters\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://rathess.xi.co.nz/exalted/index.php/Characters:Tzargarduchi_the_Creeping_Shelters\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://rathess.xi.co.nz/exalted/index.php/Characters:Tzargarduchi_the_Creeping_Shelters\" target=\"_blank\"> http://rathess.xi.co.nz/exalted/index.php/Characters:Tzargarduchi_the_Creeping_Shelters </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Also the Uncanny Costumes, the Knights of Fortune and the Helltramps.<br /> <br /> Man though writing demons was fun. I also used Tre Knights of Fortune in my 3rd ed game but they didn\u2019t have a battle yet.<br /> <br /> And for Elementals I used the old mix two Pok\u00e9mon trick and made grasscrabs by mixing Crabby With Parasect.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-22T22:41:18-08:00","id":1270011,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/223770-homebrews-of-the-first-circle?p=1270006#post1270006\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Accelerator you are a prince among men! I need to get s new laptop so I\u2019ve been using my phone but man I need to put up my demons on google so I don\u2019t keep having to look them up when a computer crashes or the wikis go down! I friggin hate it that I put up all the demons I gathered on the first thread ten years ago on 2 wikis and they both ended up dead wikis. And I had a list of Names of Demons I was going to do next but the list wasn\u2019t salvageable on the wayback machine.<br /> <br /> But man I need to update for 3rd ed, so far I only updated as I used them in major scenes, so I did Spite Ogres because I had them in a fight, and the Creeping Shelter because that was a pet/Mobilehome for my last group of PCs.</div> </div> </div> </div>So what do you think of my stuff, the Sarkany?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-22T22:58:01-08:00","id":1270014,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/223770-homebrews-of-the-first-circle?p=1270011#post1270011\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So what do you think of my stuff, the Sarkany?</div> </div> </div> </div>I like em, at first I was thinking 2nd Circleish Powers due to artifact and wealth Creation, but they are all cursed so that is interesting. I really like the flavor from things like eating people and digesting their dreams into jewelry.<br /> <br /> Maybe have something like limiting their hoard, so they have to actually grow more potent to noticeably increase the Horde or the unintended consequence of older treasures disappearing to be replaced with new Creations. Maybe the horde is cursed while they are alive to return to the horde pile but if slain it is that treasure which is most cursed. Otherwise you could just use summon demon and smash the Dragon with a goremaul and boom they are rich, rinse and repeat. So maybe such treasure is destined to drift back to Hell or the Wyld or the Endless Desert or he Underworld.<br /> <br /> Curious at some mechanics for this.<br /> <br /> Still reading the thread. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-22T23:51:45-08:00","id":1270025,"title":"","content":"The fuck????<br /> <br /> Eldagusto. <br /> <br /> Are the jaemi.... that character from harvest moon?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-22T23:57:09-08:00","id":1270026,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/223770-homebrews-of-the-first-circle?p=1270014#post1270014\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I like em, at first I was thinking 2nd Circleish Powers due to artifact and wealth Creation, but they are all cursed so that is interesting. I really like the flavor from things like eating people and digesting their dreams into jewelry.<br /> <br /> Maybe have something like limiting their hoard, so they have to actually grow more potent to noticeably increase the Horde or the unintended consequence of older treasures disappearing to be replaced with new Creations. Maybe the horde is cursed while they are alive to return to the horde pile but if slain it is that treasure which is most cursed. Otherwise you could just use summon demon and smash the Dragon with a goremaul and boom they are rich, rinse and repeat. So maybe such treasure is destined to drift back to Hell or the Wyld or the Endless Desert or he Underworld.<br /> <br /> Curious at some mechanics for this.<br /> <br /> Still reading the thread. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Um.... of course they're growing more potent as the horde grows bigger. The horde grows with their essence.<br /> <br /> As for the smashing.... duh?<br /> <br /> Look. You're a sorcerer. Probably an exalted. <br /> <br /> Money is no objection to you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-23T00:09:25-08:00","id":1270030,"title":"","content":"There's some great -and amusing! - concepts here.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-23T00:16:02-08:00","id":1270034,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/223770-homebrews-of-the-first-circle?p=1270025#post1270025\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The fuck????<br /> <br /> Eldagusto. <br /> <br /> Are the jaemi.... that character from harvest moon?</div> </div> </div> </div>By the gods! In almost a decade you are the only one to pick up on that, and I\u2019ve shared them in multiple forums and I thought all the clues were there. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-23T00:19:31-08:00","id":1270035,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/223770-homebrews-of-the-first-circle?p=1270026#post1270026\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Um.... of course they're growing more potent as the horde grows bigger. The horde grows with their essence.<br /> <br /> As for the smashing.... duh?<br /> <br /> Look. You're a sorcerer. Probably an exalted. <br /> <br /> Money is no objection to you.</div> </div> </div> </div>It reminds me of one of the Demons in the old thread that someone posted there. They were beautiful jewel encrusted shapeshifting Scarabs I think, and they fulfilled the role of being beautiful Jewelry/Adornments but also bodyguards/Assassins. They got around the loot issue because they were the treasure, so they kind of don\u2019t last when killed.<br /> <br /> Anyone remember the name of that Fanmade demon?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-23T02:30:44-08:00","id":1270059,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/223770-homebrews-of-the-first-circle?p=1269993#post1269993\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1ec21_DUlm1NO6sWzwOn0M9tGXfohlqmYJmqw1WpJhiM/edit\" target=\"_blank\">https://docs.google.com/document/d/1...qw1WpJhiM/edit</a><br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Qrsa9T2XMzWY_laBnu9ReLNPqUi6dVvCaJ8ScTKKXjM/edit\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Qrsa9T2X