t-circle?p=1424291#post1424291\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You try first. I'm tired for now.</div> </div> </div> </div>ok then. will do so later.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26173-evtrax","name":"evtrax","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"228"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-16T12:52:19-08:00","id":1424334,"title":"","content":"When Jaemi exist Why bother taking mortal serfs when I can just bind a few Jaemi?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-16T15:05:57-08:00","id":1424364,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/223770-homebrews-of-the-first-circle?p=1424334#post1424334\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">When Jaemi exist Why bother taking mortal serfs when I can just bind a few Jaemi?</div> </div> </div> </div>Jamei, i have no clue what those are.<br /> <br /> ok, heres my take on the god eating dragon. will do the false exaltation overview later.<br /> <br /> i hope <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12952\" data-vbnamecard=\"12952\">Accelerator</a> can make one to.<br /> <br /> gardra and shang yang comes from this website, <a href=\"http://compendiumofthings.wikidot.com/souls-and-creations-of-cecelyne\" target=\"_blank\">http://compendiumofthings.wikidot.co...ns-of-cecelyne</a><br /> <br /> <b>Aydahar, the heretical dragons</b><br /> <br /> the usurpation was watched by all of malfeas with pleasure as the solars were cast down and defeated. Of the dragonblooded there was little care amongst the yozi and the unqestionables, and even the citizens didnt care much now that only the dragonblooded were left to reliably summon them. But there were those who still kept an eye on creation, amongst those who did was Gardra, He Who Lights the Fires. despite his status as a soul of Cecelyne he was one of the most outspoken agaisnt her laws. This was his nature, for he was a soul of Shang Yang, who represents the infinite deserts self loathing and irony. Much of the usurpation resonated with him and his themes, and when he heard of the immaculate faith/order he was even more delighted. seeing the dragonblooded beat down disobediant gods and forced them to extol virtues that were lies. So he created the Aydahar,<br /> <br /> Resembling lesser elemental dragons, these creatures can isntantly be told apart from there elemental counterparts by the silver of there scales, identical to the sands of Cecelyne, for they are the sands of Cecelyne given form by either Gardra's whims or omen weather lashing upon the dunes of the endless desert. An Aydahar can escape when a dragon blooded uses the Immaculate faith to justify there horrors (sadly becoming all to common in the age of sorrows) or when any being uses religeon to justify an action that is in reality the most fundimental of the laws of Cecelyne, that might makes right.<br /> <br /> When in creation, an Aydahar immediatly rushes to find a cult of suffiecent power to cause enough trouble for its purposes, yet whose patron can not give a true fight to the Aydahar. At this point it ambushes the being, be it god, elemental, ghost, fair folk or something else (not even demons or physical beings are safe from the Aydahar). It devours the unlucky spirit and uses the power of the desert to create a magical mirage, effortlessly replacing the cults object of worship. At this point it not only grows the cult but also are introduced to new rituals and gain demands for more sacrifices. <br /> <br /> An Aydahar is in no way subitle. most gods take a light hand for fear of attracting something strong enough to stop them (usually an exalted of some kind). Even the most tyranical of deitys, those who have completely abandoned there duties make sure to keep there depravities small, lest they be beaten into submission. But Aydahar's are not bureaucrats like gods, and in fact enjoy attracting attention. In its disguise it gives bigger blessings, granting things like health and minor miracles, all of which are demon-tainted. Eventually the essence of the consumed being runs out, revealing the true demon. But by that point it does not matter, for the cult is so maddened that all pretences are abandoned, and more first circles are summoned through thaumaturgy as they spread the will of the yozis. <br /> <br /> At this point, with demons openly stomping there boots on human faces, the immaculates get involved. A hit squad is sent to banish the demons and break the cult. It always ends the same, with the demon being banished back to hell but always at least one dragon blooded dies, either by the might of the demons or by the rage of the cultists, seeking to either defend there god or punish those who took the god from them. and in hell the Aydahar score another victory. <br /> <br /> in hell the Aydahar's usually stay within the endless dunes of Cecelyne, for they have angered many citizens and unqeustanables with there cult snatching, and many 3rd and 2nd circles have bountys for proof of a heretical dragons death. Like there progenitor they have a long standing rivalry with the Priests of Cecelyne. As such no Aydahar has ever been granted citizenship, leaving them vulnerable to retribution by those demons that were summoned by the cults taken over by the Aydahar's. <br /> <br /> Sourcerers rarely summon Aydahar's, and when they do it is to use there spirit eating skills and the perfect mirages resulting from that. However, more often it is to manipulate communities so that they can be invaded. While she would never admit it, the scarlet empress summoned more than a few of these demons to conquer certain realm satrapys. This has precedent in the shogunate, and is even used by Lookshy. It must be noted that this tactic does not work on immaculate worshiping cultures, as the immaculate caladar means no single Ayadhar (or even many Heretical Dragons) can manage to replace the beings worshiped, and even if they do the tenets of the immaculate order means they cannot manipulate the cult to there will. In addition, any being of sufficent power cannot be consumed by the Aydahar. These are any being stronger than the average Aydahar, which without a cult to parasite is that of an average first circle demon. as such, greater dead or 2nd/3rd circle demons are immune, as are a raksha of particular strength. of special note is the reaction that ensues when an Aydahar tries to consume an exalted. The charm does work, but while the exalted is killed its essence flares one last time, utterly destroying the heretical dragon. While only dragonbloods are recorded to have this reaction (there element anhiliating the Aydahar utterly) it is only because the Aydahars arent stupid, and wont try it on a celestial exalt. This makes them unusable as hosts for infernal exaltations.<br /> <br /> they gain a point of limit for every day they are not allowed to manipulate a pre-existing cult. in game terms there devouring charm only works on beings with the cult merit, and even then it has to be around the power level of a first circle demon or lesser. they have a charm that allows them to tell if a prospective target is applicable.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26173,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26173-evtrax","user":"evtrax","date":".  making the demon better 11-17-2020, 10:42 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26173-evtrax","name":"evtrax","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"228"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-16T15:09:49-08:00","id":1424367,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/223770-homebrews-of-the-first-circle?p=1424334#post1424334\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">When Jaemi exist Why bother taking mortal serfs when I can just bind a few Jaemi?</div> </div> </div> </div> Well besides the fact they are demons and the world isn\u2019t made of Countless sorcerers they have a tendency of impregnating fauna with demon blooded offspring. And the general issues of having demon staff.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-16T15:20:44-08:00","id":1424370,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/223770-homebrews-of-the-first-circle?p=1424367#post1424367\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well besides the fact they are demons and the world isn\u2019t made of Countless sorcerers they have a tendency of impregnating fauna with demon blooded offspring. And the general issues of having demon staff.</div> </div> </div> </div>again, what are jaemi?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26173-evtrax","name":"evtrax","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"228"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-16T15:43:48-08:00","id":1424372,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>evtrax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/223770-homebrews-of-the-first-circle?p=1424370#post1424370\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">again, what are jaemi?</div> </div> </div> </div>2nd page here they are demon farmers I made in 2nd ed days. <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <a href=\"https://web.archive.org/web/20160315091428/http://rathess.xi.co.nz:80/exalted/index.php/Characters:Jaemi_the_Harvesters_Under_The_Moon\" target=\"_blank\">https://web.archive.org/web/20160315...Under_The_Moon</a> <br /> <b>Jaemi the Harvesters Under the Moon.</b><br /><br /> <span style=\"color:#252525\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Jaemi, the Harvesters Under the Moon.</span></span></span><br /> <b>Demons of the First Circle, Progeny of the Ivory Idol of Salt and Flame</b> The Frowning Idol of Salt and Flames created the first Harvester Under the Moon by incubating the blood of a sacrifice in a beast of Burden for a month. The method is now used by the Jaemi themselves who may produce new Harvesters by creating a pill of their own blood and using it to inseminate a beast of burden which will swell with a new Jaemi for one month and then burst open spawning a full grown Harvester.<br /> <br /> The Jaemi are often three or more yards tall with the head of an oxen and the snout of a boar complete with a brass ring etched with characters for Labor in Rocktongue. Their bodies are hunched lean and powerful with calluses and scars from a lifetime of labor and beige fur mixed with jet black thick hairs. Their arms are like a mix between badgers and an ape\u2019s. with three brass clawed fingers and a thumb. They often garb themselves in overalls and they wear a wide brimmed hat made of silver or brass straw to keep the harsh shining of Liger from their eyes. Their horns are brass and thickly grooved.<br /> <br /> The Jaemi were made to farm the brass and stone rubble of the Demon City. They have taken to both keeping a farm by themselves, or taking a mate and farming together, or even living in a demonic commune with each demon taking their role. The Jaemi have varied labors that they expect of themselves, and a single Harvester may farm Brass bread, heard Hell Cattle, collect silver and brass timber, and mine the jeweled bowels of the bones of Malfeas all in the same season. Though they find certain labors take priority in certain seasons, all for the sake of diversity, and they an irrepressible urge to only harvest each crop for one season a year. So in the Season of Fire they may harvest Brassbread for the Pastry Smiths at market, and then in the Season of Wood they may plant Bonecorn for the great milltowers to grind for use in tortillas.<br /> <br /> The Jaemi are masters at husbanding animals in hell. They often take to breeding with their cattle to create bloodlines of Hellbeast for superior meat, labor, and milk. They see it as their duty to do this ever few generations, and even when summoned into Creation a Sorcerer must take great pains to not have their Harvester breed with local livestock. This is particularly difficult during full moons, when the Jaemi are filled with the urge to \u201clabor\u201d and tend their animals till the sun rises. Much crops may be harvested, and bastards sown during these events.<br /> <br /> The Jaemi are rough backbones of Demon culture, they reap the fields to bring food to the markets of the Demon City, and cut lumber and quarry stone for the Hopping Puppeteers to rearrange into tenements, and they provide mined jewels for the Heranhals to make into brooches and rings. They collect Hellcattle milk to made into cheese and wine, and they fish for Kimbery spawn to feed the slaves of their betters. They provide shelter for Neomah to work their craft, and housing for Anuhles so they may harvest their silk, and food for Firmin so they may collect fashion tools for them. The Jaemi support the Demons of Hell so that they may continue their lives of toil and torture, for that is their nature. Most sacred to them is the Blood Red Moon of the Demon City which they worship as a Goddess of the Harvest. Sometimes their Patron even rewards the greatest of them with sacred tools of Orichalcum, Moonsilver, and even Starmetal tainted with Vitriol.<br /> Summoners are drawn to summoning the Jaemi to act as a diverse labor force for a multitude of projects whether it is a Lumber worker, harsh mining, or simple field work, animal sheparding, and even cooking; the Harvesters are familiar with them all and they are excellent brutes and thugs. They make excellent support for any number of other demon slaves.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Summoning</b>: (Obscurity 1/2)<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Sometimes during the Harvest Moon an empty farmstead with unharvested crops, and cattle in need of milking and shearing may find a Harvester Under the Moon crawling out of the lands well to tend the land.<br /> <br /> <b>Motivation</b>: To provide essential support for a community through diligent backbreaking labor.<br /> <b>Virtues</b>:<br /> <br /> Compassion 3 , Conviction 5 , Temperance 1 , Valor 3 Willpower 8<br /> <b>Attributes</b>:<br /> <br /> Strength 4 , Dexterity 3 , Stamina 6; Charisma 1 , Manipulation 1 , Appearance 2; Perception 2, Intelligence 1, Wits 2<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Abilities</b>: Martial Arts 3 (Grappling 3) Melee 4 (Farm Tools 3) Archery 1 (At Night 3) Thrown 1 (Rocks 3) War 1 (Herding 3) Integrity 2 (To Labor 3) Presence 2 (Intimidation 3) Performance 1 (Under the Moon 3) Resistance 5 (Under the Moon 3) Survival 4 (Farming 2, Animal Raising 1) Medicine Investigation Craft Water 1 (Following a Recipe 3), Earth 1(Mining 3) , Wood 2 (Farming 3) , Air 1 (Painting 1) , Magitech , Fire Occult 1 (Moons 3) Lore 1 Athletics 3 (Lifting 3) Awareness 2 (Intruders 3) Stealth 1 (Under the Moon 3) Dodge 1 (Under the Moon 3) Larceny 1(Black Market 3) Socialize 2 (Neighbors 3) Ride 3 (Cattle 3) Sail 1 (Rivers 1) Bureaucracy 1 (Economics 3) Linguistics (Native Old Realm)<br /> <b>Backgrounds</b>: Backing 1, Resources 2<br /> <br /> <b>Charms</b>:<br /> <br /> <br /> 1st Excellency Martial Arts, Melee, Ride<br /> 2nd Excellency Resistance, Survival, Craft, Athletics OxBody x2<br /> Landscape Travel (Doubles any travel on a Farm)<br /> Hurry Home (Back to their Farmhouse)<br /> Affinity (Water) Control (The Jaemi have learned the secrets of irrigation and with a watering can may channel water and Kimbery to feed crops)<br /> Meat of the Broken Flesh<br /> Spice of Custodial Delectation (Hard Labor gives them a mote every scene)<br /> TMA: The Jaemi have taken to spreading the Golden Harvest Style Martial Arts among their kind.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Essence</b>: 3<br /> <br /> Soak: L4/7B Thick Fur/Hair L1/B1<br /> NOTES: The Jaemi are often Armed with Exceptional Axes, Scythes, Sledges, Hoes, and Shovels. They also have a desire to start a family and will choose a neighbor to be their mate who they will constantly court for their hand in wedlock. They have an urge to keep at least two pets and will try to adopt from wild pigs, dogs, and cats. They must roll temperance to resist the urge to copulate with their cattle each month. Refraining from Labor for 25 hours results in one limit. Roll Conviction during a full moon and gain the successes in limit and willpower. They possess the Claws Horn and Hoof Mutations at varying levels spending 6 points of mutations on them. They will not eat dog, cat, or pig meat because they believe them to be pet animals rather than cattle. This does not extend to wolves, jackals, and large Predatory Cats, but it does extend to boars. Forcing them to eat or slaughter these beings for meat results in one limit added per day of slaughter.<br /> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-16T16:08:00-08:00","id":1424374,"title":"","content":"thank you <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar754_2.gif');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"754\" data-vbnamecard=\"754\">Eldagusto</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26173-evtrax","name":"evtrax","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"228"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-16T17:41:24-08:00","id":1424394,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>evtrax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/223770-homebrews-of-the-first-circle?p=1424364#post1424364\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Jamei, i have no clue what those are.<br /> <br /> ok, heres my take on the god eating dragon. will do the false exaltation overview later.<br /> <br /> i hope <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12952\" data-vbnamecard=\"12952\">Accelerator</a> can make one to.<br /> <br /> gardra and shang yang comes from this website, <a href=\"http://compendiumofthings.wikidot.com/souls-and-creations-of-cecelyne\" target=\"_blank\">http://compendiumofthings.wikidot.co...ns-of-cecelyne</a><br /> <br /> Aydahar, the heretical dragons</div> </div> </div> </div>Excellent. Put the title in bold. <br /> <br /> Also, I think you can also talk about how it introduces new forms of worship and obesiance to the Yozis, disguised as 'new rituals' and 'more sacrifices'. It is also much more active than any god, because it's a demon-tool based on cults, not a mere bureaucrat. That means much more faith and prayer, because its much more active and more unsubtle than most gods tend to be. It also tends to give bigger blessings. Things like health, glowing eyes, minor miracles, that's it. Most mortal onlookers don't actually know the miracles and blessings are demon-tainted, ala locust mana plague. Eventually, the cultists are so maddened and so misled by their influence that eventually they abandon all pretense and openly summon demons through thaumaturgy. <br /> <br /> Also, you should add in that the Realm sometimes summons these through sorcerers, implanting them within certain communities, and when they finally 'go loud', use it as a pretext to invasion.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-16T19:46:11-08:00","id":1424421,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/223770-homebrews-of-the-first-circle?p=1424394#post1424394\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Excellent. Put the title in bold.<br /> <br /> Also, I think you can also talk about how it introduces new forms of worship and obesiance to the Yozis, disguised as 'new rituals' and 'more sacrifices'. It is also much more active than any god, because it's a demon-tool based on cults, not a mere bureaucrat. That means much more faith and prayer, because its much more active and more unsubtle than most gods tend to be. It also tends to give bigger blessings. Things like health, glowing eyes, minor miracles, that's it. Most mortal onlookers don't actually know the miracles and blessings are demon-tainted, ala locust mana plague. Eventually, the cultists are so maddened and so misled by their influence that eventually they abandon all pretense and openly summon demons through thaumaturgy.<br /> <br /> Also, you should add in that the Realm sometimes summons these through sorcerers, implanting them within certain communities, and when they finally 'go loud', use it as a pretext to invasion.</div> </div> </div> </div>yeah, will revise them later. those are great ideas.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26173-evtrax","name":"evtrax","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"228"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-16T20:04:39-08:00","id":1424431,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>evtrax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/223770-homebrews-of-the-first-circle?p=1424421#post1424421\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">yeah, will revise them later. those are great ideas.</div> </div> </div> </div>And oh yeah. If it was me, I'll throw in a line about 'boots stomping on human faces'.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-16T20:54:16-08:00","id":1424447,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/223770-homebrews-of-the-first-circle?p=1424431#post1424431\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And oh yeah. If it was me, I'll throw in a line about 'boots stomping on human faces'.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think i can work that in.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26173-evtrax","name":"evtrax","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"228"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-23T01:28:35-08:00","id":1425677,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar754_2.gif');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"754\" data-vbnamecard=\"754\">Eldagusto</a> I've got some thoughts on the Gildempru. <br /> <br /> I know that you stated that they've got the stats of a First Age laboratory. That's unprecedented in the age of sorrows where you might be hard-pressed to find proper glassware for your alchemy lab. And also the sorry state of education and spread of technical knowledge of Creation (no internet, and most definitely very few great libraries) means that they don't know basic safety standards and simple alchemical solutions. You state that they're almost like Star Trek replicators, breaking down and recreating things from their base components, and capable of working just as well as any alchemy lab. <br /> <br /> One thing. Can they make alchemy products? Or more accurately, can their innards carry out the equivalent of alchemy? Can they make soups which replace bloodloss, and pastes that stop bleeding? Can they make a hearty pastry that can give the eaters the equivalent of Wind-Fire and Valiant Warrior's Courage? Can they create maiden tea and anagathics, using their essence to substitute raw materials? <br /> <br /> Can they serve as raw chemical industry, making paints, cleaning agents, catalysts, and everything else under the sun that requires complex chemical industries that Creation does not have? Can they make modern quality steel from raw ore? Are there Gildempru with recipes and alchemical agents from the first age, when they were used as research labs?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-23T01:47:53-08:00","id":1425679,"title":"","content":"I need to probably rework the Gildempru for 3rd ed. But I imagine they would work best with serving an ambitious Alchemist while they themselves don't understand the concept of the scope of what happens when you can separate the components of wreckage you feed them and the like. But the exceptional ones that somehow survived service with Savants and the like could have such secrets.<br /> <br /> Without 2nd Circles specifically cultivating them for labwork or industry they will probably wander into any work that allows them to taste interesting things.<br /> <br /> Depending on how people handle having specific Unique Demons of the 1st Circle, I can see ones that develop charms and advance learning to do things as you say, but I would probably not have them create without any raw materials I would probably have the wiser ones learning more and more how to synthesize recipes by processing a wider arrange of items like maybe eating industrial runoff and tin grass and wine and distilling and recombining it into an already heated glass of maiden tea. Or a really seasoned one eating a rare poisonous shadow gecko and glass blown from time and cinnabar to create Anagathic pills.<br /> <br /> With the wonders of Hellish Flora I would imagine making Modern Quality Steel something some Gildempru would learn to due based off the sheer metallurgical experience they would have processing various metal plants for Octavians Armory or the like.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-23T11:05:57-08:00","id":1425763,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/223770-homebrews-of-the-first-circle?p=1423984#post1423984\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><i><b>ARANY, THE FALSE HEROES</b><br /> Progeny of the Ebon Dragon<br /> Demons of the First Circle</i><br /> <br /> ...<br /> <br /> This works, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8877-mrfamiliar\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"8877\" data-vbnamecard=\"8877\">MrFamiliar</a> ?</div> </div> </div> </div>This is fantastic. Thanks for taking the time.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8877-mrfamiliar","name":"MrFamiliar","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"76"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-23T11:54:58-08:00","id":1425770,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MrFamiliar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/223770-homebrews-of-the-first-circle?p=1425763#post1425763\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is fantastic. Thanks for taking the time.</div> </div> </div> </div>If you have any more 1st circle demons, please tell me.<br /> <br /> I love making 1st circles, but I'm all out of ideas for homebrewing :-(","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-27T03:18:51-08:00","id":1433591,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://forums.sufficientvelocity.com/threads/general-exalted-thread.44/page-2211#post-13625015\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forums.sufficientvelocity.com/data/svg/20/1/1794123741/logo_icon.png\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://forums.sufficientvelocity.com/threads/general-exalted-thread.44/page-2211#post-13625015\" target=\"_blank\"> General Exalted Thread </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://forums.sufficientvelocity.com/threads/general-exalted-thread.44/page-2211#post-13625015\" target=\"_blank\"> https://forums.sufficientvelocity.com/threads/general-exalted-thread.44/page-2211#post-13625015 </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> I could see Elloge having a species of first circle demons who are all convinced that they are isekai protagonists. One of them could be chosen to bear an Unwoven Coajutor and be the voice in an Infernal Exalt's head. You could have your isekai protagonist be woven out of wyld stuff when a... </div> </div> </div><br /> KAPLAN, THE TIGER GENERALS<br /> DEMON OF THE 1ST CIRCLE<br /> PROGENY OF THE TWILIGHT OF THE GODS<br /> <br /> It is claimed, that one day the walls of hell shall be breached and its armies shall burst forth into Creation. That day shall herald a sword age that stains the seas with blood, and covers the land with the bodies of the faithful. The gates of heaven shall be broken open and all the stars pulled from the starry vault. So it is claimed by the lords and ladies of hell, and so it shall be. <br /> <br /> The Kaplan were created for this war. <br /> <br /> <br /> Eahc Kaplan looks like a tall human, strong of limb and bronzed skinned, with the wings of an eagle, the head of a lion, and the lower body of a tiger. Their body is like a trumpet, and strikes terror in those who hear it. In their backwards hands they hold a blade of frozen flame, and those struck by it are marked forever after as enemies of the Yozi. Such creatures are dealt aggravated damage by attacks from creatures of darkness and all with Essence sight know of their crime.<br /> <br /> Sorcerers summon the Tiger Generals to lead their armies or personal guards. They also serve in a lesser capacity as investigators and judges. Their keen senses excel make them excellent at interrogations, allowing them to ferret out evidence and deceit, while the terror of their voices discourages deception.<br /> <br /> Stats: Think slightly modified blood apes<br /> <br /> Charms: <br /> Excellent-Senses: (Permanent)<br /> The Tiger-generals have sharp-eyes and keen minds, capable of cutting through the haze of deception and seeing the micro-tremors of a foe's fear. Roll double-9s for all rolls involving perception or noticing details and secrets. <br /> <br /> Trumpet of Hell (10m, 1wp; simple, instant)<br /> The clarion-call of battle for the creators of the universe. Up to long-range, and includes in any forces obeying the demon in question. The clarion-call grants focus and strength to those following the demon, granting the friendly forces +2 in attack and defense rolls (this does not stack). And enemies who hear it gain a +1 difficulty to all rout checks for the rest of the scene. In social combat, roll... Frack it. Roll charisma + appearance vs target's Willpower. Success means that target not only now has a tie of fear towards you, but also has a -3 to penalty to all attempts to defy, hide, or out-talk you. <br /> <br /> Marking blade (5m, 1wip)<br /> <br /> Roll the Kaplan's essence (3) against the target's upon causing lethal damage. Success means that for 1 season all attacks from Creatures of darkness (demons, ghosts, dark gods) are aggravated. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-04T03:32:05-08:00","id":1434466,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forums.sufficientvelocity.com/threads/general-exalted-thread.44/page-290#post-2852788\" target=\"_blank\">https://forums.sufficientvelocity.co...0#post-2852788</a><br /> <br /> <b><i>Sanansaattaja, the Ladies of Obsidian Wings<br /> Demons of the First Circle<br /> Progeny of Viettelij\u00e4, Indulgent Soul of the 10th Soul of Adorjan</i> (CLAMP Joke incoming)</b><br /> <br /> Sanansaattaja are androgynous inhuman beauties of long limbs, impossible large eyes in all shades of crystal, radiant cascades of hair and fine angular features who are in fact perfectly capable of switching gender at will. What remains distinctive however is the Sanansaattaja's digit-grade legs ending in a five talon-ed feet of living obsidian, and the large powerful wings which give them their name. While not exceptional strong, Sanansaattaja are astonishingly agile and flexible, a feat matched only by the incredibly calculating and ruthless cunning the Ladies of Obsidian Wings.<br /> <br /> Created to ensnare and entrap mortals in cascade of pleasant delights before showing them the mercy of Adorjan, the Ladies of Obsidian are ruthless falcons in constant search of prey. Prey they peruse with delightful dances, smouldering glances and whispered words of pleasures to come. Pleasure that can last for years as the Sanansaattaja hide their sadism, milking victims of resources, knowledge, favors and preferably worship before unleashing a sudden torrent of anguish and sadistic sexual torture on the flesh of their victims before hiding all evidence. Or revealing in it as an initiation activity within the inevitable cults they seek to establish in Creation.<br /> <br /> <br /> Martial skill is often a secondary concern but a natural affinity for Archery leads to common assumption that those without a bow are relatively new. More importantly however is the Ladies is the realm of society as they move among the bureaucracies and societies of hell, putting their clever, twisted minds to good use promoting the cause of the Yozi's. Many a Sanansaattaja has clawed her way to understanding the basics of sorcery, the most obscure tea ceremony, or the most moving of poetry.<br /> <br /> For Sanansaattaja naturally form together in Murders, claiming high towers flocking together in highly polite, elegant courts where one ill considered choice can send a Lady tumbling down the pecking order, or vaulted to leadership on the basis of a single dance. Woe onto those who attempt to interject themselves into the politics of a Murder without being a natural Citizen for the whole group will turn on outsiders with utter ruthlessness.<br /> <br /> Obscurity 2/6 Apart from competing with the Neomah, the Ladies of Obsidan Wings are often called upon to be messengers as they can travel great distances each day. Additionally they can be called upon for training in a wide variety of skills, most often relying upon brokering deals with Murders to summon the individual with the required skill","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12952,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","user":"Accelerator","date":". 02-04-2021, 07:21 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-25T23:01:24-07:00","id":1441465,"title":"","content":"Out of curiosity, has anyone compiled all the homebrew demons in this thread into one document?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2783-tytalus","name":"Tytalus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2783_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"491"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-27T06:13:55-07:00","id":1441633,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tytalus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/223770-homebrews-of-the-first-circle?p=1441465#post1441465\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Out of curiosity, has anyone compiled all the homebrew demons in this thread into one document?</div> </div> </div> </div>No. It's pretty hard. And I'm too tired to do so.<br /> <br /> I'm hoping this doesn't fail like the previous forums.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-28T18:56:25-07:00","id":1441841,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/223770-homebrews-of-the-first-circle?p=1441633#post1441633\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> No. It's pretty hard. And I'm too tired to do so.<br /> <br /> I'm hoping this doesn't fail like the previous forums.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Fair enough. IT's the kind of thing I used to do when I had more time. I might still try to sit down and do it, but wanted to make sure I wasn't going to be replicating someone else's work first.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2783-tytalus","name":"Tytalus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2783_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"491"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-28T09:56:08-07:00","id":1457912,"title":"","content":"I will add this thread to my list of ones to save in the Wayback Machine. Seriously, Lioness is suggesting the forum could die soon. I <b>strongly encourage</b> everyone to save any and all threads you find useful at <a href=\"https://archive.org/web/\" target=\"_blank\">https://archive.org/web/</a>. Check if the thread has already been saved, but each page of a multi-page thread has to be saved separately (right-click the next page <b>number</b> on the bottom and open in a new tab. If you can't, reload the page you're on but replace .../web/2021######/... with .../web/2/[url] first. If your first (or first 10) attempts to save a page don't work, please don't give up. If it keeps failing you can check <a href=\"https://archive.org/web/*/\" target=\"_blank\">https://archive.org/web/*/</a>[url] to see if it was saved and the Wayback Machine was only kidding about the errors (it throws up fake errors a lot). Sometimes it takes 24 hours for the saved page to be indexed (making it available on the web). It's wonky right now but I've been steadily archiving whatever Exalted and oWoD urls I could salvage. I'm asking for any help I can get in this massive undertaking. We can do it! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> *insert Alchemical pep-talk*<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Argatoi, the Brass Turtles<br /> Progeny of ?, ? soul of Ligier the Green Sun</b><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Exalt in the Machine</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/533482-argatoi-the-brass-turtles-demons-of-the-first-circle#post533482\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Came up with these while getting anxious for 3e to drop. Thought I would share and seek any advice people are willing to give. In particular some different ideas for the unbound slip into creation portion would be nice. Not certain that the current condition is even feasible in the wild except under extremely unlikely events.<br /> <br /> <b>Argatoi, the brass turtles, demons of the first circle</b><br /> These large six-legged, red leather and brass plated turtles are known for their appetite for coal as well as assistance in the forging of metal. Though they resemble turtles that are about the size of a wagon, they are generally faster than creations turtles, though they have difficulty running. They are strong and resilient and can be used as beasts of burden, though that is not their specialty in the demon realm.<br /> <br /> They consider coal to be a rare delicacy, and like most things they eat they heat it up in their mouth before consuming it. They can emit a strange green light from their tongues and throats which allow them to heat meals or breath a line of green light and fire in self defense.<br /> <br /> They are very skilled at maintaining an exact temperature when heating a meal, so they can be instructed to heat a mouthful of coal to very specific temperatures. Metal smiths learned long ago that they could bargain with an Argatoi to help them forge a piece of equipment in exchange for the coal used in the forging process. The brass plates that make up part of their shells can also function as anvils within easy reach. The various ridges, spikes, rounded, and flat surfaces offer just about any kind of shape required. A smith simply needs to be familiar with a particular Argatoi's shell and move to an appropriate part.<br /> <br /> At this point most Argatoi have witnessed and been a part of the forging of a great many metalworks, and smart summoners will prize them as much for their advice on craft projects as they do during the forging. Flattery and stoking their ego seem to work best when convincing them to impart advice, though the asker should be prepared to listen to a long-winded tale about a previous work. A summoner must remember to ask before starting a work as it can be rather difficult to understand a demon turtle who is speaking with a mouthful of coal and metal.<br /> <br /> Those who wish to make use of them should be careful. The heat and green light they emit increases the usual fatigue experienced when working the forge, so a smith should set aside ample time for rest. In addition prolonged exposure can cause strange blistering and an effect not unlike sunburn, and long-term exposure may cause temporary or permanent blindness. Many smiths cover themselves from head to toe, and wear darkened goggles when using the assistance of an Argatoi. These precautions will of course heightened the effects of fatigue experienced by the crafter.<br /> <br /> A pristine deposit of coal that is set on fire by natural occurrences may draw an Argatoi from the demon realm, mouth watering for a tasty meal.</div> </div> </div> </div>Exalt in the Machine invented these, and there was a general criticism that they didn't have enough weirdness or drawbacks to fit in with other First Circles. Here's my attempt to add some of that:<br /> <br /> Argatoi are progeny of the Doomed Champion: <a href=\"https://web.archive.org/web/20160209151737/http://rathess.xi.co.nz/exalted/index.php/Characters:Drihtan\" target=\"_blank\">https://web.archive.org/web/20160209...acters<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />rihtan</a><br /> <br /> Sometimes Drihtan removes a piece of his armor, either because it\u2019s broken or for some other reason, and animates it as a Brass Turtle.<br /> <br /> Argatoi are enthusiastic for whatever forging project they\u2019re engaged in, but they cannot avoid incorporating some flaw into every work forged with their aid. Sometimes the flaw is noticeable, but most often it is a failure condition that can cause the item to break, unknown to anyone until it happens. For mundane equipment, the failure condition is as rare as a first circle demon\u2019s escape condition. For a 1-3 dot artifact, the failure condition should be as unlikely as a Second Circle Demon\u2019s escape condition. 4-5 dot artifacts should only break as easily as a Third Circle Demon escapes unbound into Creation. Mentioning this problem to a Brass Turtle, or ordering it to remove or not add such a flaw, will cause it to gain 1 Limit, and is futile in any case since they can\u2019t help themselves<br /> <br /> In addition, Argatoi must be specifically ordered by their summoner not to consume all the coal stores they can smell, and can cause havoc (and out of control fires) if they get into a coal mine. Feeding them charcoal instead of earth-coal gives them diarrhea and uncontrollable green-flame belching for a day, and makes their products more seriously flawed. If fed coal, they increase the crafter\u2019s Means by X. (I don\u2019t know 3E mechanics)<br /> <br /> Whenever a new deposit of coal or jet is opened for the first time on an overcast and rainy day, an Argato may appear under cover of the clouds, eager to burn the wet coal.<br /> <br /> <br /> I still have no idea what they eat in the Demon City in place of coal. Suggestions?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">She/Her. I am literal-minded and write literally. If I don't say something explicitly, please never assume I implied it. The only exception is if I try to make a joke.</span></span></span></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">My point of view may be different from yours but is equally valid.</span></span></span><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1x1ycoxJF0G9niMt5D3Pp7owZ7tw8AJvL?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted-cWoD-ArM url mega-library</a>. Exalted <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/663334-random-name-generator\" target=\"_blank\">name-generators</a>.","edited":{"userid":896,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","user":"Erinys","date":". 08-28-2021, 01:03 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","name":"Erinys","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar896_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4235"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-28T10:26:47-07:00","id":1457914,"title":"","content":"Here are a couple I used in a game <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> I used both of these home brew demon types for a game set in the North, which were continuously replaced by a Sorcery Shaping done by an exiled Dynastic sorcerer, as he wanted to have absolute control over the areas people. Basically it was my attempt to set up a horrific xcom 2 like game for my players, where the Solars could try to overthrow the local tyrant. <br /> <br /> <b>Demon Squads:</b><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman, serif\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Jabberer AKA Jabs</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman, serif\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Description: A black armored figure occasionally seen without their helmets, they are largely bald with grey irises, small, almost snake-like noses, and heavily pushed-back ears. The armor isn't actually part of them but the exoskeleton of another of Cecelyne's children. </span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman, serif\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Origin: Cecelyne, the Endless Desert is their progenitor and they spontaneously are birthed from her silver sands there are some rumors that they are actually born from when the winds of Adjoran touch an Anuhle egg that was laid in the Silver Sands of Cecelyne.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman, serif\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-size:10px\"><b>Essence: </b></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-size:10px\">2 </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-size:10px\"><b>Willpower: </b></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-size:10px\">5</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-size:10px\"><b>Personal Motes: </b></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-size:10px\">70</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-size:10px\"><b>Health Levels: </b></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-size:10px\">-0/-1x3/-2x3/-4/Incap.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-size:10px\"><b>Actions: </b></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-size:10px\">Climbing with Tentacle: 8 dice; Feats of Strength: 10 dice (may attempt Strength 5 feats)<br /> Resist Poison/Illness: 8 dice<br /> Senses: 7 dice<br /> Threaten: 5 dice<br /> Appearance: 3 (Hideous)<br /> Resolve: 3<br /> Guile: 1</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-size:10px\"><b>Combat:</b></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-size:10px\">Join Battle: </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-size:10px\">6 dice<br /> Black Baton Withering Attack: </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-size:10px\">11 dice (Damage 15)<br /> Black Baton Decisive Attack: 8 dice<br /> Tentacle: 10 dice (Damage 15, &amp; can drag the target to him or pull the attacker to him)</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-size:10px\">Attack (Grapple): 9 dice (10 dice to control)<br /> Combat Movement: 8 dice<br /> Evasion: 2<br /> Parry: 4<br /> Soak/Hardness: 7/0</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Charms:</b></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\">Shattering Voice:<br /> Description: Once per scene, a Jabberer can shriek with the silent wind destroying most things in a column of absolute silence.<br /> 15 motes, 1 wp, Simple<br /> 13 dice attack (Damage 20)<br /> <br /> Tentacle Pouch: 5 motes to have the whip leave its pouch of flesh.<br /> Description: As the being learns this charm a pouch of flesh grows under an arm of their choice, within this pouch lies a scorpion tailed tentacle that is only mildly controlled by the person it lives within. </span><span style=\"color:#000000\">This gives the host a powerful movement, and ranged weapon that is extremely multi-purpose but quite gross </span><span style=\"color:#000000\">and occasionally wants to feed.<br /> <br /> Tentacle Host: 10 motes, 1 wp<br /> Description: </span><span style=\"color:#000000\">This allows its wielder to make 2 attacks or any 2 actions involving its tentacle whips works as Principle of Motion. You may also take any evocations for this weapon as your own essence sustains it.</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\">Tentacle: Thrown, Short Range, Lethal, Disarming, Grappling, Flexible</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\">Accuracy: +5 at close range, +4 at short range<br /> Damage: Strength + 10L<br /> Note: You can buy additional evocations for this revolting thing. </span></span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman, serif\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">The Skinless Horrors AKA Skins</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman, serif\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Description: Unlike the Jabberers, these things can never be confused for men as they are four armed skinless masses of fleshy muscle that seep blood continuously. The grotesque things are only sent out on certain objectives usually to pound a victim into literal chunks of flesh. Basically a shock trooper used to intimidate the masses, although these are occasionally directed by Jabberers to move debris or a fully laden cart usually filled with bodies. </span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman, serif\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Origin: The progenitor of these revolting masses of skinless muscle is thought to be Malfeas but as they have never spoken it is unknown. </span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman, serif\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-size:10px\"><b>Essence: </b></span><span style=\"font-size:10px\">2 </span><span style=\"font-size:10px\"><b>Willpower: </b></span><span style=\"font-size:10px\">5</span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:10px\"><b>Personal Motes: </b></span><span style=\"font-size:10px\">70</span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:10px\"><b>Health Levels: </b></span><span style=\"font-size:10px\">-0x5/-1x2/-2x2/-4/Incap.</span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:10px\"><b>Actions: </b></span><span style=\"font-size:10px\">Feats of Strength: 15 dice (may attempt Strength 8 feats)<br /> Resist Poison/Illness: 10 dice<br /> Senses: 5 dice<br /> Threaten: 10 dice<br /> Appearance: 5 (Hideous)<br /> Resolve: 4<br /> Guile: 3</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:10px\"><b>Combat:</b></span><span style=\"font-size:10px\">Join Battle: 8</span><span style=\"font-size:10px\"> dice<br /> Charging Body Block: 13 dice (Damage 18B) (Smashing)<br /> Rend: 17 dice (Damage 15L) (Reaching)<br /> Grapple: 12 dice (Initiates a grapple on a decisive attack.)<br /> Combat Movement: 12 dice<br /> Evasion: 3<br /> Parry: 3<br /> Soak/Hardness: 10/5</span></span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman, serif\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-size:10px\">Shattering Touch:<br /> Description: These things are known for being able to simply charge through buildings leaving nothing but debris in their way. Anything between their target and them is likely shattered into debris covered with red pasty blood.<br /> 5 motes, Simple<br /> 13 dice attack (Damage 18 + 5 auto successes of Bashing damage)<br /> This destroys any cover except for full cover between this monster and the target. </span></span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman, serif\"><span style=\"font-size:10px\">Rending:<br /> Description: If this beast gets is hands on you, your likely to be literally torn limb from limb.<br /> 5 motes, Supplemental<br /> This adds 7 to any withering or decisive damage roll when performing a Savaging action. </span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman, serif\"><span style=\"font-size:10px\">Brutal Pounding:<br /> Description: If this monster hits a target for 5 or more initiative in a single withering attack it can immediately make a grapple action against that target unless it is already grappling them.<br /> 4 motes, Reflexive</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman, serif\"><span style=\"font-size:10px\">Four Arms of Wrath:<br /> Description: This charm allows the Skins to ignore any defense penalty while grappling, and to engage multiple foes with grapple attacks.</span></span></span><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1635-citadel97501","name":"Citadel97501","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"544"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-28T18:17:53-07:00","id":1457933,"title":"","content":"Turns out the Brass Turtles had already been posted on this thread. Hopefully my addition was worth it.<br /> <br /> I have Web Archived this thread now, except page 17, and a lot of the various threads and homebrew linked from it.<br /> <br /> Why do the Skinless Horrors look like yet another mockery of the UCS in Hell? There's that behemoth, too.<br /> I wouldn't be surprised if there is a First Circle demon made in mockery of each Incarna, of Gaia and Autochthon, of the Dragon Kings and Jadeborn, and all of them exist either to be disgusting or to be tortured.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Edit: By the way, please <b>don't</b> use Google Docs for saving these things. Google Docs cannot be Archived in the Wayback Machine <i>at all</i> and on September 13 Google is going to change many or most of the urls. I am racing to download <i>all the homebrew</i> before the urls all become invalid.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">She/Her. I am literal-minded and write literally. If I don't say something explicitly, please never assume I implied it. The only exception is if I try to make a joke.</span></span></span></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">My point of view may be different from yours but is equally valid.</span></span></span><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1x1ycoxJF0G9niMt5D3Pp7owZ7tw8AJvL?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted-cWoD-ArM url mega-library</a>. Exalted <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/663334-random-name-generator\" target=\"_blank\">name-generators</a>.","edited":{"userid":896,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","user":"Erinys","date":". 08-28-2021, 10:22 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","name":"Erinys","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar896_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4235"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-28T19:38:22-07:00","id":1457942,"title":"","content":"Ok guys, since this forum might die soon, what should be done? Sword of creation.net?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-29T09:58:09-07:00","id":1457985,"title":"","content"