nkedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-30T00:40:33-07:00","id":1491876,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Erinys</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/223770-homebrews-of-the-first-circle?p=1457985#post1457985\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Like I said, I recommend saving everything you care about in the Wayback Machine. Unless you can find something that could save an <b>online</b> copy of a whole website of this size.<br /> <br /> I have already saved this thread, and the threads linked from it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hey. You saved this stuff? Thanks.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-22T12:12:40-07:00","id":1518554,"title":"","content":"<b>Varos, the city-crawlers</b><br /> <br /> Living things adapt to their environment. They move faster through it. They resist its poisons and hazards. They blend in. They, in a sense, thrive in it. Fish thrive in the sea. Jungle lizards thrive in the forest, ignoring all the poisons that surround them. Desert snakes live in the South, gaining speed and strength through heat. And of course, the boulder-dogs of the Imperial Mountain do just fine blending in with the rocky soil. <br /> <br /> And in Malfeas, it is no exception.<br /> <br /> Varos are spider-like creatures, though with a few extra limbs, joints, and other miscellaneous bits. They're respectable fighters, with above average senses. Thick carapace protects them from most weapons. Claws and pincers and deadly fangs make for useful killers. A set of eye-stalks, letting them peak out from the solid-fortress that is their shell, scanning for targets. Antennae tasting the air for prey. Then they hunt. <br /> <br /> The Varos have adapted well to their environment, and their environment is the Demon City of Malfeas, and so the Varos with their basalt-crag shells have taken a little bit of their essence with them. Not for them sandy beaches or deadly caves. Instead, Varos are adapted, both in spirit and body to the very concept of an urban dwelling. They can move through structures as if it was air, scuttling through walls, verandas, balconies, as if it was no more substantial than air. Their eyes and antennae can sense you as if the intervening brickwork or wooden alcoves were not in the way. And when you walk through the streets of Malfeas, the Varos are there, having merged with the stonework or hiding in that pillar. Their favourite methodology is to hunt people through the walls, launching deadly ambushes from seemingly-harmless walls or from rooms that should have been secure, temporarily granting their victims their immaterial abilities, dragging them halfway into the floor before releasing them, leaving them helplessly wriggling in the solid stone as the Varos leaves to hunt other victims. They'll be back. <br /> <br /> The Varos are dangerous hunters, but in knock-down drag out fights they lose to blood apes, which is why they attack in multiple swarms and favor ambush tactics. Their ability to rapidly engage and disengage means they can easily outmaneuver nearly anything in their favored environment. If Varos are known to be hunting you, seven different herbs mixed together with blood (your own, if desperate) and dust from a brick can create a sweet-smelling paste that drives them away, its smell permeating through the walls and floors of a building. Wiping this paste onto a particular wall or floor or ceiling, and its touch will burn any Varos that attempts to move through it. Enough to make the creatures pop back into the air, screaming piteously as pits are scored into their armour plates.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-23T03:29:44-07:00","id":1518625,"title":"","content":"I am quite unhappy with the Varos. If anyone has any improvements, I'm read to hear it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-24T13:17:35-07:00","id":1518718,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/223770-homebrews-of-the-first-circle?p=1518625#post1518625\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am quite unhappy with the Varos. If anyone has any improvements, I'm read to hear it.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm tinkering with some stuff. Do you want suggestions or a retooled write-up?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/561-mockery","name":"Mockery","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar561_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"876"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-26T10:41:22-07:00","id":1518831,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mockery</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/223770-homebrews-of-the-first-circle?p=1518718#post1518718\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm tinkering with some stuff. Do you want suggestions or a retooled write-up?</div> </div> </div> </div>Retooled writeup","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-26T21:24:35-07:00","id":1518869,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/223770-homebrews-of-the-first-circle?p=1518831#post1518831\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Retooled writeup</div> </div> </div> </div>All right then, here we go. I feel like this is first draft material, but it's a start:<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Varos, the City-Crawlers</b><br /> <i>Progeny of the Keeper of the Forge of Night</i><br /> <br /> A Varos resembles something between a crustacean and an arachnid the size of a dog, with a chitinous body, a dozen long limbs, legs and claws and pedipalps alike bristling with setae, with long whiplike antennae and eyestalks that give it an uncanny awareness of its surroundings, able to sense through walls and structures as though they were clearest air. Only when curled up within their basalt shells for protection or slumber can other demons hope to catch them by surprise.<br /> <br /> While other demons may inhabit the infinite brass city of Malfeas as their prison, the Varos find it a nearly perfect home. Shaped as ideal urban hunters, they may slip and swim and scuttle through the structures made by men and by demons for their business and for their dwelling, treating the sturdiest walls like smoke and silk curtains. With a small effort they may extend this blessing to those objects and beings they have taken in their claws; for most, the only time they will know the same oneness of being with the city is when they are the Varos\u2019 prey.<br /> <br /> And make no mistake, the Varos are predators to the core. Hunting in packs, a dozen or more may rise from the streets of the demon city with all the warning of a descending owl, tackling other demons much larger than themselves into the ground and burying them without a trace in seconds. Surrounding demons who can do so often take to the brass-bound skies rather than see if the Varos are sated with their current prey. Those who cannot fly will usually find out shortly one way or the other. Regardless, to be swarmed, dragged underground, and eaten alive is often a kinder fate than to be stalked by one alone: such prey are added to the larder of the Varos who took them, left half-fused within the walls and ceiling. This serves to sate the demon's hunger when necessary, of course, but Varos often consider their victims as living trophies. The city-crawlers may even treat these souls with something like care and unwanted affection, sharing lesser meals to prolong their life, lest they expire, spoil, and be no good for display anymore. After all, if one has a Citizen bound in their keeping, surviving only at their mercy, how impressive must they be?<br /> <br /> The Varos detest the world in its natural state, unshaped by its inhabitants. Left to their own devices, a Varos constructs a hollow senseless simulacrum of a city out of whatever bric-a-brac they can bind together, resulting in something structurally stable, but functionally questionable: streets dead-end unexpectedly, while great towers made of wood, stone, soil and bone cut off or angle unexpectedly in random, sometimes nonsensical directions. Chambers and floors within may be shut off without windows or doors, and rooms too-large abut to others too-small.<br /> <br /> Sorcerers may summon the Varos as abductors or assassins\u2014or protection against the same\u2014or may enlist their aid to construct buildings or battle fortifications.<br /> \u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/561-mockery","name":"Mockery","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar561_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"876"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-28T14:41:31-07:00","id":1519049,"title":"","content":"Well that'd was pretty great you cleaned up the prose and even made them more interesting. Mind if I repost it somewhere?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-29T14:10:54-07:00","id":1519126,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/223770-homebrews-of-the-first-circle?p=1519049#post1519049\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well that'd was pretty great you cleaned up the prose and even made them more interesting. Mind if I repost it somewhere?</div> </div> </div> </div>Go ahead, glad to help!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/561-mockery","name":"Mockery","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar561_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"876"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-26T12:25:49-07:00","id":1524540,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://forums.sufficientvelocity.com/threads/general-exalted-thread.44/page-2265?post=17081687#post-17081687\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forums.sufficientvelocity.com/data/svg/20/1/1794123741/logo_icon.png\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://forums.sufficientvelocity.com/threads/general-exalted-thread.44/page-2265?post=17081687#post-17081687\" target=\"_blank\"> General Exalted Thread </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://forums.sufficientvelocity.com/threads/general-exalted-thread.44/page-2265?post=17081687#post-17081687\" target=\"_blank\"> https://forums.sufficientvelocity.com/threads/general-exalted-thread.44/page-2265?post=17081687#post-17081687 </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> Kodenever, the Basalt-Winged Bats Demon of the First Circle Progeny of the Gargoyle Duchess When Zabah wishes to make a new kodonever, she decapitates one of the grotesque stone statues which grow off the walls of her greater self. From the head grows a body and stone wings and vicious claws... </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://forums.sufficientvelocity.com/threads/general-exalted-thread.44/page-2367?post=23412691#post-23412691\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forums.sufficientvelocity.com/data/svg/20/1/1794123741/logo_icon.png\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://forums.sufficientvelocity.com/threads/general-exalted-thread.44/page-2367?post=23412691#post-23412691\" target=\"_blank\"> General Exalted Thread </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://forums.sufficientvelocity.com/threads/general-exalted-thread.44/page-2367?post=23412691#post-23412691\" target=\"_blank\"> https://forums.sufficientvelocity.com/threads/general-exalted-thread.44/page-2367?post=23412691#post-23412691 </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> Got a new First-Circle Demon for anyone interested: Odaana, the Craneskin Knights Demons of the First Circle, Progeny of the First Companion The First Companion created the Odaana in her own image, to be dutiful, fervent knights to fill her armies and man her honour guards. In this, she... </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://forums.sufficientvelocity.com/threads/general-exalted-thread.44/page-2280?post=19048819#post-19048819\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forums.sufficientvelocity.com/data/svg/20/1/1794123741/logo_icon.png\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://forums.sufficientvelocity.com/threads/general-exalted-thread.44/page-2280?post=19048819#post-19048819\" target=\"_blank\"> General Exalted Thread </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://forums.sufficientvelocity.com/threads/general-exalted-thread.44/page-2280?post=19048819#post-19048819\" target=\"_blank\"> https://forums.sufficientvelocity.com/threads/general-exalted-thread.44/page-2280?post=19048819#post-19048819 </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> i think this is my first post here. heres a first circle demon i created. gardra and shang yang comes from this website, http://compendiumofthings.wikidot.co...ns-of-cecelyne Aydahar, the heretical dragons the usurpation was watched by all of malfeas with pleasure as the solars were cast... </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://forums.sufficientvelocity.com/threads/general-exalted-thread.44/page-2265?post=17074998#post-17074998\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forums.sufficientvelocity.com/data/svg/20/1/1794123741/logo_icon.png\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://forums.sufficientvelocity.com/threads/general-exalted-thread.44/page-2265?post=17074998#post-17074998\" target=\"_blank\"> General Exalted Thread </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://forums.sufficientvelocity.com/threads/general-exalted-thread.44/page-2265?post=17074998#post-17074998\" target=\"_blank\"> https://forums.sufficientvelocity.com/threads/general-exalted-thread.44/page-2265?post=17074998#post-17074998 </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> Dzokerka, the Mirthful Reivers Demon of the First Circle Progeny of the Gargoyle Duchess Across Hidrae's roofs scramble a hunting pack of dzokerkae, laughing manically as they hunt their prey. These wild man-beasts wrought by Zabah have china faces, eternally locked in a smile, and they dress... </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://forums.sufficientvelocity.com/threads/general-exalted-thread.44/page-2229?post=14529048#post-14529048\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forums.sufficientvelocity.com/data/svg/20/1/1794123741/logo_icon.png\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://forums.sufficientvelocity.com/threads/general-exalted-thread.44/page-2229?post=14529048#post-14529048\" target=\"_blank\"> General Exalted Thread </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://forums.sufficientvelocity.com/threads/general-exalted-thread.44/page-2229?post=14529048#post-14529048\" target=\"_blank\"> https://forums.sufficientvelocity.com/threads/general-exalted-thread.44/page-2229?post=14529048#post-14529048 </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> Demons! Tahat - That Which Guards the Gates Demon of the First Circle Progeny of The Sword of the Yozi Like the Primordials he worships, the Sword of the Yozi has formed a city from his very soul. To police that city and protect he has created the Tahat, demons of great vision and greater... </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://forums.sufficientvelocity.com/threads/general-exalted-thread.44/page-2370?post=23775783#post-23775783\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forums.sufficientvelocity.com/data/svg/20/1/1794123741/logo_icon.png\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://forums.sufficientvelocity.com/threads/general-exalted-thread.44/page-2370?post=23775783#post-23775783\" target=\"_blank\"> General Exalted Thread </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://forums.sufficientvelocity.com/threads/general-exalted-thread.44/page-2370?post=23775783#post-23775783\" target=\"_blank\"> https://forums.sufficientvelocity.com/threads/general-exalted-thread.44/page-2370?post=23775783#post-23775783 </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> ...I've got something for y'all into devil-type demons. This basically came out of thinking about how a 'classic'-looking demon might come about in Exalted, but I'm pretty happy with the result: Irnoki, the Brazen Scribes Demons of the First Circle Progeny of the Living Tower As the empire of... </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forums.sufficientvelocity.com/threads/general-exalted-thread.44/page-2464?post=26826314#post-26826314\" target=\"_blank\">https://forums.sufficientvelocity.co...#post-26826314</a><br /> <br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forums.sufficientvelocity.com/threads/general-exalted-thread.44/page-2525?post=29063879#post-29063879\" target=\"_blank\">https://forums.sufficientvelocity.co...#post-29063879</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forums.sufficientvelocity.com/threads/general-exalted-thread.44/page-2501?post=28143242#post-28143242\" target=\"_blank\">https://forums.sufficientvelocity.co...#post-28143242</a><br /> <br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forums.sufficientvelocity.com/threads/general-exalted-thread.44/page-2464?post=26826314#post-26826314\" target=\"_blank\">https://forums.sufficientvelocity.co...#post-26826314</a><br /> <br /> <br /> Here's a bunch of stuff I found. And that's... it. <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-26T12:28:40-07:00","id":1524541,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forums.sufficientvelocity.com/threads/general-exalted-thread.44/page-2460?post=26785634#post-26785634\" target=\"_blank\">https://forums.sufficientvelocity.co...#post-26785634</a><br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-03T20:03:02-07:00","id":1525008,"title":"","content":"Oh an idea???<br /> <br /> <br /> A Nanny demon<br /> <br /> would be really useful when using a neomahs flesh weaaving for just about anything other then allowing a same sex couple or one where one or both are sterile to have a child","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-08T06:35:56-08:00","id":1525206,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/223770-homebrews-of-the-first-circle?p=1525008#post1525008\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh an idea???<br /> <br /> <br /> A Nanny demon<br /> <br /> would be really useful when using a neomahs flesh weaaving for just about anything other then allowing a same sex couple or one where one or both are sterile to have a child</div> </div> </div> </div>I swear I've once read about a demon like that once before. Bespectacled and robed servants with skin made of mother of pearl, trained in all arts ranging from tea ceremonies to calligraphy. Can't remember where, though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-08T06:36:52-08:00","id":1525207,"title":"","content":"If it's not too much trouble to everyone here, I might port things from here: <br /> <a href=\"http://exalted.xi.co.nz/wiki/ATaxonomyOfMadness/CollectedFirstCircle\" target=\"_blank\">http://exalted.xi.co.nz/wiki/ATaxono...tedFirstCircle</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-17T00:15:20-08:00","id":1525559,"title":"","content":"HALASZ, THE FISHERS OF MEN<br /> Demons of the 1st Circle<br /> <br /> &quot;... And thus, I shall make you fishers of men...&quot;<br /> <br /> ~Unknown<br /> <br /> What's that, up in the air? It's a bird! It's a plane! Ohgodhelpmehelpmehelpme~!<br /> <br /> The Fishers of Men are a strange breed, their limbs ending in specialised spinnerets. The silks are secreted from the ends of their arms, which are covered in fur, a cross between a man's hairy arms and the bristles on a spider. The web has a variety of properties; sticky, light, strong, sharp, etc, which are all useful, desired greatly by sorcerers, and are used by the Fishers of Men for their traps and strategems. For the Fishers of Men consume the flesh of other beings, both sentient and non-sentient. Deep within the City of Brass, they are always looked at with a wary eye. Some use their silks to cover up holes and pits, letting unfortunates fall through and impale themselves on great solid spears of silk. Others span silken threads across slopes, and those unlucky enough to move through find themselves cut in half. But it is their final usage which is the most infamous and gives them their names.<br /> <br /> The sticky threads of the Halasz can be used to attach to any object with a strength bordering on the supernatural. And using their native magic, the Fishers can yank on this thread, moving their target in seeming violation of the laws of mass and movement. Younger Halasz simply let their threads dangle from high up arches or balconies, grabbing those passing below and reeling them up. More intelligent ones set up entire networks of webs up in the sky, attaching between building tops or even clouds, whilst using individual silk strands to hang bait in front of more impulsive or unintelligent demons. And the oldest of them all, ride on clouds of silk that catch the wind, and reverses the pull of gravity to hold up loads. Such errant clouds can be steered against the wind, giving observers warning that something is deeply wrong before they get hoisted up, never to be seen again.<br /> <br /> Halasz are used for various purposes. Their silk can be used in construction, either hauling massive weight loads, scaffolding, or integrated directly into the masonry itself. The silk can be rendered down into alchemical mixtures or used as body armour, and last of all, the incredibly powerful silk can be used to tear down boulders, walls, entire fortresses, if enough Halasz are thrown at the problem (but then again, that counts for almost all demons). More discreet sorcerers use them for kidnappings; one moment the target is there, and the next moment he's a hundred meters up in the sky, and swiftly moving out of screaming range.<br /> <br /> (insert demon weakness so that people might hesitate summoning this)<br /> <br /> If you wanna have an idea of how they might look like, look at super Mario.\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-26T16:35:46-08:00","id":1525984,"title":"","content":"Originally posted by <b>Prince of the Night</b> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/223770-homebrews-of-the-first-circle?p=1525008#post1525008\">View Post</a><br /> Oh an idea???<br /> <br /> <br /> A Nanny demon<br /> <br /> would be really useful when using a neomahs flesh weaaving for just about anything other then allowing a same sex couple or one where one or both are sterile to have a child<br /> I swear I've once read about a demon like that once before. Bespectacled and robed servants with skin made of mother of pearl, trained in all arts ranging from tea ceremonies to calligraphy. Can't remember where, though.\u200b<br /> <br /> oh one more thing on this idea ? the nanny demon could secrete breast milk or some close approximation therof","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-04T13:01:13-08:00","id":1527944,"title":"","content":"<b>Lyuk, the Hunting Burrowers</b><br /> <br /> Demons of the 1st circle<br /> <br /> &quot;Ok, everything looks safe here.&quot;<br /> <br /> *fives minutes later*<br /> <br /> &quot;Oh god!&quot;<br /> <br /> Some demons are long runners, predators who hunt via wearing their prey to exhaustion. Others are front facing fighters, those who wander onto the battlefield and devour whomever they defeat. And others simply lie in wait, and have prey walk right past them.<br /> <br /> The Lyuk are a strange breed, with a specialized ability for warping space. Not dissimilar to the sanctum creating powers of gods, they finds a surface, and 'burrow' down. Not into the surface's solid material, but into the space between spaces. There, they hide iin their pocket dimensions, lying in wait and sensing the world outside through their charms, casting out lures and tirelessly observing the world through their 5 segmented eyes, jaws waiting.<br /> <br /> In the pocket dimensions of the Lyuk, time moves like molasses. Food does not spoil, and flesh does not rot, and people do not starve. Some enterprising sorcerers have used the Lyuk as storage areas or guardians for this purpose, for as ambush predators they only need to eat once in a great while, and they can be trusted with inanimate objects or unstable alchemical reagants. Others use them as hiding places that cannot be detected by mortal means. Other join them in their ambush, adding their own soldiers in a deadly first strike on an enemy.<br /> <br /> Charms:<br /> Casting call - The Lyuk creates illusions to have people get within range. The older they are, the better. Younger ones create illusions of gold, screams for help, or the appearance of a pretty young maiden in need of rescuing. Older ones can recreate the voice of your father, or the screams of your mother<br /> <br /> Strike from the shadows - Anyone striking from the Lyuk's pocket dimension gains a bonus when they strike from surprise. This bonus is increased if they either match, or outnumber the target.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-12T06:24:51-08:00","id":1528412,"title":"","content":"<b>Cercopis, the Six-Fingered Monkey Thieves</b><br /> <br /> Among the Second Circle, there is no certainty who was responsible for creating these demonic larcenists and letting them loose throughout Malfeas' infernal sprawl. While there is speculation that their creator has since disappeared or been forgotten, it is more likely that admitting responsibility for the Cercopis' genesis would invite a great and terrible ire from their peers, none of whom are spared from the chaos wrought by these First Circle demons' simple instinct to cheat, lie, and steal. While demons of the Second Circle cannot deny the Cercopis' usefulness and make extensive use of them in their schemes, feral colonies of these six-fingered monkeys plague Hell's shifting streets and alleyways, serving as nuisances to their contemporaries of the First Circle in their kleptomaniac games between individuals and rival families. Many only hear their cacophonous whoops and cheering in celebration of a successful score when it is far too late.<br /> <br /> Cercopis bear a great resemblance to Creation's macaques, although some key differences betray their hellish origins. They cannot hide their green fur, thus they hide in the shadows, nooks, and crannies of urban landscapes and demonic estates, and their eyes glisten with a subtle light of burning jade and emerald. The most distinctive feature of their silhouette are their six-fingered hands, each with a symmetrical pair of thumbs, index, and middle fingers. They are the rogues of the First Circle demons, operating in packs to distract, trick, and beguile their marks before making a grand and frenzied getaway with all manner of personal possessions - a common sentiment among Hell's denizens is that any Cercopis you can see are not the ones you should look for. Cercopis are deceptively cunning and cruel, valuing their prizes on how much their loss would inconvenience and distress their owners rather than adhering to ideas of inherent material value.<br /> <br /> While the instinct to steal material goods beats strong in their demonic hearts, their size and natural talents makes Cercopis into decent spies and scouts for Second Circle demons and sorcerers who dare to handle them. Their knack for occasionally replacing goods on a mark's person with items of similar mass, weight, and shape allows them to be used for nefarious means, with more than one sorcerer using these six-fingered pickpockets to plant damning evidence on their rivals, smuggle goods across borders via unsuspecting travellers, and slip combustive materials or deathly toxins into the vicinity of their enemies. If caught, Cercopis will fight vicious and dirty to outnumber on their assailants and furiously scratch and maul at soft flesh, eyes, and hair.<br /> <br /> Cercopi colonies amass exquisite hoards of trinkets and valuables, a communal collection of wealthy prizes from their schemes and competitions to outdo each other. Occasionally, these colonies are willing to exchange their prizes with outsiders and rival Cercopi families, although never giving anything away for free: currency and material value alone does not sway the Cercopis, instead looking for opportunities to deprive the other party of things they deeply care about, such as family heirlooms, memoirs of deceased friends and family, or Artifacts uncovered by Exalted adventurers. To successfully swindle and steal from a colony's hoard begrudgingly impresses the Cercopis while woe befalls any thief who is caught in the attempt or warrior who tries to take their prize by force alone as they suffer a brutal death at countless six-fingered hands, accompanied by a choir of hellish screams and wicked howls.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":23800,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23800-the-firebrand","user":"The Firebrand","date":". 01-12-2024, 09:30 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23800-the-firebrand","name":"The Firebrand","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23800_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"46"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-24T21:41:30-07:00","id":1536232,"title":"","content":"Concept: A riff on certain varieties of ants<br /> <br /> In front: The demon's head and face is near invincible. Its skin and carapace is harder than castle walls. Its eyes are xeno-crystal, and fire and acid spits from pores on its skin. No-one can hit it without getting struck by a counter-attack, and it can survive nearly any hit (relatively), and it can deal almost as much damage in return. Near impregnable. Swords shatter upon it. Sorcery merely scars the surface. Arrows veer away, as if sensing its impregnability. And it can 'spread' its invincibility to nearby objects, surfaces, and beings. <br /> <br /> At the back: Soft flesh, weak armour, capable of being struck down by nearly anything. Fast-moving legs that can be crippled. A soft, fleshy belly. <br /> <br /> Tool-concept: This demon was created to be the equivalent of doors. All demons have a limited amount of power, and this one was created to have all of its power focused on the front. Its gigantic head serves as battering ram, gate, movable wall, and barricade all at once, shielding an infantry battalion behind it or blocking an entrance to a castle. A powerful but limited tool that does well in well-planned, static battles or situations but can be easily side-stepped by a more agile enemy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-07T00:19:40-07:00","id":1539978,"title":"","content":"<b>Uveg, the air-spinners</b><br /> <br /> There, a shimmer in the air. There, a whisper in the wind. Look again. That's the nest of the Uveg, the airspinners. Strange men who look like ordinary mortals, except for the utricating, glassy hairs upon their backs, their 6 limbs, and their gaunt faces. The Uveg look upon the world in terms of shapes and essence, not in colours. In fact, they consider colours and light to be similar to fire and electricity in consideration to mortals: dangerous tools that can be reshaped into deadly weaponry. <br /> <br /> They build vast cities amongst the demon city, often using their 6 limbs to transform the nearby essence into the famous glassy silk they are so famous for. Their cities are vast, with an incredible amount of detail and amenities, from walkways to bridges, to fountains to gardens, to boulveyards to vast halls. All of them completely invisible. Visitors have been driven mad, dying of hunger and thirst or by their own hand while trying to transverse these cities while the entrance lies less than a hundred meters from them. These foolish explorers attempt to explore these cities in search of things like gold or artifacts of jade, not knowing that the Uveg despise these things for their propensity for bright colours. <br /> <br /> Brighter men instead, bring specialised sweetmeats that the Uveg are partial to, and gain in response excellent and deadly artifacts of all kinds. Gauzes which hide anything from sight. Near-invisible tools for secrecy and wetwork. Glass windows that show daylight even in the darkest of nights. Glass brushes that could absorb the hues from objects and transfer them to another, creating hues which were impossibly bright, or even indescribable. Dresses which glowed in the dark and lit up in choreography to dance moves. And most prized of all were the the Coloured Bolt Throwers, weapons which fire prismatic hues of deadly energy, at the cost of the surrounding colours when the weapon is fired (this causes disfigurements in the skin, but the Uveg do not seem to mind).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-07T00:30:56-07:00","id":1539979,"title":"","content":"New concept: Cities floating using a multittude of gasbags. Symbiotic connection between 2 demon breeds? One being capable of floating like a hot air balloon, another capable of doing the other fiddly tasks?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-10T05:53:30-07:00","id":1543524,"title":"","content":"Not mine, but interesting thought on 'hyperspecialisation'. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://exalted.xi.co.nz/wiki/TheHoverpope/Achristos\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://exalted.xi.co.nz/wiki/TheHoverpope/Achristos\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://exalted.xi.co.nz/wiki/TheHoverpope/Achristos\" target=\"_blank\"> http://exalted.xi.co.nz/wiki/TheHoverpope/Achristos </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <b>Achristos, That Which Remains</b><br /> <br /> <br /> Many people have submitted to Shoggeleth's knife, and many have lost themselves to it utterly. There are many who have had so much cut away from them that there is little left beyond one fragmented aspect of their being. These are those shattered husks, the things which were cut down to their last, and yet lived. Many were once demons, and this made them into new breeds. Many are men, and they will surely perish soon.<br /> <br /> No Achristos may use an ability in a way that does use its specialty. <b>Achristos, The Warrior Aspect</b><br /> <br /> <br /> The Warrior Aspect of the Achristos resembles nothing more than a thin, wiry man or woman made of steel without facial features, holding a weapon if that is its type. It does not speak or reason, but only fights. All but the simplest instructions are beyond its capacity to understand.<br /> Nature: Paragon<br /> Attributes: Strength 5, Dexterity 5, Stamina 5, Charisma 1, Manipulation 1, Appearance 1, Perception 1, Intelligence 1, Wits 1.<br /> Virtues: Compassion 0, Conviction 0, Temperance 0, Valor 5, Never fails valor rolls, never succeeds in other rolls.<br /> Abilities: Athletics 5, One of the following: Melee 8 (+3 in one weapon), Martial Arts 8(+3 in one style), Brawl 8 (attack or clinch +3).<br /> Charms: Uncanny Prowess, Principle of Motion<br /> Cost to Materialize: 26<br /> Base Initiative: 6<br /> Attack: varies.<br /> Dodge pool: 3 Soak: 9B/6L (Steel Skin, 4B/4L)<br /> Willpower: 7<br /> Health Levels: -0 x 7, I (Incapable of understanding pain.)<br /> Essence: 2 Essence pool: 51<br /> <br /> <br /> Other Notes: The Warrior Aspect can never dematerialize. Its essence to materialize is committed, and it cannot be forced immaterial.<br /> <b>Achristos, The Courtesan Aspect</b><br /> <br /> <br /> The Courtesan Aspect of the Achristos resembles nothing more than a well-built man or woman made of gleaming glass and gems, without facial features, seated. It does not move or reason, but only speaks. All but the simplest instructions are beyond its capacity to understand.<br /> Nature: Paragon<br /> Attributes: Strength 1, Dexterity 1, Stamina 1, Charisma 5, Manipulation 5, Appearance 5, Perception 1, Intelligence 1, Wits 1.<br /> Virtues: Compassion 5, Conviction 0, Temperance 0, Valor 0, Never fails compassion rolls, never succeeds in other rolls.<br /> Abilities: Athletics 5, One of the following: Socialize 8 (Seduction +3), Performance (one art form +3), Presence 8 (leadership or intimidation +3) .<br /> Charms: Stoke the Flames, Creation of Perfection<br /> Cost to Materialize: 26<br /> Base Initiative: 2<br /> Attack: NA<br /> Dodge pool: 0 Soak: 9B/6L (Glass Skin, 4B/4L)<br /> Willpower: 7<br /> Health Levels: -0 x 7, I (Incapable of understanding pain.)<br /> Essence: 2 Essence pool: 51<br /> <br /> <br /> Other Notes: The Courtesan Aspect cannot speak words or think in any real sense, but it is often speaking; its speech is musical, meaningless, and incredibly compelling, carrying whatever of its meanings it is trying for. Performing Achristos may indeed move, but only in the form of the one movement that is their specialty. <b>Achristos, The Scholar Aspect</b><br /> <br /> <br /> The Scholar Aspect of the Achristos resembles nothing more than a well-built man or woman made of paper with meaningless scratches of ink and without facial features, seated in a lotus position. It does not move or speak, but only thinks of what it knows. All but the simplest instructions are beyond its capacity to understand.<br /> Nature: Paragon<br /> Attributes: Strength 1, Dexterity 1, Stamina 1, Charisma 1, Manipulation 1, Appearance 1, Perception 5, Intelligence 5, Wits 5.<br /> Virtues: Compassion 0, Conviction 0, Temperance 5, Valor 0, Never fails temperence rolls, never succeeds in other rolls.<br /> Abilities: Athletics 5, One of the following: Lore 8 (One field of knowledge+3), Occult, (one field of knowledge +3), Craft 8 (One particular object +3) .<br /> Charms: Stillness, Creation of Perfection<br /> Cost to Materialize: 26<br /> Base Initiative: 6<br /> Attack: NA<br /> Dodge pool: 0 Soak: 9B/6L (Parchment Skin, 4B/4L)<br /> Willpower: 7<br /> Health Levels: -0 x 7, I (Incapable of understanding pain.)<br /> Essence: 2 Essence pool: 51<br /> <br /> <br /> Other Notes: The Scholar Aspect knows a great deal, but its speeches are the mutters of a scholar talking to himself at his desk - they focus as much as possible on the specific task that the Achristos has in mind. A Scholar Aspect who is an expert in biology may spend all of his time muttering about the larynx of a hybroc, only stopping when forced by a sorceror.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-19T20:35:22-07:00","id":1561954,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://forums.sufficientvelocity.com/threads/general-exalted-thread.44/page-2826#post-38192406\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forums.sufficientvelocity.com/data/svg/20/1/1794123741/logo_icon.png\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://forums.sufficientvelocity.com/threads/general-exalted-thread.44/page-2826#post-38192406\" target=\"_blank\"> General Exalted Thread </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://forums.sufficientvelocity.com/threads/general-exalted-thread.44/page-2826#post-38192406\" target=\"_blank\"> https://forums.sufficientvelocity.com/threads/general-exalted-thread.44/page-2826#post-38192406 </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> There's a lot Ex3 doesn't cover, though, or mentions only briefly. Paragon and Harborhead haven't ceased existing in the Ex3 version of the setting &mdash; the former even appears on the big world map in the core book &mdash; but haven't been revisited because they're considered to have problematic baggage... </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> One of my Infernal character's first experimental super-prototypes on his quest to create a wholly new and original race, akin to the Dragon Kings.<br /> <br /> <br /> Thanks to Earthscorpion and his ludicrous catalogue of exalted homebrew for both inspiring me to write this and providing the mechanics by which my character makes this.<br /> <br /> Grigori, The Men Reforged<br /> <br /> Demon of the First Circle<br /> <br /> Progeny of the King of Lions<br /> <br /> The beggars whisper and the asylum patients rave, the crippled moan and the slaves dream - and on their lips, they all share the same myth. They say that if you pray and you dream, and if you hold to passion and to love, no matter the ills of the world, then the King will come to you - he will take you in his arms and carry you away, to a better world. He will take you, and with his strange alchemies of heated blood, he will reshape you into something better, something bright and glorious and eternal, that you might join him in his work. You need only hold fast, and he will come. The myths say many things - and every last one of them is true.<br /> <br /> The Grigori resemble the people they were before their rebirth, but more, each of them rebuilt according to their subconscious vision of their ideal self. Features such as horns or fur or particularly fluffy animal ears are particularly common among those who were taken at young ages, while rippling muscle and certain engorged physical characteristics are just as common a sight among the elder. Each Grigori is unique in their own right, and each excels within their field of choice in their own ways - some can shape stone with their bare hands, and build from it wonderful spires and towers, while others are soldiers par excellence, masters of blade and fist who wrap their steel and flesh in great bands of fire. All Grigori, however, carry within them the fluxing essence of their new father, and may shift their forms in ways both subtle and oblique. When roused to great passion, many of the Grigori tend to shake and quiver, their bodies pulsing like the beat of a heart as they flicker through colors and shapes.<br /> <br /> Of the Grigori, few truly accurate general statements can be made - their very nature means they are far more individualistic and unique than most First Circle demons. However, due to usually being drawn from the ranks of the lowest of society and especially from those who are physically or mentally deformed, they often have a strong anti-authoritarian bent, as they revel in their new freedom, and resent all who would take it from them.<br /> <br /> Mechanics<br /> <br /> As a product of the Hellcat's use of Titanic Spawn Uncountable, Grigori may not usually be summoned by Sorcerers. That being said, he has granted his authority to some of his witch-lieutenants, that they might draw upon his forces when they have the need. Sorcerers summon the Grigori when they have need of a master of exceeding skill in a specific field - though the oddness with which the Grigori can manifest their mastery can surprise. More than one commander has been startled when their architect starts sweating liquid concrete. Grigori gain a point of Limit whenever they are forced to take an action against a belief they hold deeply.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-19T23:06:06-07:00","id":1561960,"title":"","content":"Idea I had a while a demon Nanny specially focused on bringing up babies creeated by neomah","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"than